//! A cut generated by a tool that turns about two axes at once ([`crate::Kernel::cut_swept`] by
//! two turns: a gear's tooth space cut by its mate, a wheel hobbed by its worm), exactly.
//!
//! Seen from the target, the tool at t is placed by M(t), and a point p of it moves at
//! ω(t) × p + u(t) in the tool's own frame. Where a face's outward normal n is square to that
//! (g = n · (ω × p + u) = 0) the face touches what it has swept: its *contact*, a curve on the
//! face at each instant, which sweeps the face's envelope. A sharp convex edge sweeps part of
//! the boundary too, wherever one of its faces leads and the other trails (g of opposite signs).
//! So at each instant the boundary's generators are the contacts and the stretches of such
//! edges. Faces that join smoothly are one face to this (a *group*: a thread's flank, made in
//! pieces along its helix), and edges that run on from one another one edge (a *run*).
//!
//! A tooth space is long one way, and the generators run along it. It is charted across: by
//! *slices* of the target's frame (planes square to the target's axis, cylinders about it, or
//! spheres about the point of it nearest the tool's axis: whichever the space runs through). In
//! one slice the space's outline is a chain of *links*, each a group's contact point or a run's
//! point in that slice followed through time, joined at *joints* of two kinds: a *node*, where
//! a contact comes to its run and the two are tangent (flank, corner, land, corner, flank: a
//! worm wheel's space); and a *crossing*, where one link's curve runs into what another has
//! swept and the outline turns a corner (a flank undercut by the tooth's own tip: the tip's
//! path is the space's side near the root, the flank's envelope farther out). A third kind is
//! followed and carried too, a *corner*: where a vertex of the tool passes through the slice,
//! the path of one edge that ends at it ends there and another's goes on (the end of a pinion's
//! tooth). The chain is
//! found in the target's middle slice: the nodes there by a search over each run and the time,
//! the links by following them from joint to joint while they are near the target, each
//! watched for the curves that cross it. It is carried to the other slices, each joint by
//! Newton's method from the slice before. Where a crossing closes to a touch as the slices go
//! (the joint a node from there on), the tooth space is made in *stretches*, each with its own
//! chain, handed over at that slice.
//!
//! A chain may have a link at an end in some slices only: a flank's envelope that comes out
//! from under the tip's path partway along the tooth (a spiroid's second flank, a sliver that
//! runs back along the path and crosses it at the least of angles, which is told by the two
//! curves' own directions there). In the slices before, the chain found ends with the link that
//! leaves the target, short of where that envelope crosses it outside. So where the middle
//! slice's chain makes no plug, the chains of the target's two end slices are looked at, and one
//! with more links is followed from its own slice: as far as its joints can be carried, outside
//! the target by then. The stretch beyond has the chain without those links, and is closed in
//! their place by *fillers*: each the missing link's outline in the slice where the two
//! stretches meet, carried along on the end of the stretch's own last link (cut clear of the
//! target, and where the two stretches meet at the other's joint).
//!
//! Each link then makes one four-sided sheet over (slice, share of the way between its
//! joints), fitted by a B-spline through its exact points. The sheets are closed into a solid,
//! the *plug*: a lid from the chain's one end to the other (straight in the slices' own
//! coordinates) and a cap in the first and the last slice, all checked to lie outside the
//! target, and the plug is subtracted. A motion that repeats (the tool turning whole turns
//! while the target turns a whole number of teeth) cuts the same space each time, turned about
//! the target's axis: one plug is made and its copies subtracted, as one tool of many solids
//! where they stand apart.
//!
//! The sheets are checked before they are used, by the tool's mesh and nothing they were made
//! from: at places within the target, a point just outside a sheet must be one the tool never
//! passes over, and a point just inside one it does.
//!
//! A chain's links may also change *within* the target along the tooth space: where the tool's
//! end faces and corners come into the cut (a hypoid pinion's tooth, a dozen changes between
//! the gear's toe and its heel). Where the way above makes no plug of a motion that doesn't
//! repeat, the space is made *under a roof* instead ([`Roof`]): a straight line across each
//! slice, in the slice's own coordinates, just outside the face of the target the space opens
//! through. Every slice's chain is trimmed where it comes out through the roof, so its ends
//! are the same points whatever links it has, and the roof is the plug's lid. The outline is
//! found afresh in each of some slices (each joint checked, by the tool's mesh, to be on the
//! boundary of what the tool sweeps: a chain through a node inside the sweep is none); the
//! slices of one outline are a stretch, carried each way to where it stops being what it is,
//! and handed over there to the next. A link the next stretch lacks comes to nothing where the
//! two meet (a contact's node passing a vertex of the tool, a crossing passing one, a joint
//! come up through the roof): its sheet's side there is a point, a three-sided face. Where
//! two links meet at a node in one stretch and cross in the next (the loop between a crossing
//! and its node being within the sweep, and often too short for the walk to find), the
//! crossing is carried into the first as far as it goes.
//!
//! Declined (None, so that the other ways are tried) where the chain can't be followed or
//! carried: a contact that splits or ends within a face, a chain whose end stays inside the
//! target, a filler, a lid or a cap that meets the target, sheets the check refuses; under a
//! roof, a target whose face is no straight line in the slices, an outline that comes out
//! through the roof between its ends, stretches that don't meet.

use super::kernel::NativeKernel;
use super::math::*;
use super::mesh_distance::MeshDistance;
use super::nurbs::NurbsCurve;
use super::surface::Surface;
use super::topo::Body;
use crate::*;
use nalgebra::Rotation3;
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};

/// How closely a sheet's B-spline follows its exact points, as a share of the tool's size.
const SHEET_FIT: f64 = 1e-8;

/// Faces whose normals differ by less than this (radians) all along an edge join smoothly
/// there: a contact passes over it (a sweep's faces, piece after piece along its path).
const SMOOTH: f64 = 1e-3;

/// The share of a sheet's point's slide along its fitted surface that counts against the fit.
const SLIDE: f64 = 0.02;

/// How far (a share of the tool's size) a contact's point is looked for from where it was
/// last, or from the place it is guessed at.
const HOP: f64 = 0.06;

/// A rigid motion's velocity in the moving body's own frame: (ω, u), a point p moving at
/// ω × p + u.
type Twist = (V3, V3);

/// The motion: steps applied in order, each running from its start to its end as t goes from 0
/// to 1 (and on, at the same rates, outside that).
struct Motion<'a> {
    steps: &'a [RigidStep],
}

impl Motion<'_> {
    fn place(&self, t: f64) -> (Rotation3<f64>, V3) {
        super::sweep_solid::rigid_at(self.steps, t)
    }

    /// The tool's velocity in its own frame at t.
    fn twist(&self, t: f64) -> Twist {
        let (mut r, mut d) = (Rotation3::identity(), V3::zeros());
        // The velocity field of the steps so far, where they have put the tool: ω × x + v.
        let (mut w, mut v) = (V3::zeros(), V3::zeros());
        for s in self.steps {
            match *s {
                RigidStep::Turn { axis, from, to } => {
                    let q = Rotation3::from_axis_angle(&axis.dir, from + (to - from) * t);
                    let c = axis.origin.coords;
                    // x ↦ q (x − c) + c carries the field with it, and adds its own.
                    let shift = c - q * c;
                    let (qw, qv) = (q * w, q * v);
                    let own = axis.dir.into_inner() * (to - from);
                    w = own + qw;
                    v = c.cross(&own) + qv + shift.cross(&qw);
                    r = q * r;
                    d = q * (d - c) + c;
                }
                RigidStep::Slide { from, to } => {
                    let a = from + (to - from) * t;
                    v += (to - from) + a.cross(&w);
                    d += a;
                }
            }
        }
        let rt = r.inverse();
        (rt * w, rt * (v + w.cross(&d)))
    }
}

/// The surfaces a tooth space is charted across, about the target's axis.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]
enum Slices {
    /// Planes square to the axis: by height along it.
    Height,
    /// Cylinders about the axis: by distance from it.
    Radius,
    /// Spheres about a point of the axis: by distance from it.
    Sphere,
}

/// Slices and the coordinates within one: a point is (c, a, b), c the slice.
#[derive(Clone, Copy)]
struct Chart {
    kind: Slices,
    o: P3,
    x: V3,
    y: V3,
    z: V3,
}

impl Chart {
    fn local(&self, p: &P3) -> (f64, f64, f64) {
        let w = p - self.o;
        (w.dot(&self.x), w.dot(&self.y), w.dot(&self.z))
    }

    /// The slice of a point.
    fn c(&self, p: &P3) -> f64 {
        let (x, y, z) = self.local(p);
        match self.kind {
            Slices::Height => z,
            Slices::Radius => x.hypot(y),
            Slices::Sphere => (x * x + y * y + z * z).sqrt(),
        }
    }

    /// The slice coordinate's gradient at a point.
    fn grad(&self, p: &P3) -> V3 {
        let (x, y, z) = self.local(p);
        match self.kind {
            Slices::Height => self.z,
            Slices::Radius => (self.x * x + self.y * y) / x.hypot(y).max(1e-300),
            Slices::Sphere => {
                (self.x * x + self.y * y + self.z * z) / (x * x + y * y + z * z).sqrt().max(1e-300)
            }
        }
    }

    /// A point's coordinates within its slice (an angle about the axis the turn nearest `near`).
    fn inner(&self, p: &P3, near: f64) -> (f64, f64) {
        let (x, y, z) = self.local(p);
        let turn = |a: f64| a + TAU * ((near - a) / TAU).round();
        match self.kind {
            Slices::Height => (x, y),
            Slices::Radius => (turn(y.atan2(x)), z),
            Slices::Sphere => (turn(y.atan2(x)), z.atan2(x.hypot(y))),
        }
    }

    fn point(&self, c: f64, (a, b): (f64, f64)) -> P3 {
        match self.kind {
            Slices::Height => self.o + self.x * a + self.y * b + self.z * c,
            Slices::Radius => self.o + (self.x * a.cos() + self.y * a.sin()) * c + self.z * b,
            Slices::Sphere => {
                self.o + ((self.x * a.cos() + self.y * a.sin()) * b.cos() + self.z * b.sin()) * c
            }
        }
    }
}

/// What an edge of the tool is to its sweep.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Debug)]
enum EdgeKind {
    /// Sharp, the material's corner under 180°: it sweeps boundary where one face leads and the
    /// other trails.
    Convex,
    /// Sharp, the corner over 180°: what it sweeps is inside.
    Concave,
    /// Its faces join smoothly: a contact passes over it from one to the other.
    Smooth,
    /// A seam, a pole, a free edge: none of these.
    Other,
}

/// Sharp edges that run on from one another without a corner, between the same two groups of
/// faces (a thread's crest, edge after edge along its helix): one edge to the sweep. A place on
/// it is σ, each part's own parameter range laid after the part before's.
struct Run {
    /// Its edges in order, each with whether σ runs along it.
    parts: Vec<(usize, bool)>,
    /// Where each part starts in σ, and the last one's end.
    start: Vec<f64>,
    /// Each part's two faces: the one of the run's first group, then of its second.
    faces: Vec<[usize; 2]>,
    /// The two groups of faces it lies between.
    groups: [usize; 2],
    kind: EdgeKind,
    /// A single edge that closes on itself (a rim): σ goes round without end.
    closed: bool,
}

impl Run {
    fn span(&self) -> f64 {
        self.start[self.start.len() - 1]
    }

    /// The part holding σ: (the part, its edge's parameter there, +1 or −1 as σ runs along the
    /// edge or against it). None past the run's ends.
    fn part(&self, b: &Body, sigma: f64) -> Option<(usize, f64, f64)> {
        if self.closed {
            let (e, _) = self.parts[0];
            return Some((0, b.edges[e].t[0] + sigma, 1.0));
        }
        let slack = 1e-9 * self.span();
        if sigma < -slack || sigma > self.span() + slack {
            return None;
        }
        let sigma = sigma.clamp(0.0, self.span());
        let k = self
            .start
            .partition_point(|&x| x <= sigma)
            .clamp(1, self.parts.len())
            - 1;
        let (e, fwd) = self.parts[k];
        let ed = &b.edges[e];
        let d = sigma - self.start[k];
        Some(if fwd {
            (k, ed.t[0] + d, 1.0)
        } else {
            (k, ed.t[1] - d, -1.0)
        })
    }

    /// σ of the point at `s` of the run's part `k`.
    fn sigma(&self, b: &Body, k: usize, s: f64) -> f64 {
        let (e, fwd) = self.parts[k];
        let ed = &b.edges[e];
        self.start[k] + if fwd { s - ed.t[0] } else { ed.t[1] - s }
    }
}

/// The tool: its body, each edge's kind, its faces in groups that join smoothly, its sharp edges
/// in runs, each face's outline in (u, v).
struct Tool<'a> {
    b: &'a Body,
    kind: Vec<EdgeKind>,
    /// Each face's group.
    group: Vec<usize>,
    /// Each face's neighbours across its smooth edges.
    smooth: Vec<Vec<usize>>,
    runs: Vec<Run>,
    /// Each edge's run and its part of it.
    run_of: Vec<Option<(usize, usize)>>,
    /// Each vertex's runs that end at it, with the run's σ there.
    ends: Vec<Vec<(usize, f64)>>,
    polys: Vec<Vec<Vec<P2>>>,
    size: f64,
}

impl<'a> Tool<'a> {
    fn new(b: &'a Body) -> Self {
        let ef = b.edge_faces();
        let ne = b.edges.len();
        let mut sides: Vec<Option<[usize; 2]>> = Vec::with_capacity(ne);
        let mut kind = Vec::with_capacity(ne);
        let normal_at = |f: usize, e: usize, s: f64, p: &P3| {
            let face = &b.faces[f];
            let hint = face.loops.iter().flatten().find(|c| c.edge == e).map(|c| {
                let uv = c.pc.point(s);
                (uv.x, uv.y)
            });
            let (u, v) = face.surf.project(p, hint);
            face.surf.normal(u, v) * if face.sense { 1.0 } else { -1.0 }
        };
        for (e, faces) in ef.iter().enumerate() {
            let two = (faces.len() == 2 && faces[0] != faces[1] && !b.edges[e].degenerate)
                .then(|| [faces[0], faces[1]]);
            // The most its faces' normals differ along it.
            let bend = two.map(|[fa, fb]| {
                let ed = &b.edges[e];
                (0..=8)
                    .map(|i| {
                        let s = ed.t[0] + (ed.t[1] - ed.t[0]) * i as f64 / 8.0;
                        let p = ed.point(s);
                        let (na, nb) = (normal_at(fa, e, s, &p), normal_at(fb, e, s, &p));
                        na.cross(&nb).norm().atan2(na.dot(&nb))
                    })
                    .fold(0.0, f64::max)
            });
            kind.push(match (two, bend) {
                (Some(_), Some(a)) if a < SMOOTH => EdgeKind::Smooth,
                (Some(_), Some(_)) => match super::blend::edge_convex(b, e) {
                    Some(true) => EdgeKind::Convex,
                    Some(false) => EdgeKind::Concave,
                    None => EdgeKind::Smooth,
                },
                _ => EdgeKind::Other,
            });
            sides.push(two);
        }
        // The faces' groups: joined over smooth edges.
        let nf = b.faces.len();
        let mut group: Vec<usize> = (0..nf).collect();
        fn root(g: &mut [usize], mut i: usize) -> usize {
            while g[i] != i {
                g[i] = g[g[i]];
                i = g[i];
            }
            i
        }
        let mut smooth: Vec<Vec<usize>> = vec![Vec::new(); nf];
        for e in 0..ne {
            if kind[e] == EdgeKind::Smooth
                && let Some([fa, fb]) = sides[e]
            {
                let (ra, rb) = (root(&mut group, fa), root(&mut group, fb));
                group[ra] = rb;
                if !smooth[fa].contains(&fb) {
                    smooth[fa].push(fb);
                    smooth[fb].push(fa);
                }
            }
        }
        for f in 0..nf {
            group[f] = root(&mut group, f);
        }
        // The sharp edges' runs: two of them go on from one another at a vertex where they are
        // the only two between their groups and their directions agree.
        let sharp = |e: usize| matches!(kind[e], EdgeKind::Convex | EdgeKind::Concave);
        let pair = |e: usize| -> Option<[usize; 2]> {
            let [fa, fb] = sides[e]?;
            let (ga, gb) = (group[fa], group[fb]);
            (ga != gb).then_some(if ga < gb { [ga, gb] } else { [gb, ga] })
        };
        // An edge's direction away from its end `end` (0: its start).
        let away = |e: usize, end: usize| -> V3 {
            let ed = &b.edges[e];
            let d = ed.curve.tangent(ed.t[end]).normalize();
            if end == 0 { d } else { -d }
        };
        let mut at_vertex: Vec<Vec<(usize, usize)>> = vec![Vec::new(); b.verts.len()];
        for e in 0..ne {
            if sharp(e) && pair(e).is_some() && !b.edges[e].closed() {
                at_vertex[b.edges[e].v[0]].push((e, 0));
                at_vertex[b.edges[e].v[1]].push((e, 1));
            }
        }
        // The edge that goes on from `e` past its end `end`, and the end of it that joins.
        let onward = |e: usize, end: usize| -> Option<(usize, usize)> {
            let v = b.edges[e].v[end];
            let same: Vec<(usize, usize)> = at_vertex[v]
                .iter()
                .copied()
                .filter(|&(o, _)| o != e && pair(o) == pair(e) && kind[o] == kind[e])
                .collect();
            let [(o, oe)] = same.as_slice() else {
                return None;
            };
            (away(e, end).dot(&away(*o, *oe)) < -(1.0 - 0.5 * SMOOTH * SMOOTH)).then_some((*o, *oe))
        };
        let mut runs: Vec<Run> = Vec::new();
        let mut run_of: Vec<Option<(usize, usize)>> = vec![None; ne];
        for e0 in 0..ne {
            if !sharp(e0) || run_of[e0].is_some() {
                continue;
            }
            let Some(groups) = pair(e0) else {
                continue;
            };
            let mut parts: Vec<(usize, bool)> = Vec::new();
            let closed = b.edges[e0].closed();
            if closed {
                if !b.edges[e0].curve.is_periodic() {
                    continue;
                }
                parts.push((e0, true));
            } else {
                // Back from its start to the run's first edge, then forward to its last.
                let (mut e, mut end) = (e0, 0);
                let mut guard = 0;
                while let Some((o, oe)) = onward(e, end) {
                    if o == e0 || guard > ne {
                        break;
                    }
                    (e, end) = (o, 1 - oe);
                    guard += 1;
                }
                // (`end` is the end of `e` the run starts at.)
                let mut fwd = end == 0;
                loop {
                    parts.push((e, fwd));
                    let Some((o, oe)) = onward(e, if fwd { 1 } else { 0 }) else {
                        break;
                    };
                    if parts.iter().any(|p| p.0 == o) {
                        break;
                    }
                    (e, fwd) = (o, oe == 0);
                }
            }
            let mut start = vec![0.0];
            let mut faces = Vec::new();
            for &(e, _) in &parts {
                let ed = &b.edges[e];
                start.push(start[start.len() - 1] + (ed.t[1] - ed.t[0]));
                let [fa, fb] = sides[e].expect("a sharp edge has two faces");
                faces.push(if group[fa] == groups[0] {
                    [fa, fb]
                } else {
                    [fb, fa]
                });
            }
            let r = runs.len();
            for (k, &(e, _)) in parts.iter().enumerate() {
                run_of[e] = Some((r, k));
            }
            runs.push(Run {
                parts,
                start,
                faces,
                groups,
                kind: kind[e0],
                closed,
            });
        }
        if std::env::var_os("CADRS_GEN_EDGES").is_some() {
            for (r, run) in runs.iter().enumerate() {
                let (mut gap, mut turn, mut bend) = (0.0f64, 0.0f64, [0.0f64; 2]);
                for k in 1..run.parts.len() {
                    let ends = |k: usize, at_start: bool| {
                        let (e, fwd) = run.parts[k];
                        let ed = &b.edges[e];
                        let s = if at_start == fwd { ed.t[0] } else { ed.t[1] };
                        let (p, d, _) = ed.curve.d2(s);
                        let d = d.normalize() * if fwd { 1.0 } else { -1.0 };
                        let n = [0, 1].map(|side| normal_at(run.faces[k][side], e, s, &p));
                        (p, d, n)
                    };
                    let (pa, da, na) = ends(k - 1, false);
                    let (pb, db, nb) = ends(k, true);
                    gap = gap.max((pa - pb).norm());
                    turn = turn.max(da.cross(&db).norm());
                    for side in 0..2 {
                        bend[side] = bend[side].max(na[side].cross(&nb[side]).norm());
                    }
                }
                eprintln!(
                    "  run {r}: {} parts of {:?} between groups {:?}, span {:.4}; at its joins: gap {gap:.2e}, turn {turn:.2e}, faces' normals {:.2e} and {:.2e}; starts {:?}",
                    run.parts.len(),
                    run.kind,
                    run.groups,
                    run.span(),
                    bend[0],
                    bend[1],
                    run.start
                        .iter()
                        .take(6)
                        .map(|x| (x * 1e4).round() / 1e4)
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                );
            }
        }
        let polys = b
            .faces
            .iter()
            .map(|f| super::classify::face_polygons(b, f))
            .collect();
        let mut ends: Vec<Vec<(usize, f64)>> = vec![Vec::new(); b.verts.len()];
        for (r, run) in runs.iter().enumerate() {
            if run.closed {
                continue;
            }
            let (first, last) = (run.parts[0], run.parts[run.parts.len() - 1]);
            ends[b.edges[first.0].v[usize::from(!first.1)]].push((r, 0.0));
            ends[b.edges[last.0].v[usize::from(last.1)]].push((r, run.span()));
        }
        Tool {
            b,
            kind,
            group,
            smooth,
            runs,
            run_of,
            ends,
            polys,
            size: b.bbox().diagonal().max(super::tol::POINT),
        }
    }

    /// Face `f`'s (u, v) at the point `p` of its edge `e` (at the edge's parameter `s`).
    fn uv_at_edge(&self, f: usize, e: usize, s: f64, p: &P3) -> P2 {
        let face = &self.b.faces[f];
        let hint = face.loops.iter().flatten().find(|c| c.edge == e).map(|c| {
            let uv = c.pc.point(s);
            (uv.x, uv.y)
        });
        let (u, v) = face.surf.project(p, hint);
        P2::new(u, v)
    }

    /// Face `f`'s point and outward normal at (u, v).
    fn at(&self, f: usize, uv: P2) -> (P3, V3) {
        let face = &self.b.faces[f];
        let n = face.surf.normal(uv.x, uv.y) * if face.sense { 1.0 } else { -1.0 };
        (face.surf.eval(uv.x, uv.y), n)
    }

    fn inside(&self, f: usize, uv: P2) -> bool {
        super::classify::in_face(&self.polys[f], &self.b.faces[f].surf, uv, 1e-9)
            != super::classify::InFace::Outside
    }

    /// A run's point at σ: (its edge, the edge's parameter, the point, its direction as σ
    /// grows, the run's two faces there).
    fn on_run(&self, r: usize, sigma: f64) -> Option<(usize, f64, P3, V3, [usize; 2])> {
        let run = &self.runs[r];
        let (k, s, sign) = run.part(self.b, sigma)?;
        let e = run.parts[k].0;
        let (p, d1, _) = self.b.edges[e].curve.d2(s);
        Some((e, s, p, d1 * sign, run.faces[k]))
    }
}

/// Newton's method on two equations in two unknowns, their slopes by differences of `h`:
/// the root within `tol` (of each equation), no farther than `reach` from the start.
fn newton2(
    f: &dyn Fn(f64, f64) -> Option<(f64, f64)>,
    start: (f64, f64),
    h: (f64, f64),
    tol: f64,
    reach: (f64, f64),
) -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
    newton2_sided(f, start, h, tol, reach, false)
}

/// [`newton2`]; `sided`: where the equations have no value a step to one side of the unknowns
/// (a place at the very end of what it is on), their slopes are taken from the other side
/// alone.
fn newton2_sided(
    f: &dyn Fn(f64, f64) -> Option<(f64, f64)>,
    start: (f64, f64),
    h: (f64, f64),
    tol: f64,
    reach: (f64, f64),
    sided: bool,
) -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
    let (mut x, mut y) = start;
    for _ in 0..40 {
        let (a, b) = f(x, y)?;
        if a.abs() <= tol && b.abs() <= tol {
            return Some((x, y));
        }
        // The slopes along one unknown, from the values a step each way.
        let slopes = |up: Option<(f64, f64)>, down: Option<(f64, f64)>, h: f64| match (up, down) {
            (Some(u), Some(d)) => Some(((u.0 - d.0) / (2.0 * h), (u.1 - d.1) / (2.0 * h))),
            (Some(u), None) if sided => Some(((u.0 - a) / h, (u.1 - b) / h)),
            (None, Some(d)) if sided => Some(((a - d.0) / h, (b - d.1) / h)),
            _ => None,
        };
        let (axx, bxx) = slopes(f(x + h.0, y), f(x - h.0, y), h.0)?;
        let (ayy, byy) = slopes(f(x, y + h.1), f(x, y - h.1), h.1)?;
        let det = axx * byy - ayy * bxx;
        if det.abs() < 1e-300 || !det.is_finite() {
            return None;
        }
        let dx = (-a * byy + b * ayy) / det;
        let dy = (-b * axx + a * bxx) / det;
        // (A step past the reach is cut to it: far from the root the slopes mislead.)
        let k = (reach.0 / dx.abs().max(1e-300))
            .min(reach.1 / dy.abs().max(1e-300))
            .min(1.0);
        x += dx * k;
        y += dy * k;
        if (x - start.0).abs() > 8.0 * reach.0 || (y - start.1).abs() > 8.0 * reach.1 {
            return None;
        }
    }
    None
}

/// A node: where the contact of the face group on `side` of run `r` reaches the run, at the
/// run's σ and the instant `t`; `p` where that is, seen from the target.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]
struct Node {
    r: usize,
    side: usize,
    sigma: f64,
    t: f64,
    p: P3,
}

/// A corner: where a vertex of the tool passes through a slice, at the instant `t`. The path of
/// one run that ends at the vertex ends there and another's goes on (each run with its σ at
/// the vertex): the outline turns from the one edge's path to the other's.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]
struct Corner {
    v: usize,
    t: f64,
    p: P3,
    before: (usize, f64),
    after: (usize, f64),
}

/// What a chain is made of between two joints: a run's stretch, or a face group's contact.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]
enum Link {
    Edge(usize),
    Face(usize),
    /// No part of the tool: a sheet that only closes the plug, outside the target, where a
    /// stretch of the tooth space lacks a link the next stretch has (see [`Span::skip`]).
    Fill,
}

/// Where a link's point is on the tool: on its run, or on a face of its group.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]
enum Place {
    Run(f64),
    Face(usize, P2),
}

/// Where two links of a chain meet: at a node, where a contact comes to its run and the two
/// are tangent; or at a crossing, where one link's curve runs into what the other has swept
/// (a pinion's flank undercut by its own tip) and the boundary turns a corner: each link's
/// place and instant there, the link before the joint and the link after.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]
enum Joint {
    Node(Node),
    Cross {
        before: (Place, f64),
        after: (Place, f64),
        p: P3,
    },
    /// Where a run's stretch ends at a vertex of the tool and another's goes on.
    Corner(Corner),
    /// Between a link and a filler ([`Link::Fill`]), or two fillers: no joint of the tool's.
    Free,
}

impl Joint {
    /// The instant on the link before the joint, or (`after`) on the link after it.
    fn t(&self, after: bool) -> f64 {
        match self {
            Joint::Node(n) => n.t,
            Joint::Cross {
                before, after: a, ..
            } => {
                if after {
                    a.1
                } else {
                    before.1
                }
            }
            Joint::Corner(k) => k.t,
            Joint::Free => f64::NAN,
        }
    }

    /// The joint as a chain walked the other way has it.
    fn turned(&self) -> Joint {
        match *self {
            Joint::Node(n) => Joint::Node(n),
            Joint::Cross { before, after, p } => Joint::Cross {
                before: after,
                after: before,
                p,
            },
            Joint::Corner(k) => Joint::Corner(Corner {
                before: k.after,
                after: k.before,
                ..k
            }),
            Joint::Free => Joint::Free,
        }
    }

    /// Where the joint is, seen from the target.
    fn point(&self) -> Option<P3> {
        match self {
            Joint::Node(n) => Some(n.p),
            Joint::Cross { p, .. } => Some(*p),
            Joint::Corner(k) => Some(k.p),
            Joint::Free => None,
        }
    }

    /// The joint's instants, for the log.
    fn told(&self) -> String {
        match self {
            Joint::Node(n) => format!("{:.4}", n.t),
            Joint::Cross { before, after, .. } => format!("{:.4}x{:.4}", before.1, after.1),
            Joint::Corner(k) => format!("{:.4}v{}", k.t, k.v),
            Joint::Free => "free".to_string(),
        }
    }
}

/// A chain in one slice: its joints, the link before each and the one after the last (the two
/// end links running on past the target), which way in time each end link runs from its joint
/// (`out`), and the turn about the target's axis its angles are told next to (`about`).
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
struct Chain {
    joints: Vec<Joint>,
    links: Vec<Link>,
    out: [f64; 2],
    about: f64,
}

impl Chain {
    /// The chain walked the other way.
    fn turned(&self) -> Chain {
        Chain {
            joints: self.joints.iter().rev().map(Joint::turned).collect(),
            links: self.links.iter().rev().copied().collect(),
            out: [self.out[1], self.out[0]],
            about: self.about,
        }
    }
}

/// What following a link reaches: its points, each with its instant and its place on the tool,
/// and the node it ends at.
struct Reach {
    pts: Vec<(f64, P3, Place)>,
    node: Option<Node>,
    /// Or the vertex of the tool its run ends at: (the vertex, the instant, the point, the
    /// run's σ there).
    corner: Option<(usize, f64, P3, f64)>,
}

/// A link's curve in a slice, as something another link may cross: its points, and theirs in
/// the slice's own coordinates with the box they fill.
struct Cand {
    link: Link,
    pts: Vec<(f64, P3, Place)>,
    ab: Vec<(f64, f64)>,
    lo: (f64, f64),
    hi: (f64, f64),
}

/// Where a link runs into what another has swept: after point `at` of its reach, at the
/// places and instants `before` (its own) and `after` (the other link's, `link`), the other
/// link followed on from there the way `dir` in time.
struct Crossing {
    at: usize,
    before: (Place, f64),
    link: Link,
    after: (Place, f64),
    dir: f64,
    p: P3,
}

/// The cut's working state: the tool, its motion, the chart and the target's distance.
struct Gen<'a> {
    tool: &'a Tool<'a>,
    motion: &'a Motion<'a>,
    chart: Chart,
    target: &'a MeshDistance,
    /// How far outside the target counts as clear of it.
    clear: f64,
    /// The tool's speed (per unit of t) at its far reach.
    speed: f64,
    /// The time step of a search or a march: the tool moves a small share of its size in it.
    dt: f64,
    /// The times the motion covers: 0 to 1, or without end for one that repeats.
    span: Option<(f64, f64)>,
    /// A motion that repeats: its period, and the turn about the target's axis from one time
    /// round to the next.
    repeat: Option<(f64, Axis, f64)>,
    /// The instants nodes are searched for over, and how near the target they are kept.
    window: (f64, f64),
    reach: f64,
    /// The tool's mesh and box, for checking what it sweeps.
    tool_mesh: &'a MeshDistance,
    tool_box: Bbox,
    /// How many steps of time from a joint two curves share a crossing of theirs must be, to be
    /// taken for one and not the joint itself.
    near_joint: f64,
    debug: bool,
    trace: bool,
}

impl Gen<'_> {
    fn world(&self, t: f64, p: &P3) -> P3 {
        let (r, d) = self.motion.place(t);
        P3::from(r * p.coords + d)
    }

    /// g of face `f` at its point (u, v) and the instant t, as a length (a share of the speed).
    fn g(&self, f: usize, uv: P2, tw: &Twist) -> f64 {
        let (p, n) = self.tool.at(f, uv);
        n.dot(&(tw.0.cross(&p.coords) + tw.1)) * self.tool.size / self.speed
    }

    /// g of the face on `side` of run `r` at the run's σ.
    fn g_run(&self, r: usize, side: usize, sigma: f64, tw: &Twist) -> Option<f64> {
        let (e, s, p, _, faces) = self.tool.on_run(r, sigma)?;
        Some(self.g(faces[side], self.tool.uv_at_edge(faces[side], e, s, &p), tw))
    }

    /// Where run `r` crosses slice `c` at t, from the guess σ.
    fn run_in_slice(&self, r: usize, t: f64, c: f64, mut sigma: f64) -> Option<f64> {
        let (rot, d) = self.motion.place(t);
        let reach = 0.02 * self.tool.runs[r].span();
        for _ in 0..40 {
            let (_, _, p, d1, _) = self.tool.on_run(r, sigma)?;
            let x = P3::from(rot * p.coords + d);
            let miss = self.chart.c(&x) - c;
            if miss.abs() <= 1e-13 * self.tool.size.max(c.abs()) {
                return Some(sigma);
            }
            let slope = self.chart.grad(&x).dot(&(rot * d1));
            if slope.abs() < 1e-300 {
                return None;
            }
            sigma -= (miss / slope).clamp(-reach, reach);
            // (Under a roof a link is followed to the very end of its run, a vertex of the
            // tool: a step a hair past the end is brought back to it.)
            // (And a link bounded at a vertex's instant as nearly as its bound's curve follows
            // it is at the vertex there, where the run itself is a hair short of the slice.)
            if self.near_joint < 1.0 && !self.tool.runs[r].closed {
                let span = self.tool.runs[r].span();
                if (sigma < 0.0 || sigma > span) && miss.abs() <= 2e-9 * self.tool.size {
                    return Some(sigma.clamp(0.0, span));
                }
                sigma = sigma.clamp(0.0, span);
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// The node of the face group on `side` of run `r` in slice `c`, from the guess (σ, t).
    fn node(&self, r: usize, side: usize, c: f64, guess: (f64, f64)) -> Option<Node> {
        let span = self.tool.runs[r].span();
        let eq = |sigma: f64, t: f64| -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
            let (e, s, p, _, faces) = self.tool.on_run(r, sigma)?;
            let tw = self.motion.twist(t);
            let f = faces[side];
            Some((
                self.chart.c(&self.world(t, &p)) - c,
                self.g(f, self.tool.uv_at_edge(f, e, s, &p), &tw),
            ))
        };
        let (sigma, t) = newton2_sided(
            &eq,
            guess,
            (1e-7 * self.tool.size, 1e-3 * self.dt),
            1e-12 * self.tool.size,
            (0.02 * span, 4.0 * self.dt),
            self.near_joint < 1.0,
        )?;
        let (_, _, p, _, _) = self.tool.on_run(r, sigma)?;
        Some(Node {
            r,
            side,
            sigma,
            t,
            p: self.world(t, &p),
        })
    }

    /// Face `f`'s contact point in slice `c` at t, from the guess (u, v).
    fn face_in_slice(&self, f: usize, t: f64, c: f64, guess: P2) -> Option<P2> {
        let tw = self.motion.twist(t);
        let surf = &self.tool.b.faces[f].surf;
        let (mu, mv) = surf.metric();
        // (A parameter's step as a length on the surface.)
        let h = (
            1e-6 * self.tool.size / mu.max(1e-300),
            1e-6 * self.tool.size / mv.max(1e-300),
        );
        let eq = |u: f64, v: f64| -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
            let uv = P2::new(u, v);
            let (p, _) = self.tool.at(f, uv);
            let g = self.g(f, uv, &tw);
            (g.is_finite() && p.coords.iter().all(|x| x.is_finite()))
                .then(|| (self.chart.c(&self.world(t, &p)) - c, g))
        };
        // (No farther than a small share of the tool's size in all: a contact is looked for
        // near where it was, and another of the same face, a thread's a turn on, is not it.)
        let reach = (
            HOP / 8.0 * self.tool.size / mu.max(1e-300),
            HOP / 8.0 * self.tool.size / mv.max(1e-300),
        );
        let (u, v) = newton2(&eq, (guess.x, guess.y), h, 1e-12 * self.tool.size, reach)?;
        let found = P2::new(u, v);
        let moved = (self.tool.at(f, found).0 - self.tool.at(f, guess).0).norm();
        (moved <= HOP * self.tool.size).then_some(found)
    }

    /// A face group's contact point in slice `c` at t, from a guess on one of its faces: on
    /// that face, or on one it joins smoothly (the contact having passed over to it). None
    /// where the contact is on none of them.
    fn group_in_slice(&self, t: f64, c: f64, (f, uv): (usize, P2)) -> Option<(usize, P2)> {
        let first = self.face_in_slice(f, t, c, uv);
        if let Some(u) = first
            && self.tool.inside(f, u)
        {
            return Some((f, u));
        }
        let from = self.tool.at(f, first.unwrap_or(uv)).0;
        let mut tried = vec![f];
        let mut front = vec![f];
        for _ in 0..3 {
            let mut next = Vec::new();
            for &a in &front {
                for &nb in &self.tool.smooth[a] {
                    if tried.contains(&nb) {
                        continue;
                    }
                    tried.push(nb);
                    let (u0, v0) = self.tool.b.faces[nb].surf.project(&from, None);
                    let start = P2::new(u0, v0);
                    if (self.tool.at(nb, start).0 - from).norm() > HOP * self.tool.size {
                        continue;
                    }
                    if let Some(u) = self.face_in_slice(nb, t, c, start)
                        && self.tool.inside(nb, u)
                    {
                        return Some((nb, u));
                    }
                    next.push(nb);
                }
            }
            front = next;
        }
        None
    }

    /// The instant near `guess` at which the tool's vertex `v` is in slice `c`, and where.
    fn corner(&self, v: usize, c: f64, guess: f64) -> Option<(f64, P3)> {
        let q = self.tool.b.verts[v].p;
        let miss = |t: f64| self.chart.c(&self.world(t, &q)) - c;
        let h = 1e-3 * self.dt;
        let mut t = guess;
        for _ in 0..40 {
            let m = miss(t);
            if m.abs() <= 1e-13 * self.tool.size.max(c.abs()) {
                return Some((t, self.world(t, &q)));
            }
            let slope = (miss(t + h) - miss(t - h)) / (2.0 * h);
            if slope.abs() < 1e-300 || !slope.is_finite() {
                return None;
            }
            t -= (m / slope).clamp(-4.0 * self.dt, 4.0 * self.dt);
            if (t - guess).abs() > 32.0 * self.dt {
                return None;
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// The run that goes on from the tool's vertex `v` in slice `c` at the instant `t`, where
    /// run `from` ends: one whose two faces' g are of opposite signs there (it sweeps boundary),
    /// with its σ at the vertex and the way in time it is within the slice.
    fn turn(&self, c: f64, v: usize, t: f64, from: usize) -> Option<(usize, f64, f64)> {
        let tw = self.motion.twist(t);
        self.tool.ends[v].iter().find_map(|&(r, sigma)| {
            if r == from || self.tool.runs[r].kind != EdgeKind::Convex {
                return None;
            }
            let (ga, gb) = (self.g_run(r, 0, sigma, &tw)?, self.g_run(r, 1, sigma, &tw)?);
            if ga * gb >= 0.0 {
                return None;
            }
            let probe = |dir: f64| {
                self.run_in_slice(r, t + dir * 0.25 * self.dt, c, sigma)
                    .is_some()
            };
            match (probe(1.0), probe(-1.0)) {
                (true, false) => Some((r, sigma, 1.0)),
                (false, true) => Some((r, sigma, -1.0)),
                _ => None,
            }
        })
    }

    fn in_span(&self, t: f64) -> bool {
        self.span.is_none_or(|(a, b)| t >= a && t <= b)
    }

    /// The nodes in slice `c` whose instants fall in `window`, near the target: found on a grid
    /// of each run's σ by the time (a cell where the run crosses the slice and a face's g
    /// changes sign), each then solved.
    fn nodes(&self, c: f64, window: (f64, f64), near: f64) -> Vec<Node> {
        use rayon::prelude::*;
        let b = self.tool.b;
        let nt = (((window.1 - window.0) / self.dt).ceil() as usize).clamp(8, 4096);
        let places: Vec<(Rotation3<f64>, V3, Twist)> = (0..=nt)
            .map(|j| {
                let t = window.0 + (window.1 - window.0) * j as f64 / nt as f64;
                let (r, d) = self.motion.place(t);
                (r, d, self.motion.twist(t))
            })
            .collect();
        let found: Vec<Vec<Node>> = (0..self.tool.runs.len())
            .into_par_iter()
            .map(|r| {
                let run = &self.tool.runs[r];
                let len: f64 = run
                    .parts
                    .iter()
                    .map(|&(e, _)| b.edges[e].curve.length(b.edges[e].t[0], b.edges[e].t[1]))
                    .sum();
                let ns = ((len / (self.tool.size / 256.0)).ceil() as usize).clamp(8, 16384);
                let whole = if run.closed { TAU } else { run.span() };
                let at = |i: usize| whole * i as f64 / ns as f64;
                // Each sample's point and its two faces' normals, in the tool's frame.
                let pts: Vec<(P3, V3, V3)> = (0..=ns)
                    .filter_map(|i| {
                        let (e, s, p, _, faces) = self.tool.on_run(r, at(i))?;
                        let na = self
                            .tool
                            .at(faces[0], self.tool.uv_at_edge(faces[0], e, s, &p))
                            .1;
                        let nb = self
                            .tool
                            .at(faces[1], self.tool.uv_at_edge(faces[1], e, s, &p))
                            .1;
                        Some((p, na, nb))
                    })
                    .collect();
                if pts.len() != ns + 1 {
                    return Vec::new();
                }
                let row = |j: usize| -> Vec<(f64, f64, f64)> {
                    let (rot, d, tw) = &places[j];
                    pts.iter()
                        .map(|(p, na, nb)| {
                            let vel = tw.0.cross(&p.coords) + tw.1;
                            let x = P3::from(rot * p.coords + d);
                            (self.chart.c(&x) - c, na.dot(&vel), nb.dot(&vel))
                        })
                        .collect()
                };
                let (ds, dtt) = (at(1) - at(0), (window.1 - window.0) / nt as f64);
                let mut out: Vec<Node> = Vec::new();
                let mut last = row(0);
                for j in 0..nt {
                    let next = row(j + 1);
                    for i in 0..ns {
                        let cell = [last[i], last[i + 1], next[i], next[i + 1]];
                        let mixed = |k: usize| {
                            let get = |q: &(f64, f64, f64)| [q.0, q.1, q.2][k];
                            cell.iter().any(|q| get(q) > 0.0) && cell.iter().any(|q| get(q) <= 0.0)
                        };
                        if !mixed(0) {
                            continue;
                        }
                        for side in 0..2 {
                            if !mixed(side + 1) {
                                continue;
                            }
                            let s = 0.5 * (at(i) + at(i + 1));
                            let t = window.0 + (window.1 - window.0) * (j as f64 + 0.5) / nt as f64;
                            let Some(n) = self.node(r, side, c, (s, t)) else {
                                continue;
                            };
                            if (n.sigma - s).abs() > 1.5 * ds
                                || (n.t - t).abs() > 1.5 * dtt
                                || self.target.distance(&n.p) > near
                            {
                                continue;
                            }
                            if !out.iter().any(|m| {
                                m.side == side
                                    && (m.sigma - n.sigma).abs() < 0.5 * ds
                                    && (m.t - n.t).abs() < 0.5 * dtt
                            }) {
                                out.push(n);
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    last = next;
                }
                out
            })
            .collect();
        found.into_iter().flatten().collect()
    }

    /// A link's point at a place and an instant, seen from the target.
    fn at_place(&self, link: Link, t: f64, place: Place) -> Option<P3> {
        match (link, place) {
            (Link::Edge(r), Place::Run(sigma)) => {
                Some(self.world(t, &self.tool.on_run(r, sigma)?.2))
            }
            (Link::Face(_), Place::Face(f, uv)) => Some(self.world(t, &self.tool.at(f, uv).0)),
            _ => None,
        }
    }

    /// The way into the tool at a link's point, seen from the target: against its face's
    /// normal, or its run's two faces' together.
    fn inward(&self, link: Link, t: f64, place: Place) -> Option<V3> {
        let n = match (link, place) {
            (Link::Edge(r), Place::Run(sigma)) => {
                let (e, s, p, _, faces) = self.tool.on_run(r, sigma)?;
                let of = |f: usize| self.tool.at(f, self.tool.uv_at_edge(f, e, s, &p)).1;
                of(faces[0]) + of(faces[1])
            }
            (Link::Face(_), Place::Face(f, uv)) => self.tool.at(f, uv).1,
            _ => return None,
        };
        Some(-(self.motion.place(t).0 * n))
    }

    /// A link's place at a node of it.
    fn place_at(&self, node: &Node, link: Link) -> Option<Place> {
        match link {
            Link::Edge(_) => Some(Place::Run(node.sigma)),
            Link::Face(_) => {
                let (e, s, p, _, faces) = self.tool.on_run(node.r, node.sigma)?;
                let f = faces[node.side];
                Some(Place::Face(f, self.tool.uv_at_edge(f, e, s, &p)))
            }
            Link::Fill => None,
        }
    }

    /// A link followed from a place of it at `t0`, the way `dir` in time, as far as it goes:
    /// a run's stretch while its two faces' g are of opposite signs, a face group's contact
    /// while it is within the group; to the node it ends at (None where it runs off the run,
    /// leaves the group by no run, or the motion ends). `entry`: the node it starts from.
    fn march(
        &self,
        c: f64,
        link: Link,
        from: Place,
        t0: f64,
        dir: f64,
        entry: Option<&Node>,
    ) -> Reach {
        let start = self.at_place(link, t0, from);
        let mut pts: Vec<(f64, P3, Place)> = start.map(|p| (t0, p, from)).into_iter().collect();
        let none = |pts: Vec<(f64, P3, Place)>| Reach {
            pts,
            node: None,
            corner: None,
        };
        if pts.is_empty() {
            return none(pts);
        }
        match (link, from) {
            (Link::Edge(r), Place::Run(sigma0)) => {
                let tw = self.motion.twist(t0);
                let (Some(ga), Some(gb)) =
                    (self.g_run(r, 0, sigma0, &tw), self.g_run(r, 1, sigma0, &tw))
                else {
                    return none(pts);
                };
                // Each side's sign along the stretch; from a node, its own side's is against
                // the other's, and nothing yet at the node itself.
                let at_node = entry.filter(|n| n.r == r).map(|n| n.side);
                let signs = match at_node {
                    Some(0) => [-gb.signum(), gb.signum()],
                    Some(_) => [ga.signum(), -ga.signum()],
                    None => [ga.signum(), gb.signum()],
                };
                if signs[0] * signs[1] >= 0.0 {
                    return none(pts);
                }
                let (mut sigma, mut t) = (sigma0, t0);
                for step in 1..200_000 {
                    let tn = t0 + dir * self.dt * step as f64;
                    let at = (|| {
                        if !self.in_span(tn) {
                            return None;
                        }
                        let sn = self.run_in_slice(r, tn, c, sigma)?;
                        let tw = self.motion.twist(tn);
                        Some((sn, [self.g_run(r, 0, sn, &tw)?, self.g_run(r, 1, sn, &tw)?]))
                    })();
                    let Some((sn, g)) = at else {
                        // (A run that crosses the slice at a slant passes through it in less
                        // than a step: by finer steps as far as it goes.)
                        let mut tn = tn;
                        for fine in [0.25, 0.0625, 0.015625] {
                            loop {
                                let tf = t + dir * self.dt * fine;
                                if (tn - tf) * dir <= 0.0 {
                                    break;
                                }
                                let on = (|| {
                                    if !self.in_span(tf) {
                                        return None;
                                    }
                                    let sf = self.run_in_slice(r, tf, c, sigma)?;
                                    let tw = self.motion.twist(tf);
                                    let g =
                                        [self.g_run(r, 0, sf, &tw)?, self.g_run(r, 1, sf, &tw)?];
                                    Some((sf, g, self.at_place(link, tf, Place::Run(sf))?))
                                })();
                                let Some((sf, g, x)) = on else {
                                    tn = tf;
                                    break;
                                };
                                if let Some(side) =
                                    [0, 1].into_iter().find(|&s| g[s] * signs[s] <= 0.0)
                                {
                                    let node =
                                        self.node(r, side, c, (0.5 * (sigma + sf), 0.5 * (t + tf)));
                                    if let Some(n) = &node {
                                        pts.push((n.t, n.p, Place::Run(n.sigma)));
                                    }
                                    return Reach {
                                        pts,
                                        node,
                                        corner: None,
                                    };
                                }
                                pts.push((tf, x, Place::Run(sf)));
                                (sigma, t) = (sf, tf);
                            }
                        }
                        // Off the run's end: at the vertex there, if the run's stretch goes
                        // on to it (else at the node before it).
                        let run = &self.tool.runs[r];
                        let end = if sigma < 0.5 * run.span() {
                            0.0
                        } else {
                            run.span()
                        };
                        let found = self.tool.ends.iter().position(|e| e.contains(&(r, end)));
                        let Some((v, (tv, p))) = found
                            .filter(|_| !run.closed && self.in_span(tn))
                            .and_then(|v| Some((v, self.corner(v, c, 0.5 * (t + tn))?)))
                        else {
                            return none(pts);
                        };
                        if (tv - t) * dir < -1e-9 * self.dt || (tn - tv) * dir < -1e-9 * self.dt {
                            return none(pts);
                        }
                        let tw = self.motion.twist(tv);
                        let (Some(ga), Some(gb)) =
                            (self.g_run(r, 0, end, &tw), self.g_run(r, 1, end, &tw))
                        else {
                            return none(pts);
                        };
                        if let Some(side) =
                            [0, 1].into_iter().find(|&s| [ga, gb][s] * signs[s] <= 0.0)
                        {
                            let node = self.node(r, side, c, (0.5 * (sigma + end), 0.5 * (t + tv)));
                            if let Some(n) = &node {
                                pts.push((n.t, n.p, Place::Run(n.sigma)));
                            }
                            return Reach {
                                pts,
                                node,
                                corner: None,
                            };
                        }
                        pts.push((tv, p, Place::Run(end)));
                        return Reach {
                            pts,
                            node: None,
                            corner: Some((v, tv, p, end)),
                        };
                    };
                    // (The other side's first: at a node's first step its own is next to
                    // nothing either way.)
                    let order = match at_node {
                        Some(s) => [1 - s, s],
                        None => [0, 1],
                    };
                    let ended = order
                        .into_iter()
                        .find(|&s| g[s] * signs[s] <= 0.0 && !(step == 1 && at_node == Some(s)));
                    if let Some(side) = ended {
                        let node = self.node(r, side, c, (0.5 * (sigma + sn), 0.5 * (t + tn)));
                        if let Some(n) = &node {
                            pts.push((n.t, n.p, Place::Run(n.sigma)));
                        }
                        return Reach {
                            pts,
                            node,
                            corner: None,
                        };
                    }
                    let Some(x) = self.at_place(link, tn, Place::Run(sn)) else {
                        return none(pts);
                    };
                    pts.push((tn, x, Place::Run(sn)));
                    (sigma, t) = (sn, tn);
                }
                none(pts)
            }
            (Link::Face(group), Place::Face(f0, uv0)) => {
                let b = self.tool.b;
                let mut on = (f0, uv0);
                let mut t = t0;
                for step in 1..200_000 {
                    let tn = t0 + dir * self.dt * step as f64;
                    if !self.in_span(tn) {
                        return none(pts);
                    }
                    if let Some(next) = self.group_in_slice(tn, c, on) {
                        pts.push((
                            tn,
                            self.world(tn, &self.tool.at(next.0, next.1).0),
                            Place::Face(next.0, next.1),
                        ));
                        (on, t) = (next, tn);
                        continue;
                    }
                    // It left between t and tn: where, by halving.
                    let (mut lo, mut hi) = (t, tn);
                    for _ in 0..48 {
                        let mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi);
                        match self.group_in_slice(mid, c, on) {
                            Some(m) => (lo, on) = (mid, m),
                            None => hi = mid,
                        }
                    }
                    let x = self.tool.at(on.0, on.1).0;
                    // The run it left by: of the face's sharp edges, the nearest (not where
                    // it came from).
                    let mut best: Option<(f64, usize, f64)> = None;
                    for co in b.faces[on.0].loops.iter().flatten() {
                        let Some((r, k)) = self.tool.run_of[co.edge] else {
                            continue;
                        };
                        if !self.tool.runs[r].groups.contains(&group) {
                            continue;
                        }
                        let ed = &b.edges[co.edge];
                        let s = ed.curve.closest(&x, ed.t[0], ed.t[1]);
                        let dist = (ed.point(s) - x).norm();
                        let sigma = if self.tool.runs[r].closed {
                            s - ed.t[0]
                        } else {
                            self.tool.runs[r].sigma(b, k, s)
                        };
                        if entry.is_some_and(|n| {
                            n.r == r && (sigma - n.sigma).abs() < 1e-6 * self.tool.size && step == 1
                        }) {
                            continue;
                        }
                        if best.is_none_or(|(d, ..)| dist < d) {
                            best = Some((dist, r, sigma));
                        }
                    }
                    let node = best
                        .filter(|(dist, ..)| *dist <= 1e-3 * self.tool.size)
                        .and_then(|(_, r, sigma)| {
                            let side = usize::from(self.tool.runs[r].groups[0] != group);
                            self.node(r, side, c, (sigma, lo))
                        });
                    if let Some(n) = &node
                        && let Some(place) = self.place_at(n, link)
                    {
                        pts.push((n.t, n.p, place));
                    }
                    return Reach {
                        pts,
                        node,
                        corner: None,
                    };
                }
                none(pts)
            }
            _ => none(pts),
        }
    }

    /// From a node along its run, where the run sweeps boundary. None where it sweeps none
    /// there (a run that isn't convex, or one whose other face's g is nothing too).
    fn along_edge(&self, c: f64, from: &Node) -> Option<Reach> {
        let r = from.r;
        if self.tool.runs[r].kind != EdgeKind::Convex {
            return None;
        }
        let other = 1 - from.side;
        let go = self.g_run(r, other, from.sigma, &self.motion.twist(from.t))?;
        if go.abs() < 1e-9 * self.tool.size {
            return None;
        }
        // The side of the node (earlier or later) where this face's g is against the other's.
        let probe = |dir: f64| -> Option<f64> {
            let t = from.t + dir * 0.25 * self.dt;
            let sigma = self.run_in_slice(r, t, c, from.sigma)?;
            self.g_run(r, from.side, sigma, &self.motion.twist(t))
        };
        let dir = match (probe(1.0), probe(-1.0)) {
            (Some(g), _) if g * go < 0.0 => 1.0,
            (_, Some(g)) if g * go < 0.0 => -1.0,
            _ => return None,
        };
        Some(self.march(
            c,
            Link::Edge(r),
            Place::Run(from.sigma),
            from.t,
            dir,
            Some(from),
        ))
    }

    /// From a node across its face group, along the group's contact in the slice. None where
    /// the contact doesn't run into the group from the node.
    fn across_face(&self, c: f64, from: &Node) -> Option<Reach> {
        let link = Link::Face(self.tool.runs[from.r].groups[from.side]);
        let Place::Face(f0, uv0) = self.place_at(from, link)? else {
            return None;
        };
        // The side (earlier or later) on which the contact runs into the group.
        let probe = |dir: f64| self.group_in_slice(from.t + dir * 0.25 * self.dt, c, (f0, uv0));
        let dir = match (probe(1.0), probe(-1.0)) {
            (Some(_), None) => 1.0,
            (None, Some(_)) => -1.0,
            _ => return None,
        };
        Some(self.march(c, link, Place::Face(f0, uv0), from.t, dir, Some(from)))
    }

    /// The link `link` followed from `node`.
    fn follow(&self, c: f64, node: &Node, link: Link) -> Option<Reach> {
        match link {
            Link::Edge(_) => self.along_edge(c, node),
            Link::Face(_) => self.across_face(c, node),
            Link::Fill => None,
        }
    }

    /// The link that goes on from `node`, reached by `by` (None at a chain's start, where
    /// `face_first` picks the side), and what following it reaches.
    fn next(
        &self,
        c: f64,
        node: &Node,
        by: Option<Link>,
        face_first: bool,
    ) -> Option<(Reach, Link)> {
        let link = match by {
            None if face_first => Link::Face(self.tool.runs[node.r].groups[node.side]),
            None => Link::Edge(node.r),
            Some(Link::Face(_)) => Link::Edge(node.r),
            Some(Link::Edge(_)) => Link::Face(self.tool.runs[node.r].groups[node.side]),
            Some(Link::Fill) => return None,
        };
        let r = self.follow(c, node, link);
        if self.trace {
            eprintln!(
                "  from node (run {} {:?}, side {}, σ {:.5}, t {:.6}, {:.3} from the target) by {by:?}: {}",
                node.r,
                self.tool.runs[node.r].kind,
                node.side,
                node.sigma,
                node.t,
                self.target.distance(&node.p),
                match &r {
                    Some(reach) => self.told(link, reach),
                    None => "nothing".to_string(),
                }
            );
        }
        Some((r?, link))
    }

    /// A reach, for the trace.
    fn told(&self, link: Link, reach: &Reach) -> String {
        let far = |f: fn(f64, f64) -> f64, from: f64| {
            reach
                .pts
                .iter()
                .map(|p| self.target.distance(&p.1))
                .fold(from, f)
        };
        format!(
            "{link:?}, {} points, nearest {:.3}, farthest {:.3}, to {}",
            reach.pts.len(),
            far(f64::min, f64::INFINITY),
            far(f64::max, f64::NEG_INFINITY),
            match &reach.node {
                Some(n) => format!(
                    "(run {} {:?}, side {}, σ {:.5}, t {:.6})",
                    n.r, self.tool.runs[n.r].kind, n.side, n.sigma, n.t
                ),
                None => match reach.corner {
                    Some((v, t, ..)) => format!("vertex {v} at t {t:.6}"),
                    None => "no node".to_string(),
                },
            }
        )
    }

    fn clear_of_target(&self, p: &P3) -> bool {
        self.target.distance(p) > self.clear
    }

    /// A vector at a point of a slice, in the slice's own coordinates (as lengths).
    fn within(&self, p: &P3, v: &V3, about: f64) -> (f64, f64) {
        let h = 1e-6 * self.tool.size;
        let (a0, b0) = self.chart.inner(p, about);
        let (c, _) = (self.chart.c(p), 0.0);
        let ea = self.chart.point(c, (a0 + h, b0)) - self.chart.point(c, (a0 - h, b0));
        let eb = self.chart.point(c, (a0, b0 + h)) - self.chart.point(c, (a0, b0 - h));
        (
            v.dot(&ea) / ea.norm().max(1e-300),
            v.dot(&eb) / eb.norm().max(1e-300),
        )
    }

    /// Which way a link's point moves within slice `c` as t grows, at a place and an instant
    /// of it (in the slice's own coordinates, as lengths; from points a little to each side, or
    /// to the one side the link is on).
    fn heading(
        &self,
        c: f64,
        link: Link,
        (place, t): (Place, f64),
        about: f64,
    ) -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
        let eta = 0.05 * self.dt;
        let at = |t: f64| self.at_place(link, t, self.place(link, t, c, place)?);
        let here = at(t)?;
        let (a, b) = (at(t - eta).unwrap_or(here), at(t + eta).unwrap_or(here));
        let v = self.within(&here, &(b - a), about);
        (v.0.hypot(v.1) > 0.0).then_some(v)
    }

    /// Where two links cross in slice `c`, from places and instants near it: each link's place
    /// and instant there, and the point.
    fn cross_at(
        &self,
        c: f64,
        (la, pa, ta): (Link, Place, f64),
        (lb, pb, tb): (Link, Place, f64),
        about: f64,
    ) -> Option<Joint> {
        let x0 = self.at_place(lb, tb, pb)?;
        let eq = |ta: f64, tb: f64| -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
            let xa = self.at_place(la, ta, self.place(la, ta, c, pa)?)?;
            let xb = self.at_place(lb, tb, self.place(lb, tb, c, pb)?)?;
            Some(self.within(&x0, &(xa - xb), about))
        };
        let (ta, tb) = newton2_sided(
            &eq,
            (ta, tb),
            (1e-3 * self.dt, 1e-3 * self.dt),
            1e-12 * self.tool.size,
            (4.0 * self.dt, 4.0 * self.dt),
            self.near_joint < 1.0,
        )?;
        // (A run and the contact of a face of its own meet at their node too, each at the same
        // instant: that is no crossing.)
        let own = |edge: Link, face: Link| matches!((edge, face), (Link::Edge(r), Link::Face(g)) if self.tool.runs[r].groups.contains(&g));
        if self.near_joint < 1.0 && (own(la, lb) || own(lb, la)) && (ta - tb).abs() < 1e-5 * self.dt
        {
            return None;
        }
        let (pa, pb) = (self.place(la, ta, c, pa)?, self.place(lb, tb, c, pb)?);
        Some(Joint::Cross {
            before: (pa, ta),
            after: (pb, tb),
            p: self.at_place(lb, tb, pb)?,
        })
    }

    /// The curves of slice `c` a link may cross: each node's two links followed from it, and
    /// for a motion that repeats their copies a few turns of the tool before and after (the
    /// same link as it cuts the next tooth space, turned to this one).
    fn cands(&self, c: f64, nodes: &[Node], about: f64) -> Vec<Cand> {
        use rayon::prelude::*;
        let reaches: Vec<(Link, Reach)> = nodes
            .par_iter()
            .flat_map_iter(|n| {
                [
                    Link::Face(self.tool.runs[n.r].groups[n.side]),
                    Link::Edge(n.r),
                ]
                .into_iter()
                .filter_map(|link| Some((link, self.follow(c, n, link)?)))
                .flat_map(|(link, reach)| {
                    // (And the runs that go on from the vertex a run's path ends at.)
                    let mut on: Vec<(Link, Reach)> = Vec::new();
                    if let (Link::Edge(mut r), Some(mut k)) = (link, reach.corner) {
                        for _ in 0..6 {
                            let Some((next, sigma, dir)) = self.turn(c, k.0, k.1, r) else {
                                break;
                            };
                            let link = Link::Edge(next);
                            let far = self.march(c, link, Place::Run(sigma), k.1, dir, None);
                            let corner = far.corner;
                            on.push((link, far));
                            match corner {
                                Some(at) => (k, r) = (at, next),
                                None => break,
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    on.insert(0, (link, reach));
                    on
                })
                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
            })
            .filter(|(_, r)| r.pts.len() >= 2)
            .collect();
        let mut out: Vec<Cand> = Vec::new();
        let ends = |pts: &[(f64, P3, Place)]| (pts[0].0, pts[pts.len() - 1].0);
        for (link, reach) in reaches {
            let (a, z) = ends(&reach.pts);
            let same = |x: f64, y: f64| (x - y).abs() < 0.5 * self.dt;
            if out.iter().any(|o| {
                let (oa, oz) = ends(&o.pts);
                o.link == link && ((same(a, oa) && same(z, oz)) || (same(a, oz) && same(z, oa)))
            }) {
                continue;
            }
            let copies: Vec<i32> = match self.repeat {
                Some(_) => (-6..=6).collect(),
                None => vec![0],
            };
            for k in copies {
                let pts: Vec<(f64, P3, Place)> = match (k, self.repeat) {
                    (0, _) | (_, None) => reach.pts.iter().map(|p| (p.0, p.1, p.2)).collect(),
                    (k, Some((period, axis, angle))) => {
                        let turn = Rotation3::from_axis_angle(&axis.dir, angle * k as f64);
                        let o = axis.origin.coords;
                        reach
                            .pts
                            .iter()
                            .map(|p| {
                                (
                                    p.0 + period * k as f64,
                                    P3::from(turn * (p.1.coords - o) + o),
                                    p.2,
                                )
                            })
                            .collect()
                    }
                };
                // (Only what comes near the target.)
                if !pts
                    .iter()
                    .any(|p| self.target.distance(&p.1) < 4.0 * self.clear)
                {
                    continue;
                }
                let ab: Vec<(f64, f64)> =
                    pts.iter().map(|p| self.chart.inner(&p.1, about)).collect();
                let lo = ab.iter().fold((f64::INFINITY, f64::INFINITY), |m, q| {
                    (m.0.min(q.0), m.1.min(q.1))
                });
                let hi = ab
                    .iter()
                    .fold((f64::NEG_INFINITY, f64::NEG_INFINITY), |m, q| {
                        (m.0.max(q.0), m.1.max(q.1))
                    });
                out.push(Cand {
                    link,
                    pts,
                    ab,
                    lo,
                    hi,
                });
            }
        }
        out
    }

    /// The first place along a link's reach where it runs into what another link has swept.
    fn first_crossing(
        &self,
        c: f64,
        link: Link,
        reach: &Reach,
        cands: &[Cand],
        about: f64,
    ) -> Option<Crossing> {
        let ab: Vec<(f64, f64)> = reach
            .pts
            .iter()
            .map(|p| self.chart.inner(&p.1, about))
            .collect();
        let cross = |u: (f64, f64), v: (f64, f64)| u.0 * v.1 - u.1 * v.0;
        let sub = |u: (f64, f64), v: (f64, f64)| (u.0 - v.0, u.1 - v.1);
        let through = |q: &P3| -> Vec<bool> {
            cands
                .iter()
                .map(|cand| {
                    cand.pts
                        .iter()
                        .any(|p| (p.1 - q).norm() < 1e-6 * self.tool.size)
                })
                .collect()
        };
        let (Some(first), Some(last)) = (reach.pts.first(), reach.pts.last()) else {
            return None;
        };
        let (at_start, at_end) = (through(&first.1), through(&last.1));
        for i in 0..ab.len().saturating_sub(1) {
            let (a0, a1) = (ab[i], ab[i + 1]);
            let da = sub(a1, a0);
            let (lo, hi) = (
                (a0.0.min(a1.0), a0.1.min(a1.1)),
                (a0.0.max(a1.0), a0.1.max(a1.1)),
            );
            // The crossings of this stretch, the first along it taken.
            let mut found: Option<(f64, Crossing)> = None;
            for (ci, cand) in cands.iter().enumerate() {
                if cand.hi.0 < lo.0 || cand.lo.0 > hi.0 || cand.hi.1 < lo.1 || cand.lo.1 > hi.1 {
                    continue;
                }
                // (A curve that goes through the joint this link starts or ends at is tangent
                // to it there, and may run back along this one, to cross it at the least of
                // angles: its crossings are told by the two curves' own directions where they
                // meet, not their points', and are none at the joint itself.)
                let through = at_start[ci] || at_end[ci];
                for j in 0..cand.ab.len() - 1 {
                    let (b0, b1) = (cand.ab[j], cand.ab[j + 1]);
                    if b0.0.max(b1.0) < lo.0
                        || b0.0.min(b1.0) > hi.0
                        || b0.1.max(b1.1) < lo.1
                        || b0.1.min(b1.1) > hi.1
                    {
                        continue;
                    }
                    let db = sub(b1, b0);
                    let det = cross(da, db);
                    let size = (da.0.hypot(da.1)) * (db.0.hypot(db.1));
                    if det.abs() <= if through { 1e-12 } else { 1e-3 } * size {
                        continue;
                    }
                    let w = sub(b0, a0);
                    let (al, be) = (cross(w, db) / det, cross(w, da) / det);
                    if !(0.0..=1.0).contains(&al) || !(0.0..=1.0).contains(&be) {
                        continue;
                    }
                    let (pa, pb) = (&reach.pts[i], &cand.pts[j]);
                    let ta = pa.0 + (reach.pts[i + 1].0 - pa.0) * al;
                    let tb = pb.0 + (cand.pts[j + 1].0 - pb.0) * be;
                    // (Not the link's own curve, met again as a candidate; nor a curve that
                    // only meets it where it starts or ends, at a joint of the two.)
                    if cand.link == link && (ta - tb).abs() < 4.0 * self.dt {
                        continue;
                    }
                    let x = pa.1 + (reach.pts[i + 1].1 - pa.1) * al;
                    let joined = |q: &P3| (x - q).norm() < 1e-6 * self.tool.size;
                    if joined(&reach.pts[0].1) || joined(&reach.pts[reach.pts.len() - 1].1) {
                        continue;
                    }
                    // Run into what the other has swept: over to the side of the other's curve
                    // its tool is on. (In lengths: the curves' directions told as the ways
                    // into the tools are.)
                    let Some(into_b) = self.inward(cand.link, pb.0, pb.2) else {
                        continue;
                    };
                    let mb = self.within(&pb.1, &into_b, about);
                    let step_a = self.within(&pa.1, &(reach.pts[i + 1].1 - pa.1), about);
                    let step_b = self.within(&pb.1, &(cand.pts[j + 1].1 - pb.1), about);
                    if !through && cross(step_b, step_a) * cross(step_b, mb) <= 0.0 {
                        continue;
                    }
                    if found.as_ref().is_some_and(|f| f.0 <= al) {
                        continue;
                    }
                    let Some(Joint::Cross { before, after, p }) =
                        self.cross_at(c, (link, pa.2, ta), (cand.link, pb.2, tb), about)
                    else {
                        continue;
                    };
                    // The other link's way on: out of what this one has swept.
                    let Some(into_a) = self.inward(link, pa.0, pa.2) else {
                        continue;
                    };
                    let ma = self.within(&pa.1, &into_a, about);
                    let along = (cand.pts[j + 1].0 - pb.0).signum();
                    let dir = if through {
                        // Not at the joint the two share; and by the curves' directions at
                        // the crossing itself.
                        let apart =
                            |t: f64, joint: f64| (t - joint).abs() > self.near_joint * self.dt;
                        if (at_start[ci] && !apart(before.1, first.0))
                            || (at_end[ci] && !apart(before.1, last.0))
                        {
                            continue;
                        }
                        let (Some(da), Some(db)) = (
                            self.heading(c, link, before, about),
                            self.heading(c, cand.link, after, about),
                        ) else {
                            continue;
                        };
                        let way = (reach.pts[i + 1].0 - pa.0).signum();
                        let da = (da.0 * way, da.1 * way);
                        if cross(db, da) * cross(db, mb) <= 0.0 {
                            continue;
                        }
                        if cross(da, db) * cross(da, ma) < 0.0 {
                            1.0
                        } else {
                            -1.0
                        }
                    } else if cross(step_a, step_b) * cross(step_a, ma) < 0.0 {
                        along
                    } else {
                        -along
                    };
                    found = Some((
                        al,
                        Crossing {
                            at: i,
                            before,
                            link: cand.link,
                            after,
                            dir,
                            p,
                        },
                    ));
                }
            }
            if let Some((_, x)) = found {
                return Some(x);
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// The chain through `seed` in slice `c`: followed each way, link by link (on to the
    /// next at a node; over to another's curve where it runs into what that has swept), to the
    /// link that leaves the target for good. None where an end stays within the target.
    /// `full`: not 0, each way is followed on past that link while more go on from it (to
    /// `full` links at most), ending with the last one that ends clear of the target: the
    /// links a chain has in another slice, where they come within the target, are found here
    /// too, outside it.
    fn chain(&self, c: f64, seed: &Node, cands: &[Cand], about: f64, full: usize) -> Option<Chain> {
        // Where the walk stands: at a node, reached by a link; or on a link it crossed over to.
        #[derive(Clone, Copy)]
        enum At {
            Node(Node, Option<Link>),
            Cross(Link, Place, f64, f64, P3),
            Corner(Corner, f64),
        }
        // The link on from there, as far as its next joint: its points, the link, and the
        // joint with where the walk stands after it.
        type Step = (Reach, Link, Option<(Joint, At)>);
        let advance = |at: &At, face_first: bool| -> Option<Step> {
            let (mut reach, link) = match at {
                At::Node(n, by) => self.next(c, n, *by, face_first)?,
                At::Cross(link, place, t, dir, _) => {
                    let r = self.march(c, *link, *place, *t, *dir, None);
                    if self.trace {
                        eprintln!("  from a crossing at t {t:.6} on: {}", self.told(*link, &r));
                    }
                    (r, *link)
                }
                At::Corner(k, dir) => {
                    let link = Link::Edge(k.after.0);
                    let r = self.march(c, link, Place::Run(k.after.1), k.t, *dir, None);
                    if self.trace {
                        eprintln!(
                            "  from vertex {} at t {:.6} on: {}",
                            k.v,
                            k.t,
                            self.told(link, &r)
                        );
                    }
                    (r, link)
                }
            };
            if reach.pts.len() < 2 {
                return None;
            }
            let far = match self.first_crossing(c, link, &reach, cands, about) {
                Some(x) => {
                    if self.trace {
                        eprintln!(
                            "    crossed by {:?} after {} points (at t {:.6}, the other's {:.6})",
                            x.link,
                            x.at + 1,
                            x.before.1,
                            x.after.1
                        );
                    }
                    reach.pts.truncate(x.at + 1);
                    reach.pts.push((x.before.1, x.p, x.before.0));
                    reach.node = None;
                    reach.corner = None;
                    Some((
                        Joint::Cross {
                            before: x.before,
                            after: x.after,
                            p: x.p,
                        },
                        At::Cross(x.link, x.after.0, x.after.1, x.dir, x.p),
                    ))
                }
                None => match (reach.node, reach.corner, link) {
                    (Some(n), ..) => Some((Joint::Node(n), At::Node(n, Some(link)))),
                    (None, Some((v, t, p, sigma)), Link::Edge(r)) => {
                        self.turn(c, v, t, r).map(|(next, at, dir)| {
                            let k = Corner {
                                v,
                                t,
                                p,
                                before: (r, sigma),
                                after: (next, at),
                            };
                            (Joint::Corner(k), At::Corner(k, dir))
                        })
                    }
                    _ => None,
                },
            };
            Some((reach, link, far))
        };
        let touches = |reach: &Reach| reach.pts.iter().any(|p| !self.clear_of_target(&p.1));
        // The link the walk takes on from where it stands.
        let link_of = |at: &At| -> Link {
            match at {
                At::Node(n, Some(Link::Face(_))) => Link::Edge(n.r),
                At::Node(n, _) => Link::Face(self.tool.runs[n.r].groups[n.side]),
                At::Cross(link, ..) => *link,
                At::Corner(k, _) => Link::Edge(k.after.0),
            }
        };
        // One way from the seed: (the joints after it, the links, the last link's way in time,
        // whether any of it met the target).
        let grow = |face_first: bool| -> Option<(Vec<Joint>, Vec<Link>, f64, bool)> {
            let (mut joints, mut links): (Vec<Joint>, Vec<Link>) = (Vec::new(), Vec::new());
            let mut at = At::Node(*seed, None);
            let mut out = 0.0;
            let mut met = false;
            // (A full walk's chain so far: to the last link that ended clear.)
            let mut kept: Option<(Vec<Joint>, Vec<Link>, f64, bool)> = None;
            loop {
                let Some((reach, link, far)) = advance(&at, face_first) else {
                    if kept.is_some() {
                        return kept;
                    }
                    // Nothing goes on from this joint: the link that reached it is the last,
                    // if the joint is clear of the target.
                    let here = match &at {
                        At::Node(n, _) => n.p,
                        At::Cross(.., p) => *p,
                        At::Corner(k, _) => k.p,
                    };
                    if joints.is_empty() || !self.clear_of_target(&here) {
                        return None;
                    }
                    joints.pop();
                    return Some((joints, links, out, met));
                };
                met |= touches(&reach);
                links.push(link);
                out = (reach.pts[reach.pts.len() - 1].0 - reach.pts[0].0).signum();
                let ends_clear = self.clear_of_target(&reach.pts[reach.pts.len() - 1].1);
                let Some((joint, then)) = far else {
                    return if ends_clear {
                        Some((joints, links, out, met))
                    } else {
                        kept
                    };
                };
                if ends_clear {
                    // Clear at its far joint: the last link, unless what goes on from there
                    // comes back to the target, or this link is clear only at its very end
                    // and the next is clear at length (a better one to cut).
                    let on = advance(&then, face_first);
                    // (What comes back to the target as a link the chain has already, the
                    // seed's two among them, is this tooth space come round to its other
                    // side, or the next one, a turn of the tool on.)
                    let seen = |l: &Link| {
                        links.contains(l)
                            || *l == Link::Edge(seed.r)
                            || *l == Link::Face(self.tool.runs[seed.r].groups[seed.side])
                    };
                    let next_space = on.as_ref().is_some_and(|(_, l, _)| seen(l));
                    let back = !next_space && on.as_ref().is_some_and(|(r, ..)| touches(r));
                    let clear_for = reach
                        .pts
                        .iter()
                        .rev()
                        .take_while(|p| self.clear_of_target(&p.1))
                        .count();
                    let short = clear_for < 3
                        && !links.contains(&link_of(&then))
                        && on.as_ref().is_some_and(|(r, ..)| r.pts.len() >= 12);
                    if !back && !short {
                        if full == 0 || next_space || on.is_none() || links.len() >= full {
                            return Some((joints, links, out, met));
                        }
                        kept = Some((joints.clone(), links.clone(), out, met));
                    }
                }
                joints.push(joint);
                at = then;
                if joints.len() > 64 {
                    return kept;
                }
            }
        };
        let (fwd_joints, fwd_links, fwd_out, met_a) = grow(true)?;
        let (back_joints, back_links, back_out, met_b) = grow(false)?;
        if !(met_a || met_b) {
            return None;
        }
        let mut joints: Vec<Joint> = back_joints.iter().rev().map(Joint::turned).collect();
        let mut links: Vec<Link> = back_links.into_iter().rev().collect();
        joints.push(Joint::Node(*seed));
        joints.extend(fwd_joints);
        links.extend(fwd_links);
        Some(Chain {
            joints,
            links,
            out: [back_out, fwd_out],
            about,
        })
    }
}

/// Whether two chains are one, or one a whole number of `period`s after the other (either way
/// round).
fn same_chain(a: &Chain, b: &Chain, period: Option<f64>, dt: f64) -> bool {
    if a.links.len() != b.links.len() {
        return false;
    }
    let matches = |bj: &[Joint], bl: &[Link]| -> bool {
        if a.links.iter().zip(bl).any(|(x, y)| x != y) {
            return false;
        }
        let k = match period {
            Some(p) => ((bj[0].t(false) - a.joints[0].t(false)) / p).round(),
            None => 0.0,
        };
        let near = |x: f64, y: f64| (y - x - k * period.unwrap_or(0.0)).abs() < 0.5 * dt;
        a.joints.iter().zip(bj).all(|(x, y)| match (x, y) {
            (Joint::Node(m), Joint::Node(n)) => m.r == n.r && m.side == n.side && near(m.t, n.t),
            (Joint::Cross { .. }, Joint::Cross { .. }) => {
                near(x.t(false), y.t(false)) && near(x.t(true), y.t(true))
            }
            (Joint::Corner(m), Joint::Corner(n)) => m.v == n.v && near(m.t, n.t),
            _ => false,
        })
    };
    let rj: Vec<Joint> = b.joints.iter().rev().map(Joint::turned).collect();
    let rl: Vec<Link> = b.links.iter().rev().copied().collect();
    matches(&b.joints, &b.links) || matches(&rj, &rl)
}

/// A chain carried across the slices from `c.0` to `c.1`.
///
/// A node's own instant is found where a contact comes to its run, and that is a poor place to
/// find: the contact's sheet and the run's are tangent there, so the least roughness of the tool
/// (a face made in pieces whose normals differ by a hundred-thousandth where they join) moves
/// it a long way, by leaps from slice to slice. But for the same reason it matters little where
/// the two sheets hand over: near the node they are one surface, as closely as the leaps are
/// small squared. So the run's sheet is taken to an instant that changes smoothly with the
/// slice (just past the node and every leap of it, where the run's stretch has ended but the
/// run is still there), and the contact's sheet to where it comes nearest the run's sheet's
/// edge there. A crossing is a plain meeting of two curves: each link is bounded at its own
/// instant there.
struct Carried {
    chain: Chain,
    c: (f64, f64),
    /// The slices of all the tooth space's stretches, this one among them.
    whole: (f64, f64),
    /// The joints themselves in some slices, in order.
    rows: Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>)>,
    /// Each joint's instant as the link before it is bounded, a curve of the slice (its x), and
    /// as the link after it is.
    before: Vec<NurbsCurve>,
    after: Vec<NurbsCurve>,
    /// Where the two end links are cut: a time before or after the first and the last joint,
    /// as a polynomial of the slice's place between `c.0` and `c.1`, signed.
    ends: [Vec<f64>; 2],
    /// For a stretch with fillers ([`Link::Fill`]): the stretch next to it that has the links
    /// in their place, and the slice the two meet in.
    fill: Option<(usize, f64)>,
    /// Or where the two end links are cut as the instants themselves, curves of the slice (a
    /// tooth space trimmed at its roof: see [`Roof`]); `ends` is unused then.
    cuts: Option<[NurbsCurve; 2]>,
}

impl Carried {
    /// Joint `j` in the row nearest slice `c`.
    fn near(&self, j: usize, c: f64) -> &Joint {
        let k = self
            .rows
            .partition_point(|r| r.0 <= c)
            .clamp(1, self.rows.len() - 1);
        let (a, z) = (&self.rows[k - 1], &self.rows[k]);
        if (c - a.0).abs() <= (z.0 - c).abs() {
            &a.1[j]
        } else {
            &z.1[j]
        }
    }

    /// The instant link `i` starts at (or, `end`, ends at) in slice `c`: a joint's, as the
    /// link is bounded there, or the chain's cut.
    fn bound(&self, i: usize, end: bool, c: f64) -> f64 {
        let k = self.chain.links.len();
        let cut = |which: usize| {
            let x = (c - self.whole.0) / (self.whole.1 - self.whole.0);
            self.ends[which]
                .iter()
                .rev()
                .fold(0.0, |acc, k| acc * x + k)
        };
        match (i, end, &self.cuts) {
            (0, false, Some(cuts)) => return cuts[0].point(c).x,
            (i, true, Some(cuts)) if i == k - 1 => return cuts[1].point(c).x,
            _ => {}
        }
        match (i, end) {
            (0, false) => self.before[0].point(c).x + cut(0),
            (i, true) if i == k - 1 => self.after[k - 2].point(c).x + cut(1),
            (i, false) => self.after[i - 1].point(c).x,
            (i, true) => self.before[i].point(c).x,
        }
    }
}

/// A polynomial of degree `deg` through (x, y) by least squares: its coefficients, lowest first.
fn poly_fit(x: &[f64], y: &[f64], deg: usize) -> Option<Vec<f64>> {
    let n = deg + 1;
    let mut a = nalgebra::DMatrix::<f64>::zeros(x.len(), n);
    for (i, xi) in x.iter().enumerate() {
        let mut p = 1.0;
        for j in 0..n {
            a[(i, j)] = p;
            p *= xi;
        }
    }
    let b = nalgebra::DVector::from_column_slice(y);
    let sol = a.svd(true, true).solve(&b, 1e-12).ok()?;
    Some(sol.iter().copied().collect())
}

/// The curve of the slice through values at slices (its x the value).
fn through(cs: &[f64], values: &[f64]) -> NurbsCurve {
    let pts: Vec<P3> = values.iter().map(|&v| P3::new(v, 0.0, 0.0)).collect();
    NurbsCurve::interpolate(&pts, cs, 5.min(cs.len() - 1), None, None)
}

impl Gen<'_> {
    /// A joint of a chain in slice `c`, from itself in a slice nearby.
    fn joint_at(&self, c: f64, chain: &Chain, j: usize, from: &Joint) -> Option<Joint> {
        match from {
            Joint::Node(m) => Some(Joint::Node(self.node(m.r, m.side, c, (m.sigma, m.t))?)),
            Joint::Cross { before, after, .. } => self.cross_at(
                c,
                (chain.links[j], before.0, before.1),
                (chain.links[j + 1], after.0, after.1),
                chain.about,
            ),
            Joint::Corner(k) => {
                let (t, p) = self.corner(k.v, c, k.t)?;
                Some(Joint::Corner(Corner { t, p, ..*k }))
            }
            Joint::Free => Some(Joint::Free),
        }
    }

    /// A joint's place and instant on one of its two links.
    fn joint_on(&self, joint: &Joint, link: Link, after: bool) -> Option<(Place, f64)> {
        match joint {
            Joint::Node(n) => Some((self.place_at(n, link)?, n.t)),
            Joint::Cross {
                before, after: a, ..
            } => Some(if after { *a } else { *before }),
            Joint::Corner(k) => {
                let (_, sigma) = if after { k.after } else { k.before };
                Some((Place::Run(sigma), k.t))
            }
            Joint::Free => None,
        }
    }

    /// Whether a row of a chain's joints keeps its links the way round they are in the chain.
    fn in_order(&self, chain: &Chain, row: &[Joint]) -> bool {
        chain.joints.windows(2).zip(row.windows(2)).all(|(c, w)| {
            let way = (c[1].t(false) - c[0].t(true)).signum();
            // (Under a roof a link is carried to where it comes to nothing, as nearly as its
            // sheet's side there is to be a point.)
            (w[1].t(false) - w[0].t(true)) * way
                > if self.near_joint < 1.0 { 1e-9 } else { 1e-6 } * self.dt
        }) && row
            .iter()
            .all(|m| self.in_span(m.t(false)) && self.in_span(m.t(true)))
    }

    /// A chain's joints in slice `c`, from themselves in a slice nearby.
    fn row_at(&self, chain: &Chain, c: f64, from: &[Joint]) -> Option<Vec<Joint>> {
        let row: Option<Vec<Joint>> = from
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
            .map(|(j, m)| self.joint_at(c, chain, j, m))
            .collect();
        row.filter(|r| self.in_order(chain, r))
    }

    /// A chain's joints in slice `c`, from themselves in the slice `c0`: at once, or by way of
    /// slices between (a joint may move far along its links for a little of the slice: a
    /// crossing of two curves that run nearly along one another).
    fn row_from(&self, chain: &Chain, c: f64, (c0, from): (f64, &[Joint])) -> Option<Vec<Joint>> {
        if let Some(row) = self.row_at(chain, c, from) {
            return Some(row);
        }
        for steps in [2, 4, 8, 16, 32] {
            let mut row = from.to_vec();
            let all = (1..=steps).all(|i| {
                let ci = c0 + (c - c0) * i as f64 / steps as f64;
                match self.row_at(chain, ci, &row) {
                    Some(r) => {
                        row = r;
                        true
                    }
                    None => false,
                }
            });
            if all {
                return Some(row);
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// The chain found in slice `from`, carried to the slices from `lo` to `hi` or as far each
    /// way as its joints can be followed with their links the same way round: its joints in
    /// those slices, in order.
    fn rows(&self, chain: &Chain, from: f64, (lo, hi): (f64, f64)) -> Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>)> {
        let step = (hi - lo) / 48.0;
        // Each way from the start, the step halved where a slice can't be reached (to a
        // millionth of the way across, where the chain ends: a crossing closing to a touch).
        let mut rows: Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>)> = vec![(from, chain.joints.clone())];
        for (dir, end) in [(1.0, hi), (-1.0, lo)] {
            let (mut c, mut row, mut h) = (from, chain.joints.clone(), step);
            while (end - c) * dir > 1e-9 * step {
                let cn = if (end - c) * dir <= h {
                    end
                } else {
                    c + dir * h
                };
                match self.row_at(chain, cn, &row) {
                    Some(r) => {
                        (c, row) = (cn, r);
                        rows.push((c, row.clone()));
                        h = (h * 2.0).min(step);
                    }
                    None => {
                        h *= 0.5;
                        if h < 1e-6 * (hi - lo) {
                            if self.trace {
                                // Which joint can't be followed on.
                                let tried: Vec<Option<Joint>> = row
                                    .iter()
                                    .enumerate()
                                    .map(|(j, m)| self.joint_at(cn, chain, j, m))
                                    .collect();
                                eprintln!(
                                    "  carried no farther than slice {c:.6} (toward {end:.4}): beyond it joints found {:?}",
                                    tried
                                        .iter()
                                        .map(|j| j.map(|j| (
                                            (j.t(false) * 1e5).round() / 1e5,
                                            (j.t(true) * 1e5).round() / 1e5
                                        )))
                                        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                                );
                            }
                            break;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        rows.sort_by(|a, b| a.0.total_cmp(&b.0));
        rows
    }

    /// A stretch's joints bound for its sheets: each joint's instant as the link before it is
    /// bounded and as the link after it is, curves of the slice, with the rows they were
    /// found in.
    #[allow(clippy::type_complexity)]
    fn bind(
        &self,
        span: &Span,
        pinch: &[Vec<usize>; 2],
    ) -> Option<(Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>)>, Vec<NurbsCurve>, Vec<NurbsCurve>)> {
        use rayon::prelude::*;
        let chain = &span.chain;
        let rows = &span.rows;
        let n = chain.joints.len();
        let at = |c: f64, from: (f64, &[Joint])| self.row_from(chain, c, from);
        if rows.len() < 6 {
            return None;
        }
        if self.trace {
            for (c, row) in rows.iter().step_by((rows.len() / 8).max(1)) {
                eprintln!(
                    "  slice {c:.4}: joints at t {:?}",
                    row.iter()
                        .map(|m| (
                            (m.t(false) * 1e6).round() / 1e6,
                            (m.t(true) * 1e6).round() / 1e6
                        ))
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                );
            }
        }
        // Which way in time each node's two links run from it: its run's stretch, and its
        // contact. (They run the same way where a contact comes to its run as the run's stretch
        // ends: on the one side of that instant there are both, on the other neither; and
        // opposite ways where the stretch starts as the contact leaves.)
        let mut run_way = vec![0.0; n];
        let mut contact_way = vec![0.0; n];
        for j in 0..n {
            let Joint::Node(m) = &chain.joints[j] else {
                continue;
            };
            let face_before = matches!(chain.links[j], Link::Face(_));
            if face_before == matches!(chain.links[j + 1], Link::Face(_)) {
                return None;
            }
            let before = if j == 0 {
                chain.out[0]
            } else {
                (chain.joints[j - 1].t(true) - m.t).signum()
            };
            let after = if j == n - 1 {
                chain.out[1]
            } else {
                (chain.joints[j + 1].t(false) - m.t).signum()
            };
            (contact_way[j], run_way[j]) = if face_before {
                (before, after)
            } else {
                (after, before)
            };
        }
        // The runs' sheets' bounds at the nodes: a curve through each node's instants in some
        // of the slices (in more of them while that brings it closer to the rest: as close as
        // the tool's roughness lets a node's instants lie on any curve), moved past them all.
        let cs: Vec<f64> = rows.iter().map(|r| r.0).collect();
        let edge_side: Vec<Option<NurbsCurve>> = (0..n)
            .map(|j| {
                let Joint::Node(_) = &chain.joints[j] else {
                    return None;
                };
                let ts: Vec<f64> = rows.iter().map(|r| r.1[j].t(false)).collect();
                let through_some = |stride: usize| -> (NurbsCurve, f64) {
                    let mut pick: Vec<usize> = (0..rows.len()).step_by(stride).collect();
                    if *pick.last().unwrap() != rows.len() - 1 {
                        pick.push(rows.len() - 1);
                    }
                    let curve = through(
                        &pick.iter().map(|&i| cs[i]).collect::<Vec<_>>(),
                        &pick.iter().map(|&i| ts[i]).collect::<Vec<_>>(),
                    );
                    let leap = (0..rows.len())
                        .map(|i| (curve.point(cs[i]).x - ts[i]).abs())
                        .fold(0.0, f64::max);
                    (curve, leap)
                };
                let mut stride = (rows.len() / 12).max(1);
                let (mut smooth, mut leap) = through_some(stride);
                while stride > 2 && leap > 1e-6 * self.dt {
                    let (finer, less) = through_some(stride / 2);
                    if less > 0.7 * leap {
                        break;
                    }
                    (smooth, leap, stride) = (finer, less, stride / 2);
                }
                // (Past the node on the side its stretch isn't: the run is there all the
                // same.)
                // (Under a roof, a node found to a hair is bounded where it is: a run that comes
                // to nothing at a vertex of the tool, where its stretch ends, must do so there.)
                let past = if self.near_joint < 1.0 && leap < 1e-9 * self.dt {
                    0.0
                } else {
                    1e-6 * self.dt
                };
                let shift = -run_way[j] * (1.5 * leap + past);
                if self.trace {
                    eprintln!(
                        "  node {j}: its instants leap by up to {:.2e} of a step; its run's sheet bounded {:.2e} of a step past them",
                        leap / self.dt,
                        shift / self.dt
                    );
                }
                let knots: Vec<f64> = (0..rows.len()).step_by(stride.max(1)).map(|i| cs[i]).chain([cs[rows.len() - 1]]).collect();
                let mut knots = knots;
                knots.dedup();
                let moved: Vec<f64> = knots.iter().map(|&c| smooth.point(c).x + shift).collect();
                Some(through(&knots, &moved))
            })
            .collect();
        // Each joint's two bounds in a slice, the link before's and the link after's, with the
        // speed (within the slice) of what moves there: at a node the run's bound from its
        // curve and the contact's where it comes nearest the run's sheet's edge; at a crossing
        // each link's own instant.
        type Bounds = Vec<(f64, f64, f64)>;
        let bound_of = |c: f64, row: &[Joint], j: usize| -> Option<(f64, f64, f64)> {
            Some(j).and_then(|j| match &row[j] {
                    Joint::Node(m) => {
                        let te = edge_side[j].as_ref()?.point(c).x;
                        let why = |what: &str, t: f64| {
                            if self.trace {
                                eprintln!(
                                    "    slice {c:.6}: node {j} (t {:.9}, σ {:.6}): {what} (t {t:.9}; its run bounded at {te:.9})",
                                    m.t, m.sigma
                                );
                            }
                        };
                        let Some(sigma) = self.run_in_slice(m.r, te, c, m.sigma) else {
                            why("its run isn't in the slice where it is bounded", te);
                            return None;
                        };
                        let edge = self.world(te, &self.tool.on_run(m.r, sigma)?.2);
                        let link = Link::Face(self.tool.runs[m.r].groups[m.side]);
                        let start = self.place_at(m, link)?;
                        let contact = |t: f64| -> Option<P3> {
                            self.at_place(link, t, self.place(link, t, c, start)?)
                        };
                        // (From as far along the contact from the node as the run's bound is
                        // from it.)
                        let eta = contact_way[j] * 0.25 * (te - m.t).abs().max(1e-4 * self.dt);
                        // (A node found to a hair, its run bounded a hair past it: the contact
                        // is bounded at the node's own instant, which goes smoothly with the
                        // slice whatever the contact does beside it, where its point nearest
                        // the run's edge may leap as the contact turns back on itself.)
                        if self.near_joint < 1.0 && (te - m.t).abs() < 1e-4 * self.dt {
                            let speed = match (contact(m.t), contact(m.t + eta)) {
                                (Some(x), Some(ahead)) => ((ahead - x) / eta).norm(),
                                _ => self.speed,
                            };
                            return Some(if matches!(chain.links[j], Link::Face(_)) {
                                (m.t, te, speed)
                            } else {
                                (te, m.t, speed)
                            });
                        }
                        let mut t = m.t + contact_way[j] * (te - m.t).abs();
                        let mut speed = 0.0;
                        for _ in 0..24 {
                            let (Some(x), Some(ahead)) = (contact(t), contact(t + eta)) else {
                                why("its contact isn't followed", t);
                                return None;
                            };
                            let v = (ahead - x) / eta;
                            speed = v.norm();
                            if speed < 1e-300 {
                                return None;
                            }
                            let dtt = (edge - x).dot(&v) / (speed * speed);
                            t += dtt;
                            if dtt.abs() < 1e-9 * self.dt {
                                break;
                            }
                        }

                        Some(if matches!(chain.links[j], Link::Face(_)) {
                            (t, te, speed)
                        } else {
                            (te, t, speed)
                        })
                    }
                    Joint::Cross { before, after, .. } => {
                        let speed_of = |link: Link, (place, t): (Place, f64)| -> Option<f64> {
                            let eta = 1e-2 * self.dt;
                            let a = self.at_place(link, t, self.place(link, t, c, place)?)?;
                            let b = self
                                .at_place(link, t + eta, self.place(link, t + eta, c, place)?)
                                .or_else(|| {
                                    self.at_place(
                                        link,
                                        t - eta,
                                        self.place(link, t - eta, c, place)?,
                                    )
                                })?;
                            Some((b - a).norm() / eta)
                        };
                        // (Under a roof a crossing may be at the very end of a run, at a
                        // vertex of the tool, where a stretch starts or ends: the tool's own
                        // speed stands in where the link's isn't to be had.)
                        let or_tool = |v: Option<f64>| {
                            if self.near_joint < 1.0 {
                                Some(v.unwrap_or(self.speed))
                            } else {
                                v
                            }
                        };
                        let speed = or_tool(speed_of(chain.links[j], *before))?
                            .max(or_tool(speed_of(chain.links[j + 1], *after))?);
                        Some((before.1, after.1, speed))
                    }
                    Joint::Corner(k) => {
                        let eta = 1e-2 * self.dt;
                        let q = self.tool.b.verts[k.v].p;
                        let speed = (self.world(k.t + eta, &q) - k.p).norm() / eta;
                        Some((k.t, k.t, speed))
                    }
                    Joint::Free => None,
            })
        };
        let bounds_at = |c: f64, row: &[Joint]| -> Option<Bounds> {
            (0..n)
                .map(|j| {
                    let bound = bound_of(c, row, j);
                    if bound.is_none() && self.trace {
                        eprintln!(
                            "    slice {c:.6}: joint {j} ({}) has no bounds",
                            row[j].told()
                        );
                    }
                    bound
                })
                .collect()
        };
        let bounds: Option<Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>, Bounds)>> = rows
            .par_iter()
            .map(|(c, row)| bounds_at(*c, row).map(|b| (*c, row.clone(), b)))
            .collect();
        if bounds.is_none() && self.trace {
            for (c, row) in rows {
                if bounds_at(*c, row).is_none() {
                    eprintln!(
                        "  no bounds in slice {c:.5}: joints at t {:?}",
                        row.iter()
                            .map(|m| (m.t(false), m.t(true)))
                            .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                    );
                }
            }
        }
        let mut bounds = bounds?;
        // A link that comes to nothing in the stretch's first slice or its last (`pinch`: it
        // is no part of the stretch beyond) is bounded there at one instant from both sides, so
        // that its sheet's side is a point: the instant of its joint that isn't a node (found
        // exactly), where it has one.
        for (end, links) in pinch.iter().enumerate() {
            let at = if end == 0 { 0 } else { bounds.len() - 1 };
            for &l in links {
                let (a, z) = (bounds[at].2[l - 1].1, bounds[at].2[l].0);
                let exact = |j: usize| !matches!(chain.joints[j], Joint::Node(_));
                let t = match (exact(l - 1), exact(l)) {
                    (true, false) => a,
                    (false, true) => z,
                    _ => 0.5 * (a + z),
                };
                bounds[at].2[l - 1].1 = t;
                bounds[at].2[l].0 = t;
            }
        }
        // (A bound's instant as closely as moves its link's point a small share of a sheet's
        // fit.)
        let fine: Vec<f64> = (0..n)
            .map(|j| {
                let speed = bounds.iter().map(|b| b.2[j].2).fold(0.0, f64::max);
                0.05 * SHEET_FIT * self.tool.size / speed.max(1e-300)
            })
            .collect();
        let mut fitted: Option<(Vec<NurbsCurve>, Vec<NurbsCurve>)> = None;
        for _ in 0..12 {
            let cs: Vec<f64> = bounds.iter().map(|b| b.0).collect();
            let before: Vec<NurbsCurve> = (0..n)
                .map(|j| through(&cs, &bounds.iter().map(|b| b.2[j].0).collect::<Vec<_>>()))
                .collect();
            let after: Vec<NurbsCurve> = (0..n)
                .map(|j| through(&cs, &bounds.iter().map(|b| b.2[j].1).collect::<Vec<_>>()))
                .collect();
            let mids: Vec<Option<(f64, Vec<Joint>, Bounds)>> = bounds
                .par_windows(2)
                .map(|w| {
                    let cm = 0.5 * (w[0].0 + w[1].0);
                    // (From the slice before, or the one after: a stretch's first row may
                    // have a link of no length, a poor place to start from.)
                    let row = at(cm, (w[0].0, &w[0].1)).or_else(|| at(cm, (w[1].0, &w[1].1)))?;
                    let b = bounds_at(cm, &row)?;
                    Some((cm, row, b))
                })
                .collect();
            if self.trace {
                for (w, m) in bounds.windows(2).zip(&mids) {
                    if m.is_none() {
                        let cm = 0.5 * (w[0].0 + w[1].0);
                        let row = at(cm, (w[0].0, &w[0].1));
                        eprintln!(
                            "  no bounds midway in slice {cm:.5}: {}; each joint from the slice before: {:?}",
                            if row.is_some() {
                                "its joints found"
                            } else {
                                "its joints not found"
                            },
                            w[0].1
                                .iter()
                                .enumerate()
                                .map(|(j, m)| self
                                    .joint_at(cm, chain, j, m)
                                    .map(|j| (j.t(false), j.t(true))))
                                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                        );
                    }
                }
            }
            let mids: Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>, Bounds)> = mids.into_iter().collect::<Option<_>>()?;
            // (How far off, in shares of what is fine.)
            let off = |m: &(f64, Vec<Joint>, Bounds)| -> f64 {
                (0..n)
                    .map(|j| {
                        // Under a roof a crossing is judged by what its bounds are for: the
                        // two links' points at their bounds must be one point (how far apart
                        // they are, against a sheet's fit). Where two curves cross at the
                        // least of angles the crossing's instants are found only as closely as
                        // the curves part, far short of what is fine, yet the two points slide
                        // along them together.
                        if self.near_joint < 1.0
                            && let Joint::Cross {
                                before: (pb, _),
                                after: (pa, _),
                                ..
                            } = &m.1[j]
                        {
                            let at = |link: Link, t: f64, near: Place| {
                                self.at_place(link, t, self.place(link, t, m.0, near)?)
                            };
                            return match (
                                at(chain.links[j], before[j].point(m.0).x, *pb),
                                at(chain.links[j + 1], after[j].point(m.0).x, *pa),
                            ) {
                                (Some(x), Some(y)) => {
                                    (x - y).norm() / (0.25 * SHEET_FIT * self.tool.size)
                                }
                                _ => 1e9,
                            };
                        }
                        (before[j].point(m.0).x - m.2[j].0)
                            .abs()
                            .max((after[j].point(m.0).x - m.2[j].1).abs())
                            / fine[j]
                    })
                    .fold(0.0, f64::max)
            };
            let worst = mids.iter().map(&off).fold(0.0, f64::max);
            if self.trace {
                // (Which joint's, and where.)
                let at = mids
                    .iter()
                    .flat_map(|m| {
                        (0..n).map(|j| {
                            let off = (before[j].point(m.0).x - m.2[j].0)
                                .abs()
                                .max((after[j].point(m.0).x - m.2[j].1).abs())
                                / fine[j];
                            (off, j, m.0)
                        })
                    })
                    .max_by(|a, b| a.0.total_cmp(&b.0));
                eprintln!(
                    "  {} slices: the bounds are off by {:.2} of what is fine{}",
                    bounds.len(),
                    worst,
                    at.map_or(String::new(), |(_, j, c)| format!(
                        ": joint {j} in slice {c:.6}"
                    ))
                );
            }
            // (Under a roof: a crossing just born at its node, the two curves all but tangent
            // there, is found along them only as closely as they part; its bounds are taken
            // as they are once the slices are many.)
            let born = self.near_joint < 1.0 && bounds.len() > 300 && worst < 5e4;
            // (A link bounded at one instant where it comes to nothing is a few times what is
            // fine from where it was carried to: no more slices bring that closer.)
            let pinched = pinch.iter().any(|p| !p.is_empty()) && worst <= 4.0;
            if worst <= 1.0 || (bounds.len() > 1200 && worst < 20.0) || born || pinched {
                fitted = Some((before, after));
                break;
            }
            if bounds.len() > 1200 {
                if self.debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: a link's bound won't settle across the slices (off by {worst:.1} of what is fine)"
                    );
                }
                return None;
            }
            bounds.extend(mids.into_iter().filter(|m| off(m) > 1.0));
            bounds.sort_by(|a, b| a.0.total_cmp(&b.0));
        }
        let (before, after) = fitted?;
        let rows: Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>)> = bounds.into_iter().map(|b| (b.0, b.1)).collect();
        Some((rows, before, after))
    }

    /// Where the chain's two end links are cut, the same in every stretch: a time before or
    /// after the first and the last joint, as a polynomial of the slice's place across all the
    /// stretches, signed. In each of some slices the link is followed from its joint: the cut
    /// comes soon after it is `past` clear of the target for good (as it is in the nearest of
    /// the target's own slices, `inner`, for a slice beyond them, where it is clear from the
    /// start) and before it ends.
    fn cuts(&self, spans: &[Span], past: f64, inner: (f64, f64)) -> Option<[Vec<f64>; 2]> {
        let whole = (spans[0].c.0, spans[spans.len() - 1].c.1);
        // (The stretches that have this end's link: one without it is closed there by a
        // filler.)
        let of = |end: usize| {
            let real: Vec<&Span> = spans.iter().filter(|s| s.skip[end] == 0).collect();
            self.cut_of(&real, end, whole, past, inner)
        };
        Some([of(0)?, of(1)?])
    }

    /// Where the stretches `real` (which go on from one another) cut the link at their chains'
    /// end `end`: see [`Gen::cuts`]. `(c0, c1)`: all the tooth space's slices.
    fn cut_of(
        &self,
        real: &[&Span],
        end: usize,
        (c0, c1): (f64, f64),
        past: f64,
        inner: (f64, f64),
    ) -> Option<Vec<f64>> {
        use rayon::prelude::*;
        let samples = 96;
        {
            let (r0, r1) = (real.first()?.c.0, real.last()?.c.1);
            let of = |c: f64| -> &Span {
                real.iter()
                    .find(|s| c <= s.c.1)
                    .unwrap_or(&real[real.len() - 1])
            };
            let dir = real[0].chain.out[end];
            // The link followed in slice `c`: its points' instants past the joint and how far
            // each is from the target.
            let followed = |c: f64| -> Option<Vec<(f64, f64)>> {
                let span = of(c);
                let (chain, rows) = (&span.chain, &span.rows);
                // (This end's joint and link, as this stretch counts them.)
                let (ji, link) = if end == 0 {
                    (0, chain.links[0])
                } else {
                    (chain.joints.len() - 1, chain.links[chain.links.len() - 1])
                };
                let i = rows.partition_point(|r| r.0 <= c).clamp(1, rows.len()) - 1;
                let joint = self.row_from(chain, c, (rows[i].0, &rows[i].1))?[ji];
                let (place, t0) = self.joint_on(&joint, link, end == 1)?;
                let reach = match &joint {
                    Joint::Node(m) => self.follow(c, m, link)?,
                    Joint::Cross { .. } | Joint::Corner(_) => {
                        self.march(c, link, place, t0, dir, None)
                    }
                    Joint::Free => return None,
                };
                let last = reach.pts.last()?.0;
                if reach.pts.len() < 2 || (last - t0).signum() != dir {
                    if self.trace {
                        eprintln!("  end {end} in slice {c:.4}: {}", self.told(link, &reach));
                    }
                    return None;
                }
                Some(
                    reach
                        .pts
                        .iter()
                        .map(|p| ((p.0 - t0).abs(), self.target.distance(&p.1)))
                        .collect(),
                )
            };
            // (How long until clear, how long it goes on.)
            let spans_at: Vec<Option<(f64, f64)>> = (0..=samples)
                .into_par_iter()
                .map(|s| {
                    let c = r0 + (r1 - r0) * s as f64 / samples as f64;
                    let here = followed(c)?;
                    let most = here[here.len() - 1].0;
                    let within = (inner.0.max(r0), inner.1.min(r1));
                    let near = if within.0 <= within.1 {
                        c.clamp(within.0, within.1)
                    } else {
                        c
                    };
                    let there = if near == c { None } else { Some(followed(near)?) };
                    let judged = there.as_ref().unwrap_or(&here);
                    let within = judged.iter().rposition(|p| p.1 < past).unwrap_or(0);
                    if within + 1 >= judged.len() {
                        if self.trace {
                            eprintln!(
                                "  end {end} in slice {near:.4}: never {past:.4} clear of the target (at its end {:.4})",
                                judged[judged.len() - 1].1
                            );
                        }
                        return None;
                    }
                    Some((judged[within + 1].0, most))
                })
                .collect();
            let spans_at: Option<Vec<(f64, f64)>> = spans_at.into_iter().collect();
            let Some(spans_at) = spans_at else {
                if self.debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: an end link doesn't come {past:.4} clear of the target in every slice"
                    );
                }
                return None;
            };
            let least = spans_at.iter().map(|s| s.0).fold(0.0, f64::max);
            let most = spans_at.iter().map(|s| s.1).fold(f64::INFINITY, f64::min);
            if self.trace && std::env::var_os("CADRS_GEN_ENDS").is_some() {
                for (j, s) in spans_at.iter().enumerate().step_by(4) {
                    eprintln!(
                        "  end {end} slice {:.4}: clear after {:.1} steps, goes on {:.1}",
                        r0 + (r1 - r0) * j as f64 / samples as f64,
                        s.0 / self.dt,
                        s.1 / self.dt
                    );
                }
            }
            if self.trace {
                eprintln!(
                    "  end {end}: clear after {:.1} to {:.1} steps, goes on at least {:.1}",
                    spans_at.iter().map(|s| s.0).fold(f64::INFINITY, f64::min) / self.dt,
                    least / self.dt,
                    most / self.dt
                );
            }
            // A curve of the slice a few steps past where the link is clear, as near it as a
            // polynomial follows (a plug that goes no farther out than it must keeps clear of
            // the next tooth space's), and before the link ends.
            // (The polynomial's variable: the slice's place across all the stretches.)
            let xs: Vec<f64> = (0..=samples)
                .map(|j| (r0 + (r1 - r0) * j as f64 / samples as f64 - c0) / (c1 - c0))
                .collect();
            // (Three steps past, or a third of the way to its end where that is nearer.)
            let wanted: Vec<f64> = spans_at
                .iter()
                .map(|s| s.0 + (3.0 * self.dt).min((s.1 - s.0) / 3.0))
                .collect();
            let fits = |co: &[f64]| {
                xs.iter().zip(&spans_at).all(|(x, s)| {
                    let y = co.iter().rev().fold(0.0, |acc, k| acc * x + k);
                    let room = s.1 - s.0;
                    y >= s.0 + (0.5 * self.dt).min(0.1 * room)
                        && y <= s.1 - (2.0 * self.dt).min(0.2 * room)
                })
            };
            // (A polynomial by least squares runs under some of its points: lifted until it is
            // over them all.)
            let fit = (0..=6).find_map(|deg| {
                let mut co = poly_fit(&xs, &wanted, deg)?;
                let short = xs
                    .iter()
                    .zip(&wanted)
                    .map(|(x, w)| w - co.iter().rev().fold(0.0, |acc, k| acc * x + k))
                    .fold(0.0, f64::max);
                co[0] += short;
                fits(&co).then_some(co)
            });
            // Or, where the link ends soon after it is clear (too soon for a curve that keeps
            // by where it clears, which may turn sharply where the link's joint comes into the
            // target): a curve a little before its end, lowered until it is before it all
            // along.
            let fit = fit.or_else(|| {
                let latest: Vec<f64> = spans_at
                    .iter()
                    .map(|s| {
                        let room = s.1 - s.0;
                        s.1 - (2.0 * self.dt).min(0.2 * room) - (0.5 * self.dt).min(0.1 * room)
                    })
                    .collect();
                (0..=6).find_map(|deg| {
                    let mut co = poly_fit(&xs, &latest, deg)?;
                    let over = xs
                        .iter()
                        .zip(&latest)
                        .map(|(x, w)| co.iter().rev().fold(0.0, |acc, k| acc * x + k) - w)
                        .fold(0.0, f64::max);
                    co[0] -= over;
                    fits(&co).then_some(co)
                })
            });
            let Some(co) = fit else {
                if self.debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: an end link stops before it is {past:.4} clear of the target"
                    );
                }
                return None;
            };
            Some(co.into_iter().map(|k| k * dir).collect())
        }
    }
}

/// A stretch of a tooth space along its length, across which its chain's joints stay what they
/// are (a node a node, a crossing a crossing): the chain as found in one of its slices, and its
/// joints in some of them, in order, from `c.0` to `c.1`.
struct Span {
    chain: Chain,
    rows: Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>)>,
    c: (f64, f64),
    /// How many links the tooth space's chain has before this stretch's first and after its
    /// last, in the stretches where it has the most: links that are outside the target all
    /// along this stretch (the chain found here ends before them), where the plug is closed by
    /// fillers in their place.
    skip: [usize; 2],
}

/// A link's sheet: its points over (slice, share of the way from its first bound to its
/// second).
struct Sheet<'a> {
    g: &'a Gen<'a>,
    carried: &'a Carried,
    /// The link's place in the chain.
    i: usize,
    link: Link,
    /// Places over a grid of (slice, share), each to start the search for a point near it from.
    grid: Vec<Vec<Place>>,
    /// The grid's shares.
    shares: usize,
    missed: AtomicUsize,
}

/// A sheet's grid: how many slices.
const GRID: usize = 96;

impl<'a> Sheet<'a> {
    fn new(g: &'a Gen<'a>, carried: &'a Carried, i: usize) -> Option<Self> {
        use rayon::prelude::*;
        let chain = &carried.chain;
        let link = chain.links[i];
        let k = chain.links.len();
        // The joint the grid's rows start from: the link's first, or for the chain's first link
        // (which starts at a cut) its second.
        let (ji, backward) = if i == 0 || matches!(chain.joints[i - 1], Joint::Free) {
            (i, true)
        } else {
            (i - 1, false)
        };
        let mid = 0.5 * (carried.c.0 + carried.c.1);
        let long = (carried.bound(i, true, mid) - carried.bound(i, false, mid)).abs();
        // (Shares close enough that each point starts the next: a few steps apart.)
        let shares = (((long / g.dt) / 3.0).ceil() as usize).clamp(8, 4096);
        let rows: Vec<Option<Vec<Place>>> = (0..=GRID)
            .into_par_iter()
            .map(|ci| {
                let c = carried.c.0 + (carried.c.1 - carried.c.0) * ci as f64 / GRID as f64;
                let (ta, tb) = (carried.bound(i, false, c), carried.bound(i, true, c));
                let (from, to) = if backward { (tb, ta) } else { (ta, tb) };
                // (The joint itself in this slice, for the place to start from.)
                let why = |what: &str| {
                    if g.trace {
                        eprintln!(
                            "  sheet {i} {link:?} in slice {c:.5} (t {from:.6} to {to:.6}): {what}"
                        );
                    }
                };
                let joint = g
                    .joint_at(c, chain, ji, carried.near(ji, c))
                    .or_else(|| g.joint_from(carried, ji, c));
                let Some(joint) = joint else {
                    why("its joint isn't found");
                    return None;
                };
                let (start, _) = g.joint_on(&joint, link, !backward)?;
                let Some(mut on) = g.place(link, from, c, start) else {
                    why("no place where it starts");
                    return None;
                };
                let mut row = vec![on];
                let mut last = from;
                for li in 1..=shares {
                    let t = from + (to - from) * li as f64 / shares as f64;
                    let Some(next) = g.place_on(link, (last, t), c, on) else {
                        why(&format!("no place at t {t:.6}"));
                        return None;
                    };
                    (on, last) = (next, t);
                    row.push(on);
                }
                // An end link's cut must fall on the link itself (a contact still within its
                // faces there), not past where it ends.
                // (A roofed stretch's cuts are found on the links themselves: at the slice a
                // stretch starts in, one may be at the very end of its link.)
                if (i == 0 || i + 1 == k)
                    && carried.cuts.is_none()
                    && let Place::Face(f, uv) = on
                    && g.group_in_slice(to, c, (f, uv)).is_none()
                {
                    why("its cut is past where it ends");
                    if g.trace {
                        let reach = g.march(c, link, start, from, (to - from).signum(), None);
                        eprintln!(
                            "    followed from its joint: {}; its last instants {:?}",
                            g.told(link, &reach),
                            reach
                                .pts
                                .iter()
                                .rev()
                                .take(3)
                                .map(|p| p.0)
                                .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                        );
                    }
                    return None;
                }
                if backward {
                    row.reverse();
                }
                Some(row)
            })
            .collect();
        Some(Sheet {
            g,
            carried,
            i,
            link,
            grid: rows.into_iter().collect::<Option<Vec<_>>>()?,
            shares,
            missed: AtomicUsize::new(0),
        })
    }

    /// The instant and the place of the sheet's point at (slice, share).
    fn on(&self, c: f64, share: f64) -> (f64, Place) {
        let g = self.g;
        let (ta, tb) = (
            self.carried.bound(self.i, false, c),
            self.carried.bound(self.i, true, c),
        );
        let t = ta + (tb - ta) * share;
        // The place to start from: between the grid's four about it where they are of one
        // kind (one run, or one face), else the nearest.
        let x = ((c - self.carried.c.0) / (self.carried.c.1 - self.carried.c.0) * GRID as f64)
            .clamp(0.0, GRID as f64);
        let y = (share * self.shares as f64).clamp(0.0, self.shares as f64);
        let (i, j) = (
            (x.floor() as usize).min(GRID - 1),
            (y.floor() as usize).min(self.shares - 1),
        );
        let (fx, fy) = (x - i as f64, y - j as f64);
        let corners = [
            (self.grid[i][j], (1.0 - fx) * (1.0 - fy)),
            (self.grid[i + 1][j], fx * (1.0 - fy)),
            (self.grid[i][j + 1], (1.0 - fx) * fy),
            (self.grid[i + 1][j + 1], fx * fy),
        ];
        let nearest = corners
            .iter()
            .max_by(|a, b| a.1.total_cmp(&b.1))
            .expect("four corners")
            .0;
        let guess = match nearest {
            Place::Run(_) => Place::Run(
                corners
                    .iter()
                    .map(|(p, w)| match p {
                        Place::Run(s) => s * w,
                        Place::Face(..) => 0.0,
                    })
                    .sum(),
            ),
            Place::Face(f, _) => {
                if corners
                    .iter()
                    .all(|(p, _)| matches!(p, Place::Face(g, _) if *g == f))
                {
                    let mut uv = V2::zeros();
                    for (p, w) in &corners {
                        if let Place::Face(_, q) = p {
                            uv += q.coords * *w;
                        }
                    }
                    Place::Face(f, P2::from(uv))
                } else {
                    nearest
                }
            }
        };
        let on = g.place(self.link, t, c, guess).unwrap_or_else(|| {
            self.missed.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
            guess
        });
        (t, on)
    }

    fn point(&self, c: f64, share: f64) -> P3 {
        let (t, on) = self.on(c, share);
        self.g.at_place(self.link, t, on).unwrap_or_else(|| {
            self.missed.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
            P3::origin()
        })
    }
}

impl Gen<'_> {
    /// Joint `j` of a carried chain in slice `c`, by way of slices between its nearest row's
    /// and that one.
    fn joint_from(&self, carried: &Carried, j: usize, c: f64) -> Option<Joint> {
        let k = carried
            .rows
            .partition_point(|r| r.0 <= c)
            .clamp(1, carried.rows.len() - 1);
        let (a, z) = (&carried.rows[k - 1], &carried.rows[k]);
        let from = if (c - a.0).abs() <= (z.0 - c).abs() {
            a
        } else {
            z
        };
        for steps in [4, 16, 64] {
            let mut joint = from.1[j];
            let all = (1..=steps).all(|i| {
                let ci = from.0 + (c - from.0) * i as f64 / steps as f64;
                match self.joint_at(ci, &carried.chain, j, &joint) {
                    Some(next) => {
                        joint = next;
                        true
                    }
                    None => false,
                }
            });
            if all {
                return Some(joint);
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// A link's place in slice `c` at t, from one near it.
    fn place(&self, link: Link, t: f64, c: f64, near: Place) -> Option<Place> {
        match (link, near) {
            (Link::Edge(r), Place::Run(sigma)) => {
                Some(Place::Run(self.run_in_slice(r, t, c, sigma)?))
            }
            (Link::Face(_), Place::Face(f, uv)) => {
                // (At a link's end the contact is at the group's edge: a point a hair outside
                // is taken too.)
                let (f, uv) = self
                    .group_in_slice(t, c, (f, uv))
                    .or_else(|| Some((f, self.face_in_slice(f, t, c, uv)?)))?;
                Some(Place::Face(f, uv))
            }
            _ => None,
        }
    }

    /// A link's place in slice `c` at `t.1`, from its place `near` at `t.0`: at once, or (where
    /// a contact's point found so is off its faces: it may move far over them in a little
    /// time) by way of the instants between.
    fn place_on(&self, link: Link, t: (f64, f64), c: f64, near: Place) -> Option<Place> {
        let within = |p: &Place| match p {
            Place::Face(f, uv) => self.tool.inside(*f, *uv),
            Place::Run(_) => true,
        };
        let direct = self.place(link, t.1, c, near);
        if direct.as_ref().is_some_and(within) {
            return direct;
        }
        for steps in [4, 16] {
            let mut on = near;
            let all = (1..=steps).all(|i| {
                let ti = t.0 + (t.1 - t.0) * i as f64 / steps as f64;
                match self.place(link, ti, c, on) {
                    Some(p) => {
                        on = p;
                        true
                    }
                    None => false,
                }
            });
            if all && within(&on) {
                return Some(on);
            }
        }
        // (A hair past the link's end, as [`Gen::place`] takes it.)
        direct
    }

    /// Whether the tool passes over `x` (a point of the target's frame) at some instant: by
    /// more than `deep` into it, by its mesh. (A check of the sheets, not what they are made
    /// from.)
    fn swept(&self, x: &P3, deep: f64) -> bool {
        let (a, z) = self.span.unwrap_or((0.0, 1.0));
        // (In steps over which the tool moves less than `deep`.)
        let n = (((z - a) * self.speed / (0.5 * deep)).ceil() as usize).max(1);
        let bb = self.tool_box.grow(deep);
        (0..=n).any(|i| {
            let t = a + (z - a) * i as f64 / n as f64;
            let (r, d) = self.motion.place(t);
            let p = P3::from(r.inverse() * (x.coords - d));
            bb.contains(&p) && self.tool_mesh.distance(&p) < -deep
        })
    }
}

/// The surface through `at` over a box, within `tol`: a quintic B-spline through its points at
/// sites halved wherever it misses midway ([`super::sweep_pipe::fit_patch`], saying how it goes
/// when `trace`).
fn fit_sheet(
    at: &(dyn Fn(f64, f64) -> P3 + Sync),
    ((u0, u1), (v0, v1)): UvBox,
    (nu, nv): (usize, usize),
    tol: f64,
    trace: bool,
) -> Option<super::nurbs::NurbsSurface> {
    use rayon::prelude::*;
    let sites = |lo: f64, hi: f64, n: usize| -> Vec<f64> {
        (0..=n)
            .map(|i| lo + (hi - lo) * i as f64 / n as f64)
            .collect()
    };
    let (mut us, mut vs) = (sites(u0, u1, nu), sites(v0, v1, nv));
    for round in 0..14 {
        let surf = super::sweep_tube::tensor(at, &us, &vs);
        // How far the surface is from the sheet's point at (u, v): off the surface in full,
        // along it a small share only. (A sheet's points slide along it a little where the
        // tool's own surfaces are less than perfectly smooth: a contact's place on a face
        // turns on the face's slope. The sheet is the same surface for that.)
        let miss = |u: f64, v: f64| {
            let (p, su, sv) = surf.ders1(u, v);
            let d = p - at(u, v);
            let n = su.cross(&sv);
            let off = if n.norm() > 1e-300 {
                d.dot(&n).abs() / n.norm()
            } else {
                d.norm()
            };
            off.max(d.norm() * SLIDE)
        };
        let mid = |x: &[f64], i: usize| 0.5 * (x[i] + x[i + 1]);
        // Each cell's misses: midway along u at its v sites, midway along v at its u sites, and
        // at its middle.
        let by_u: Vec<f64> = (0..us.len() - 1)
            .into_par_iter()
            .map(|i| vs.iter().map(|&v| miss(mid(&us, i), v)).fold(0.0, f64::max))
            .collect();
        let by_v: Vec<f64> = (0..vs.len() - 1)
            .into_par_iter()
            .map(|j| us.iter().map(|&u| miss(u, mid(&vs, j))).fold(0.0, f64::max))
            .collect();
        let mut split_u: Vec<bool> = by_u.iter().map(|e| *e > tol).collect();
        let mut split_v: Vec<bool> = by_v.iter().map(|e| *e > tol).collect();
        let cells: Vec<(usize, usize)> = (0..us.len() - 1)
            .flat_map(|i| (0..vs.len() - 1).map(move |j| (i, j)))
            .filter(|&(i, j)| !(split_u[i] || split_v[j]))
            .collect();
        let middles: Vec<(usize, usize, f64)> = cells
            .par_iter()
            .map(|&(i, j)| (i, j, miss(mid(&us, i), mid(&vs, j))))
            .collect();
        let mut worst = by_u.iter().chain(&by_v).copied().fold(0.0, f64::max);
        for (i, j, e) in middles {
            worst = worst.max(e);
            if e > tol {
                split_u[i] = true;
                split_v[j] = true;
            }
        }
        if trace {
            let iu = (0..by_u.len())
                .max_by(|a, b| by_u[*a].total_cmp(&by_u[*b]))
                .unwrap();
            let um = mid(&us, iu);
            let jv = (0..vs.len())
                .max_by(|a, b| miss(um, vs[*a]).total_cmp(&miss(um, vs[*b])))
                .unwrap();
            eprintln!(
                "    worst along u: {:.3e} at u {:.6} (between sites {:.6} and {:.6}), v {:.6}",
                by_u[iu],
                um,
                us[iu],
                us[iu + 1],
                vs[jv]
            );
            eprintln!(
                "    fit round {round}: {} by {} sites, off by {:.2e} (of {tol:.2e}); to split: {} and {}",
                us.len(),
                vs.len(),
                worst,
                split_u.iter().filter(|s| **s).count(),
                split_v.iter().filter(|s| **s).count()
            );
        }
        if !split_u.iter().chain(&split_v).any(|s| *s) {
            return Some(surf);
        }
        if us.len() > 1200 || vs.len() > 600 {
            return None;
        }
        let halve = |x: &[f64], split: &[bool]| -> Vec<f64> {
            let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(2 * x.len());
            for i in 0..x.len() - 1 {
                out.push(x[i]);
                if split[i] {
                    out.push(0.5 * (x[i] + x[i + 1]));
                }
            }
            out.push(x[x.len() - 1]);
            out
        };
        // (No interval more than twice its neighbours: a quintic through sites crowded at one
        // place and sparse beside it sways between the sparse ones.)
        let graded = |x: Vec<f64>| -> Vec<f64> {
            let mut x = x;
            loop {
                let n = x.len() - 1;
                let h = |k: usize| x[k + 1] - x[k];
                let split: Vec<bool> = (0..n)
                    .map(|k| {
                        let left = if k > 0 { h(k - 1) } else { f64::INFINITY };
                        let right = if k + 1 < n { h(k + 1) } else { f64::INFINITY };
                        h(k) > 2.0 * left.min(right) * (1.0 + 1e-9)
                    })
                    .collect();
                if !split.iter().any(|s| *s) {
                    return x;
                }
                x = halve(&x, &split);
            }
        };
        us = graded(halve(&us, &split_u));
        vs = graded(halve(&vs, &split_v));
    }
    None
}

/// Why a cut isn't made this way, for the debug log.
fn declined(debug: bool, why: &str) {
    if debug {
        eprintln!("generated cut: declined: {why}");
    }
}

impl Gen<'_> {
    /// The plug of a tooth space: each stretch's sheets, a lid from the chain's one end to the
    /// other and a cap in the first and the last slice, sewn into a solid. None where a sheet
    /// won't fit, the tool's mesh says a sheet is no part of what it sweeps, or the lid or a cap
    /// comes within the target.
    fn plug(&self, stretches: &[Carried]) -> Option<Body> {
        use rayon::prelude::*;
        let debug = self.debug;
        // (Each stretch has its own links: stretch s's link i's sheet is slot off[s] + i.)
        let ks: Vec<usize> = stretches.iter().map(|s| s.chain.links.len()).collect();
        let off: Vec<usize> = ks
            .iter()
            .scan(0, |sum, k| {
                let at = *sum;
                *sum += k;
                Some(at)
            })
            .collect();
        let near = stretches[0].chain.about;
        let (c0, c1) = stretches[0].whole;
        let fit = SHEET_FIT * self.tool.size;
        if debug && stretches[0].cuts.is_some() {
            for (s, st) in stretches.iter().enumerate() {
                eprintln!(
                    "generated cut: stretch {s}, faces {}..{}, slices {:.6}..{:.6}: {:?} {:?}",
                    off[s],
                    off[s] + ks[s] - 1,
                    st.c.0,
                    st.c.1,
                    st.chain.links,
                    st.chain.joints.iter().map(Joint::told).collect::<Vec<_>>()
                );
            }
        }
        // Every stretch's every link's sheet: (the stretch, the sheet; none for a filler, which
        // is made from the sheets beside it).
        let slots: Vec<(usize, usize)> = (0..stretches.len())
            .flat_map(|s| (0..ks[s]).map(move |i| (s, i)))
            .collect();
        let sheets: Option<Vec<(usize, Option<Sheet>)>> = slots
            .iter()
            .map(|&(s, i)| {
                if stretches[s].chain.links[i] == Link::Fill {
                    return Some((s, None));
                }
                Some((s, Some(Sheet::new(self, &stretches[s], i)?)))
            })
            .collect();
        let Some(sheets) = sheets else {
            declined(debug, "a link can't be followed across its sheet");
            return None;
        };
        if self.trace {
            for (s, sh) in &sheets {
                let Some(sh) = sh else {
                    continue;
                };
                let (a, z) = stretches[*s].c;
                let cm = 0.5 * (a + z);
                eprintln!(
                    "  stretch {s} sheet {} {:?}: a grid of {} by {}; in its middle slice from t {:.6} to {:.6}",
                    sh.i,
                    sh.link,
                    GRID + 1,
                    sh.shares + 1,
                    stretches[*s].bound(sh.i, false, cm),
                    stretches[*s].bound(sh.i, true, cm)
                );
            }
        }
        // A check of the sheets by the tool's mesh, where they are within the target: just
        // outside each the tool never comes, just inside it does.
        {
            let probe = 2e-3 * self.tool.size;
            let spots: Vec<(usize, f64, f64)> = (0..sheets.len())
                .filter(|&i| sheets[i].1.is_some())
                .flat_map(|i| {
                    [0.15, 0.5, 0.85]
                        .into_iter()
                        .flat_map(move |x| [0.2, 0.5, 0.8].into_iter().map(move |y| (i, x, y)))
                })
                .collect();
            let wrong = spots.par_iter().find_map_any(|&(i, x, share)| {
                let (s, sh) = &sheets[i];
                let sh = sh.as_ref()?;
                let (a, z) = stretches[*s].c;
                let (t, on) = sh.on(a + (z - a) * x, share);
                let p = self.at_place(sh.link, t, on)?;
                if self.target.distance(&p) > 0.0 {
                    return None;
                }
                // (A sheet that narrows to a point where its stretch ends is not probed where
                // it is narrower than the probe is far: the point beside it is beside its
                // neighbour too.)
                if stretches[*s].cuts.is_some() {
                    let across = a + (z - a) * x;
                    if (sh.point(across, 0.0) - sh.point(across, 1.0)).norm() < 8.0 * probe {
                        return None;
                    }
                }
                let into = self.inward(sh.link, t, on)?.normalize();
                let why = if self.swept(&(p - into * probe), 0.25 * probe) {
                    Some("the tool passes over a sheet's outside")
                } else if !self.swept(&(p + into * probe), 0.25 * probe) {
                    Some("the tool never comes inside a sheet")
                } else {
                    None
                };
                if self.trace
                    && let Some(why) = why
                {
                    eprintln!(
                        "  check: {why}: stretch {s} sheet {} {:?} at slice share {x}, share {share} (t {t:.6}), {:.4} within the target",
                        sh.i,
                        sh.link,
                        -self.target.distance(&p)
                    );
                }
                why
            });
            if let Some(why) = wrong {
                declined(debug, why);
                return None;
            }
        }
        let surfaces: Vec<Option<super::nurbs::NurbsSurface>> = sheets
            .par_iter()
            .map(|(s, sh)| {
                let sh = sh.as_ref()?;
                let at = |c: f64, share: f64| sh.point(c, share);
                fit_sheet(&at, (stretches[*s].c, (0.0, 1.0)), (8, 4), fit, false)
            })
            .collect();
        if self.trace {
            for ((s, sh), fitted) in sheets.iter().zip(&surfaces) {
                let Some(sh) = sh else {
                    continue;
                };
                eprintln!(
                    "  stretch {s} sheet {} {:?}: {}; {} points missed",
                    sh.i,
                    sh.link,
                    match fitted {
                        Some(f) => format!("fits with {} by {} poles", f.cps.len(), f.cps[0].len()),
                        None => "doesn't fit".to_string(),
                    },
                    sh.missed.load(Ordering::Relaxed)
                );
            }
        }
        if sheets
            .iter()
            .filter_map(|(_, s)| s.as_ref())
            .any(|s| s.missed.load(Ordering::Relaxed) > 0)
        {
            declined(debug, "a sheet's point can't be found");
            return None;
        }
        if sheets
            .iter()
            .zip(&surfaces)
            .any(|((_, sh), fitted)| sh.is_some() && fitted.is_none())
        {
            declined(debug, "a sheet won't fit");
            return None;
        }
        let mut clear: Vec<P3> = Vec::new();
        // The fillers: where a stretch lacks a link the stretch next to it has, that link's
        // outline in the slice the two meet in, carried along this stretch on the end of its
        // own nearest link (in each slice the same shape, in the slice's own coordinates). It
        // meets the other stretch's sheet edge to edge, and is outside the target all along.
        let mut surfaces = surfaces;
        for (at, &(s, i)) in slots.iter().enumerate() {
            if surfaces[at].is_some() {
                continue;
            }
            let stretch = &stretches[s];
            let links = &stretch.chain.links;
            let Some((nb, seam)) = stretch.fill else {
                declined(debug, "a filler with no stretch beside it");
                return None;
            };
            let before = links.iter().take_while(|l| **l == Link::Fill).count();
            let after = links.iter().rev().take_while(|l| **l == Link::Fill).count();
            // (The stretch's own link the fillers hang on, and the end of it they hang on.)
            let (on, end) = if i < before {
                (before, 0.0)
            } else {
                (ks[s] - 1 - after, 1.0)
            };
            let (Some(own), Some(theirs), Some(shape)) = (
                surfaces[off[s] + on].as_ref(),
                surfaces[off[nb] + on].as_ref(),
                surfaces[off[nb] + i].as_ref(),
            ) else {
                declined(debug, "a filler with no sheet to follow");
                return None;
            };
            let anchor = self.chart.inner(&theirs.point(seam, end), near);
            let filler = |c: f64, share: f64| -> P3 {
                let base = self.chart.inner(&own.point(c, end), near);
                let at = self.chart.inner(&shape.point(seam, share), near);
                self.chart
                    .point(c, (base.0 + at.0 - anchor.0, base.1 + at.1 - anchor.1))
            };
            let Some(piece) = fit_sheet(&filler, (stretch.c, (0.0, 1.0)), (8, 4), fit, false)
            else {
                declined(debug, "a filler won't fit");
                return None;
            };
            let (a, z) = stretch.c;
            for x in 0..=16 {
                for y in 0..=8 {
                    clear.push(filler(a + (z - a) * x as f64 / 16.0, y as f64 / 8.0));
                }
                if self.trace {
                    let c = a + (z - a) * x as f64 / 16.0;
                    eprintln!(
                        "  filler {i} of stretch {s} in slice {c:.4}: from the target {:?}",
                        (0..=8)
                            .map(|y| {
                                let d = self.target.distance(&filler(c, y as f64 / 8.0));
                                (d * 1e3).round() / 1e3
                            })
                            .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                    );
                }
            }
            surfaces[at] = Some(piece);
        }
        let mut patches: Vec<(super::nurbs::NurbsSurface, UvBox)> = Vec::new();
        for (&(s, _), fitted) in slots.iter().zip(surfaces) {
            let Some(fitted) = fitted else {
                declined(debug, "a sheet won't fit");
                return None;
            };
            patches.push((fitted, (stretches[s].c, (0.0, 1.0))));
        }
        let fitted: Vec<super::nurbs::NurbsSurface> = patches.iter().map(|p| p.0.clone()).collect();
        let of = |c: f64| -> usize {
            stretches
                .iter()
                .position(|s| c <= s.c.1)
                .unwrap_or(stretches.len() - 1)
        };
        // The chain's two ends in each slice's own coordinates (from the fitted sheets, so that
        // the lid and the caps start at their very edges).
        let ends = |s: usize, c: f64| -> ((f64, f64), (f64, f64)) {
            let a = fitted[off[s]].point(c, 0.0);
            let z = fitted[off[s] + ks[s] - 1].point(c, 1.0);
            (self.chart.inner(&a, near), self.chart.inner(&z, near))
        };
        let lerp =
            |a: (f64, f64), z: (f64, f64), m: f64| (a.0 + (z.0 - a.0) * m, a.1 + (z.1 - a.1) * m);
        // The lid, a piece for each stretch and link (so that every edge of it is one sheet's
        // or one cap's too), and the caps: in the first and the last slice, each link's outline
        // joined to its piece of the lid's edge, straight in the slice's coordinates.
        for (s, stretch) in stretches.iter().enumerate() {
            let (a, z) = stretch.c;
            let lid = |c: f64, m: f64| -> P3 {
                let (from, to) = ends(s, c);
                self.chart.point(c, lerp(from, to, m))
            };
            let k = ks[s];
            for i in 0..k {
                let (m0, m1) = (i as f64 / k as f64, (i + 1) as f64 / k as f64);
                let Some(piece) = fit_sheet(&lid, ((a, z), (m0, m1)), (4, 1), fit, false) else {
                    declined(debug, "the lid won't fit");
                    return None;
                };
                for x in 0..=8 {
                    for y in 0..=4 {
                        clear.push(lid(
                            a + (z - a) * x as f64 / 8.0,
                            m0 + (m1 - m0) * y as f64 / 4.0,
                        ));
                    }
                }
                patches.push((piece, ((a, z), (m0, m1))));
            }
        }
        for c in [c0, c1] {
            let s = of(c);
            let (from, to) = ends(s, c);
            let k = ks[s];
            for i in 0..k {
                let (m0, m1) = (i as f64 / k as f64, (i + 1) as f64 / k as f64);
                let sheet = &fitted[off[s] + i];
                let cap = |share: f64, v: f64| -> P3 {
                    let on = self.chart.inner(&sheet.point(c, share), near);
                    let at = lerp(from, to, m0 + (m1 - m0) * share);
                    self.chart.point(c, lerp(on, at, v))
                };
                let Some(piece) = fit_sheet(&cap, ((0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0)), (8, 2), fit, false)
                else {
                    declined(debug, "a cap won't fit");
                    return None;
                };
                for x in 0..=8 {
                    for y in 0..=4 {
                        clear.push(cap(x as f64 / 8.0, y as f64 / 4.0));
                    }
                }
                patches.push((piece, ((0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0))));
            }
        }
        if self.trace {
            // (Which of them: the fillers' points first, then each stretch's lid's, then the
            // caps'.)
            let near: Vec<(usize, f64)> = clear
                .iter()
                .enumerate()
                .map(|(i, p)| (i, self.target.distance(p)))
                .filter(|(_, d)| *d <= 0.5 * self.clear)
                .collect();
            if let (Some(first), Some(last)) = (near.first(), near.last()) {
                let worst = near.iter().map(|n| n.1).fold(f64::INFINITY, f64::min);
                eprintln!(
                    "  {} of the {} points of fillers, lids and caps are within {:.4} of the target (the nearest {worst:.4}): points {} to {}; a filler has {}, a lid piece or a cap {}",
                    near.len(),
                    clear.len(),
                    0.5 * self.clear,
                    first.0,
                    last.0,
                    17 * 9,
                    9 * 5
                );
            }
        }
        if clear
            .par_iter()
            .any(|p| self.target.distance(p) <= 0.5 * self.clear)
        {
            declined(debug, "the lid or a cap comes within the target");
            return None;
        }
        if debug && std::env::var_os("CADRS_GEN_PLUG").is_some() {
            // (Each patch's sides that are all but points: how far a side's points spread.)
            for (i, (s, ((u0, u1), (v0, v1)))) in patches.iter().enumerate() {
                let spread = |f: &dyn Fn(f64) -> P3| {
                    let p0 = f(0.0);
                    (1..=16)
                        .map(|k| (f(k as f64 / 16.0) - p0).norm())
                        .fold(0.0, f64::max)
                };
                let sides = [
                    spread(&|x| s.point(u0 + (u1 - u0) * x, *v0)),
                    spread(&|x| s.point(*u1, v0 + (v1 - v0) * x)),
                    spread(&|x| s.point(u0 + (u1 - u0) * x, *v1)),
                    spread(&|x| s.point(*u0, v0 + (v1 - v0) * x)),
                ];
                if sides.iter().any(|x| *x < 1e-3 * self.tool.size) {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: patch {i}: its sides spread {:?}",
                        sides.map(|x| format!("{x:.2e}"))
                    );
                }
            }
        }
        let mut all = Body::default();
        for (s, domain) in patches {
            let surf = Surface::Nurbs(std::sync::Arc::new(s));
            match super::face_build::face_from_surface(&surf, Some(domain)) {
                Ok(f) => {
                    all.append(&f);
                }
                Err(e) => {
                    if debug {
                        eprintln!("generated cut: declined: a sheet makes no face: {e}");
                    }
                    return None;
                }
            }
        }
        match super::surfacing::sewn_solid(all, 1e3 * fit) {
            Ok(b) => Some(b),
            Err(e) => {
                if debug {
                    eprintln!("generated cut: declined: the plug doesn't close: {e}");
                }
                None
            }
        }
    }

    /// The chains of slice `c`, one through each of its nodes within the target (each chain
    /// once). None where one of those nodes has no chain.
    fn chains_at(&self, c: f64, nodes: &[Node], cands: &[Cand], about: f64) -> Option<Vec<Chain>> {
        let period = self.repeat.map(|r| r.0);
        let mut chains: Vec<Chain> = Vec::new();
        for seed in nodes.iter().filter(|n| !self.clear_of_target(&n.p)) {
            if chains.iter().any(|c| {
                c.joints.iter().any(|j| {
                    let Joint::Node(m) = j else {
                        return false;
                    };
                    m.r == seed.r
                        && m.side == seed.side
                        && match period {
                            Some(p) => {
                                let turns = (seed.t - m.t) / p;
                                (turns - turns.round()).abs() * p < 0.5 * self.dt
                            }
                            None => (seed.t - m.t).abs() < 0.5 * self.dt,
                        }
                })
            }) {
                continue;
            }
            let Some(chain) = self.chain(c, seed, cands, about, 0) else {
                if self.debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: no chain from the node of run {} (side {}) at t {:.5} in slice {c:.4}",
                        seed.r, seed.side, seed.t
                    );
                }
                return None;
            };
            if !chains
                .iter()
                .any(|c| same_chain(c, &chain, period, self.dt))
            {
                chains.push(chain);
            }
        }
        Some(chains)
    }

    /// A chain like `like` (the same links in the same order) in slice `c`, found afresh
    /// there; for a motion that repeats, the one of its turns whose first joint is nearest
    /// `like`'s in the row `by`.
    fn chain_like(&self, like: &Chain, c: f64, by: &[Joint]) -> Option<Chain> {
        let nodes = self.nodes(c, self.window, self.reach);
        let cands = self.cands(c, &nodes, like.about);
        let k = like.links.len();
        // The part of a chain that has `like`'s links, in order.
        let part = |ch: Chain| -> Option<Chain> {
            let n = ch.links.len();
            let w = (0..=n.checked_sub(k)?).find(|&w| ch.links[w..w + k] == like.links[..])?;
            if w == 0 && n == k {
                return Some(ch);
            }
            // (Each end link's way in time from its joint: toward the joint left out, or the
            // chain's own end.)
            let first = if w > 0 {
                (ch.joints[w - 1].t(true) - ch.joints[w].t(false)).signum()
            } else {
                ch.out[0]
            };
            let last = if w + k < n {
                (ch.joints[w + k - 1].t(false) - ch.joints[w + k - 2].t(true)).signum()
            } else {
                ch.out[1]
            };
            Some(Chain {
                joints: ch.joints[w..w + k - 1].to_vec(),
                links: ch.links[w..w + k].to_vec(),
                out: [first, last],
                about: ch.about,
            })
        };
        let either = |ch: Chain| -> Option<Chain> {
            let other = ch.turned();
            part(ch).or_else(|| part(other))
        };
        // (As a chain is found, then followed on past the links that leave the target: `like`
        // may have links that are outside it in this slice.)
        for full in [0, k] {
            for seed in nodes.iter().filter(|n| !self.clear_of_target(&n.p)) {
                let Some(found) = self.chain(c, seed, &cands, like.about, full) else {
                    continue;
                };
                if self.trace {
                    eprintln!("  in slice {c:.5} a chain of links {:?}", found.links);
                }
                let Some(found) = either(found) else {
                    continue;
                };
                // The turn of the tool it is found in, brought to `like`'s.
                let later = match self.repeat {
                    Some((period, ..)) => {
                        ((found.joints[0].t(false) - by[0].t(false)) / period).round() * period
                    }
                    None => 0.0,
                };
                let joints: Option<Vec<Joint>> = found
                    .joints
                    .iter()
                    .enumerate()
                    .map(|(j, joint)| match joint {
                        Joint::Node(m) => self
                            .node(m.r, m.side, c, (m.sigma, m.t - later))
                            .map(Joint::Node),
                        Joint::Cross { before, after, .. } => self.cross_at(
                            c,
                            (found.links[j], before.0, before.1 - later),
                            (found.links[j + 1], after.0, after.1 - later),
                            like.about,
                        ),
                        Joint::Corner(k) => {
                            let (t, p) = self.corner(k.v, c, k.t - later)?;
                            Some(Joint::Corner(Corner { t, p, ..*k }))
                        }
                        Joint::Free => Some(Joint::Free),
                    })
                    .collect();
                return Some(Chain {
                    joints: joints?,
                    ..found
                });
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// A stretch to go on from `here` the way `dir`, where this one's chain can be carried no
    /// farther: the chain found in slice `beyond`, which has `here`'s links but for some at its
    /// ends, those being outside the target where `here` stops. With the slices `here` keeps
    /// and those the other takes: handed over between where `here` stops and where the links
    /// the other lacks come within the target. None where there is no such chain, or it can't
    /// be carried to the end of the slices.
    #[allow(clippy::type_complexity)]
    fn shorter(
        &self,
        here: &Span,
        dir: f64,
        beyond: f64,
        (lo, hi): (f64, f64),
    ) -> Option<(((f64, f64), (f64, f64)), Span)> {
        let k = here.chain.links.len();
        let by = if dir > 0.0 {
            &here.rows[here.rows.len() - 1]
        } else {
            &here.rows[0]
        };
        let limit = by.0;
        let point = |j: &Joint| j.point();
        // How far from the target the nearest of `here`'s joints before `a` and from `z` on
        // is, in a row of it.
        let off = |row: &[Joint], a: usize, z: usize| -> f64 {
            row[..a]
                .iter()
                .chain(&row[z..])
                .filter_map(point)
                .map(|p| self.target.distance(&p))
                .fold(f64::INFINITY, f64::min)
        };
        let nodes = self.nodes(beyond, self.window, self.reach);
        let cands = self.cands(beyond, &nodes, here.chain.about);
        for found in self.chains_at(beyond, &nodes, &cands, here.chain.about)? {
            for ch in [found.turned(), found] {
                let m = ch.links.len();
                if m < 2 || m >= k {
                    continue;
                }
                let Some(a) = (0..=k - m).find(|&a| here.chain.links[a..a + m] == ch.links[..])
                else {
                    continue;
                };
                // (Its joints are `here`'s from `a` to `a + m − 1`.)
                let z = a + m - 1;
                if off(&by.1, a, z) <= 4.0 * self.clear {
                    continue;
                }
                // The turn of the tool it is found in, brought to `here`'s.
                let later = match self.repeat {
                    Some((period, ..)) => {
                        ((ch.joints[0].t(false) - by.1[a].t(false)) / period).round() * period
                    }
                    None => 0.0,
                };
                let joints: Option<Vec<Joint>> = ch
                    .joints
                    .iter()
                    .enumerate()
                    .map(|(j, joint)| match joint {
                        Joint::Node(n) => self
                            .node(n.r, n.side, beyond, (n.sigma, n.t - later))
                            .map(Joint::Node),
                        Joint::Cross { before, after, .. } => self.cross_at(
                            beyond,
                            (ch.links[j], before.0, before.1 - later),
                            (ch.links[j + 1], after.0, after.1 - later),
                            ch.about,
                        ),
                        Joint::Corner(k) => {
                            let (t, p) = self.corner(k.v, beyond, k.t - later)?;
                            Some(Joint::Corner(Corner { t, p, ..*k }))
                        }
                        Joint::Free => None,
                    })
                    .collect();
                let chain = Chain {
                    joints: joints?,
                    ..ch
                };
                let rows = self.rows(&chain, beyond, (lo, hi));
                let (o0, o1) = (rows[0].0, rows[rows.len() - 1].0);
                // Handed over most of the way from where `here` stops to where the links the
                // other lacks come near the target.
                let near = here
                    .rows
                    .iter()
                    .filter(|r| off(&r.1, a, z) <= 8.0 * self.clear)
                    .map(|r| r.0)
                    .fold(if dir > 0.0 { here.c.0 } else { here.c.1 }, |m, c| {
                        if dir > 0.0 { m.max(c) } else { m.min(c) }
                    });
                let hand = limit + 0.75 * (near - limit);
                let (mine, theirs) = if dir > 0.0 {
                    ((here.c.0, hand), (hand, o1))
                } else {
                    ((hand, here.c.1), (o0, hand))
                };
                let reaches = if dir > 0.0 {
                    (hi - o1) <= 1e-9 * (hi - lo)
                } else {
                    (o0 - lo) <= 1e-9 * (hi - lo)
                };
                if !(reaches && mine.0 < mine.1 && theirs.0 < theirs.1 && hand >= o0 && hand <= o1)
                {
                    continue;
                }
                return Some((
                    (mine, theirs),
                    Span {
                        chain,
                        rows,
                        c: (o0, o1),
                        skip: [a, k - 1 - z],
                    },
                ));
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// The stretches of a tooth space along its length: the chain found in slice `mid` carried
    /// as far each way as its joints stay what they are, and where it stops short of the
    /// slices `lo` to `hi` a chain found afresh beyond, with a crossing where this has a node
    /// or a node where this has a crossing; the two handed over where the crossing closes to a
    /// touch. `inner`: the target's own slices, where a chain can be found.
    fn spans(
        &self,
        chain: &Chain,
        mid: f64,
        (lo, hi): (f64, f64),
        inner: (f64, f64),
    ) -> Option<Vec<Span>> {
        let whole = hi - lo;
        let n = chain.joints.len();
        let rows = self.rows(chain, mid, (lo, hi));
        let ends = |rows: &[(f64, Vec<Joint>)]| (rows[0].0, rows[rows.len() - 1].0);
        let mut spans = vec![Span {
            chain: chain.clone(),
            c: ends(&rows),
            rows,
            skip: [0, 0],
        }];
        // A stretch's rows from `a` to `z`, with a row at each of the two.
        let clip = |span: &Span, (a, z): (f64, f64)| -> Option<Span> {
            let nearest = |c: f64| {
                span.rows
                    .iter()
                    .min_by(|x, y| (x.0 - c).abs().total_cmp(&(y.0 - c).abs()))
                    .expect("a stretch has rows")
            };
            let mut rows: Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>)> =
                vec![(a, self.row_at(&span.chain, a, &nearest(a).1)?)];
            rows.extend(span.rows.iter().filter(|r| r.0 > a && r.0 < z).cloned());
            rows.push((z, self.row_at(&span.chain, z, &nearest(z).1)?));
            Some(Span {
                chain: span.chain.clone(),
                rows,
                c: (a, z),
                skip: span.skip,
            })
        };
        for dir in [1.0, -1.0] {
            loop {
                let at = if dir > 0.0 { spans.len() - 1 } else { 0 };
                let (limit, end, last) = if dir > 0.0 {
                    (spans[at].c.1, hi, inner.1)
                } else {
                    (spans[at].c.0, lo, inner.0)
                };
                // (Far enough: past the target's own slices by most of the way asked.)
                if (end - limit) * dir <= 1e-9 * whole
                    || (limit - last) * dir >= 0.5 * (end - last) * dir
                {
                    break;
                }
                if spans.len() > 6 {
                    return None;
                }
                // A chain found a little beyond.
                let beyond = limit + dir * whole / 96.0;
                if (last - beyond) * dir < 0.0 {
                    if self.debug {
                        eprintln!(
                            "generated cut: the chain stops at slice {limit:.5}, short of the target's end"
                        );
                    }
                    return None;
                }
                let here = &spans[at];
                let by = if dir > 0.0 {
                    &here.rows[here.rows.len() - 1].1
                } else {
                    &here.rows[0].1
                };
                let Some(other) = self.chain_like(&here.chain, beyond, by) else {
                    // The chain there may lack this one's end links, which are outside the
                    // target by then: it is carried on from before they come out.
                    if here.skip == [0, 0]
                        && let Some((cs, theirs)) = self.shorter(here, dir, beyond, (lo, hi))
                        && let (Some(mine), Some(theirs)) = (clip(here, cs.0), clip(&theirs, cs.1))
                    {
                        if self.debug {
                            eprintln!(
                                "generated cut: past slice {:.5} the chain has fewer links ({} and {} of them outside the target): {:?}",
                                if dir > 0.0 { mine.c.1 } else { mine.c.0 },
                                theirs.skip[0],
                                theirs.skip[1],
                                theirs.chain.links
                            );
                        }
                        spans[at] = mine;
                        if dir > 0.0 {
                            spans.push(theirs);
                        } else {
                            spans.insert(0, theirs);
                        }
                        break;
                    }
                    if self.debug {
                        eprintln!("generated cut: no chain like it is found past slice {limit:.5}");
                    }
                    return None;
                };
                let rows = self.rows(&other, beyond, (lo, hi));
                let (o0, o1) = ends(&rows);
                let other = Span {
                    chain: other,
                    rows,
                    c: (o0, o1),
                    skip: [0, 0],
                };
                // The joints that differ: handed over where the one with crossings there stops.
                let differ: Vec<usize> = (0..n)
                    .filter(|&j| {
                        matches!(here.chain.joints[j], Joint::Node(_))
                            != matches!(other.chain.joints[j], Joint::Node(_))
                    })
                    .collect();
                let crosses = |ch: &Chain| {
                    differ
                        .iter()
                        .all(|&j| matches!(ch.joints[j], Joint::Cross { .. }))
                };
                let hand = if differ.is_empty() {
                    None
                } else if crosses(&here.chain) {
                    Some(limit)
                } else if crosses(&other.chain) {
                    Some(if dir > 0.0 { o0 } else { o1 })
                } else {
                    None
                };
                let Some(hand) = hand else {
                    if self.debug {
                        eprintln!(
                            "generated cut: the chain past slice {limit:.5} doesn't go on from this one"
                        );
                    }
                    return None;
                };
                if self.debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: a stretch from slice {:.5} to {:.5} hands over at {hand:.5} to one from {o0:.5} to {o1:.5} (joints {differ:?} change)",
                        here.c.0, here.c.1
                    );
                }
                let (mine, theirs) = if dir > 0.0 {
                    ((here.c.0, hand), (hand, o1))
                } else {
                    ((hand, here.c.1), (o0, hand))
                };
                if !(mine.0 < mine.1 && theirs.0 < theirs.1 && hand >= o0 && hand <= o1) {
                    return None;
                }
                let (mine, theirs) = (clip(here, mine)?, clip(&other, theirs)?);
                spans[at] = mine;
                if dir > 0.0 {
                    spans.push(theirs);
                } else {
                    spans.insert(0, theirs);
                }
            }
        }
        Some(spans)
    }
}

type UvBox = ((f64, f64), (f64, f64));

/// The stretches bound for their sheets. One that lacks links at its ends ([`Span::skip`]) is
/// given fillers in their place, and its own nearest link is cut where the stretch beside it
/// has that link's joint: as long after its other joint here as there, in the slice the two
/// stretches meet in.
#[allow(clippy::type_complexity)]
fn carried(
    spans: &[Span],
    bound: &[(Vec<(f64, Vec<Joint>)>, Vec<NurbsCurve>, Vec<NurbsCurve>)],
    whole: (f64, f64),
    ends: &[Vec<f64>; 2],
    own: &[[Option<Vec<f64>>; 2]],
    blend: f64,
) -> Option<Vec<Carried>> {
    // A stretch's own cut of its end link (a time past its joint, a polynomial of the slice's
    // place across them all), brought over the last `blend` of the stretch to `long` where it
    // meets the stretch beside it.
    fn cut_to<'a>(
        own: &'a [f64],
        whole: (f64, f64),
        (a, z): (f64, f64),
        seam: f64,
        long: f64,
        blend: f64,
    ) -> impl Fn(f64) -> f64 + 'a {
        let poly = move |c: f64| {
            let x = (c - whole.0) / (whole.1 - whole.0);
            own.iter().rev().fold(0.0, |acc, k| acc * x + k)
        };
        let off = long - poly(seam);
        let far = if seam == z { a } else { z };
        move |c: f64| {
            let u = (1.0 - (seam - c) / ((seam - far) * blend)).clamp(0.0, 1.0);
            poly(c) + off * u * u * u * (10.0 - 15.0 * u + 6.0 * u * u)
        }
    }
    let cut = |own, c, seam, long| cut_to(own, whole, c, seam, long, blend);
    let mut out = Vec::new();
    for (i, (s, (rows, before, after))) in spans.iter().zip(bound).enumerate() {
        let [a, b] = s.skip;
        if a == 0 && b == 0 {
            out.push(Carried {
                chain: s.chain.clone(),
                c: s.c,
                whole,
                rows: rows.clone(),
                before: before.clone(),
                after: after.clone(),
                ends: ends.clone(),
                fill: None,
                cuts: None,
            });
            continue;
        }
        let m = s.chain.links.len();
        let nb = [i.wrapping_sub(1), i + 1]
            .into_iter()
            .find(|&j| j < spans.len() && spans[j].skip == [0, 0])?;
        let seam = if nb > i { s.c.1 } else { s.c.0 };
        let (_, theirs_before, theirs_after) = &bound[nb];
        let cs: Vec<f64> = rows.iter().map(|r| r.0).collect();
        let none = || through(&[s.c.0, s.c.1], &[0.0, 0.0]);
        // (This stretch's first link is the other's link `a`, from its joint a − 1 to its
        // joint a; its last the other's link a + m − 1.)
        let first = match (a > 0, &own[i][0]) {
            (true, Some(co)) => {
                let long = theirs_after[a - 1].point(seam).x - theirs_before[a].point(seam).x;
                let cut = cut(co, s.c, seam, long);
                Some(through(
                    &cs,
                    &cs.iter()
                        .map(|&c| before[0].point(c).x + cut(c))
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>(),
                ))
            }
            (true, None) => return None,
            _ => None,
        };
        let last = match (b > 0, &own[i][1]) {
            (true, Some(co)) => {
                let long =
                    theirs_before[a + m - 1].point(seam).x - theirs_after[a + m - 2].point(seam).x;
                let cut = cut(co, s.c, seam, long);
                Some(through(
                    &cs,
                    &cs.iter()
                        .map(|&c| after[m - 2].point(c).x + cut(c))
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>(),
                ))
            }
            (true, None) => return None,
            _ => None,
        };
        let padded = |row: &[Joint]| -> Vec<Joint> {
            let mut all = vec![Joint::Free; a];
            all.extend(row.iter().copied());
            all.extend(vec![Joint::Free; b]);
            all
        };
        let mut links = vec![Link::Fill; a];
        links.extend(s.chain.links.iter().copied());
        links.extend(vec![Link::Fill; b]);
        let mut all_before: Vec<NurbsCurve> = (0..a).map(|_| none()).collect();
        all_before.extend(before.iter().cloned());
        all_before.extend(last);
        all_before.extend((1..b).map(|_| none()));
        let mut all_after: Vec<NurbsCurve> = (1..a).map(|_| none()).collect();
        all_after.extend(first);
        all_after.extend(after.iter().cloned());
        all_after.extend((0..b).map(|_| none()));
        out.push(Carried {
            chain: Chain {
                joints: padded(&s.chain.joints),
                links,
                out: s.chain.out,
                about: s.chain.about,
            },
            c: s.c,
            whole,
            rows: rows.iter().map(|(c, row)| (*c, padded(row))).collect(),
            before: all_before,
            after: all_after,
            ends: ends.clone(),
            fill: Some((nb, seam)),
            cuts: None,
        });
    }
    Some(out)
}

/// A polynomial's value (its coefficients lowest first).
fn poly_at(co: &[f64], x: f64) -> f64 {
    co.iter().rev().fold(0.0, |acc, k| acc * x + k)
}

/// A tooth space's roof: a straight line across each slice, in the slice's own coordinates, just
/// outside the target's surface there (the face the tooth space opens through). What the tool
/// sweeps under it is the plug; the chain of each slice is trimmed where it comes out through
/// it, so that a chain's end is the same point whichever links it has.
struct Roof {
    about: f64,
    /// The slices its polynomials run over (their variable from 0 to 1).
    c: (f64, f64),
    /// A point the lines are told from.
    mid: (f64, f64),
    /// The way out across the line (an angle in the slice's coordinates) and the line's
    /// distance from `mid` that way, polynomials of the slice.
    angle: Vec<f64>,
    off: Vec<f64>,
}

impl Roof {
    /// How far past the roof a point is, in its slice's coordinates (negative under it, on the
    /// target's side).
    fn past(&self, chart: &Chart, p: &P3) -> f64 {
        let (a, b) = chart.inner(p, self.about);
        self.past_at(chart.c(p), (a, b))
    }

    fn past_at(&self, c: f64, (a, b): (f64, f64)) -> f64 {
        let x = (c - self.c.0) / (self.c.1 - self.c.0);
        let (angle, off) = (poly_at(&self.angle, x), poly_at(&self.off, x));
        (a - self.mid.0) * angle.cos() + (b - self.mid.1) * angle.sin() - off
    }

    /// The roof through the two points a chain comes out by in each of some slices (each with
    /// a point deep under it), as nearly as polynomials of the slice follow them: within `tol`.
    fn fit(chart: &Chart, about: f64, exits: &[(f64, [(f64, f64); 3])], tol: f64) -> Option<Roof> {
        let c = (exits.first()?.0, exits.last()?.0);
        if !(c.1 > c.0) {
            return None;
        }
        let n = 2.0 * exits.len() as f64;
        let mid = exits.iter().fold((0.0, 0.0), |m, (_, e)| {
            (m.0 + (e[0].0 + e[1].0) / n, m.1 + (e[0].1 + e[1].1) / n)
        });
        let (mut xs, mut angles, mut offs) = (Vec::new(), Vec::new(), Vec::new());
        let mut last: Option<f64> = None;
        for (ci, [a, z, deep]) in exits {
            let (da, db) = (z.0 - a.0, z.1 - a.1);
            let len = da.hypot(db);
            if !(len > 0.0) {
                return None;
            }
            let mut out = (-db / len, da / len);
            if out.0 * (deep.0 - a.0) + out.1 * (deep.1 - a.1) > 0.0 {
                out = (-out.0, -out.1);
            }
            let mut angle = out.1.atan2(out.0);
            if let Some(l) = last {
                angle += TAU * ((l - angle) / TAU).round();
            }
            last = Some(angle);
            xs.push((ci - c.0) / (c.1 - c.0));
            angles.push(angle);
            offs.push(out.0 * (a.0 - mid.0) + out.1 * (a.1 - mid.1));
        }
        // How far a slice's two points are from a roof's line, as a length.
        let off_of = |roof: &Roof, (ci, e): &(f64, [(f64, f64); 3])| -> f64 {
            [e[0], e[1]]
                .into_iter()
                .map(|p| {
                    let x = (ci - c.0) / (c.1 - c.0);
                    let angle = poly_at(&roof.angle, x);
                    let over = roof.past_at(*ci, p);
                    let foot = (p.0 - over * angle.cos(), p.1 - over * angle.sin());
                    (chart.point(*ci, p) - chart.point(*ci, foot)).norm()
                })
                .fold(0.0, f64::max)
        };
        // (Through most of the slices will do: in a slice at an end of the target, where the
        // target's own end face crosses it, a chain may come out by that face instead.)
        (0..=5).find_map(|deg| {
            let mut used: Vec<usize> = (0..exits.len()).collect();
            for _ in 0..4 {
                let pick = |v: &[f64]| used.iter().map(|&i| v[i]).collect::<Vec<_>>();
                let roof = Roof {
                    about,
                    c,
                    mid,
                    angle: poly_fit(&pick(&xs), &pick(&angles), deg)?,
                    off: poly_fit(&pick(&xs), &pick(&offs), deg)?,
                };
                let near: Vec<usize> = (0..exits.len())
                    .filter(|&i| off_of(&roof, &exits[i]) <= tol)
                    .collect();
                if near.len() < 6 || 5 * near.len() < 3 * exits.len() {
                    return None;
                }
                if near == used {
                    return Some(roof);
                }
                used = near;
            }
            None
        })
    }
}

/// A chain trimmed at a roof, with where its two end links meet the roof (each one's instant
/// and place there).
type Trimmed = (Chain, [(f64, Place); 2]);

/// A chain's joints in a slice, with where its two end links meet the roof (each one's instant
/// and place there).
type Row = (f64, Vec<Joint>, [(f64, Place); 2]);

/// Whether two chains have the same links joined the same ways.
fn alike(a: &Chain, b: &Chain) -> bool {
    a.links == b.links
        && a.joints.iter().zip(&b.joints).all(|(x, y)| match (x, y) {
            (Joint::Node(m), Joint::Node(n)) => m.r == n.r && m.side == n.side,
            (Joint::Cross { .. }, Joint::Cross { .. }) => true,
            (Joint::Corner(m), Joint::Corner(n)) => m.v == n.v,
            _ => false,
        })
}

/// Whether two chains have the same links, joined the same ways but that the one may have a node
/// where the other has its two links cross (the loop between a crossing and its node, within
/// what the tool sweeps, grown from nothing or too short to be found).
fn akin(a: &Chain, b: &Chain) -> bool {
    a.links == b.links
        && a.joints.iter().zip(&b.joints).all(|(x, y)| match (x, y) {
            (Joint::Node(m), Joint::Node(n)) => m.r == n.r && m.side == n.side,
            (Joint::Corner(m), Joint::Corner(n)) => m.v == n.v,
            (Joint::Corner(_), _) | (_, Joint::Corner(_)) => false,
            _ => true,
        })
}

/// The links of `a` and of `b` that have no partner in the other, the two taken in order (by
/// their longest common run of links, not needing to be together).
fn unmatched(a: &[Link], b: &[Link]) -> (Vec<usize>, Vec<usize>) {
    let (n, m) = (a.len(), b.len());
    let mut best = vec![vec![0usize; m + 1]; n + 1];
    for i in (0..n).rev() {
        for j in (0..m).rev() {
            best[i][j] = if a[i] == b[j] {
                best[i + 1][j + 1] + 1
            } else {
                best[i + 1][j].max(best[i][j + 1])
            };
        }
    }
    let (mut i, mut j) = (0, 0);
    let (mut ua, mut ub) = (Vec::new(), Vec::new());
    while i < n && j < m {
        if a[i] == b[j] {
            (i, j) = (i + 1, j + 1);
        } else if best[i + 1][j] >= best[i][j + 1] {
            ua.push(i);
            i += 1;
        } else {
            ub.push(j);
            j += 1;
        }
    }
    ua.extend(i..n);
    ub.extend(j..m);
    (ua, ub)
}

impl Gen<'_> {
    /// How near the tool comes to a point of the target's frame over the motion: the least of
    /// its distance from the tool (by the tool's mesh; negative within it). Found by steps the
    /// tool can't pass through the point in; from `floor` (negative) down it is looked into no
    /// farther.
    fn depth(&self, x: &P3, floor: f64) -> f64 {
        let (a, z) = self.span.unwrap_or((0.0, 1.0));
        let least = 0.25 * floor.abs() / self.speed;
        let reach = self.tool.size;
        let bb = self.tool_box.grow(reach);
        let (mut t, mut best) = (a, f64::INFINITY);
        while t <= z {
            let (r, d) = self.motion.place(t);
            let p = P3::from(r.inverse() * (x.coords - d));
            let dist = if bb.contains(&p) {
                self.tool_mesh.distance(&p)
            } else {
                reach
            };
            best = best.min(dist);
            if best < floor {
                break;
            }
            // (The tool's points near it move at `speed` at most, or little more.)
            t += (0.5 * dist.abs() / self.speed).max(least);
        }
        best
    }

    /// The points of link `i` of a chain in slice `c`, from its first joint to its second (an
    /// end link: from its joint out, as far as it goes).
    fn link_points(&self, c: f64, chain: &Chain, i: usize) -> Option<Vec<(f64, P3, Place)>> {
        let k = chain.links.len();
        let link = chain.links[i];
        let (j, after, dir, to) = if i == 0 {
            (0, false, chain.out[0], None)
        } else if i == k - 1 {
            (i - 1, true, chain.out[1], None)
        } else {
            let way = (chain.joints[i].t(false) - chain.joints[i - 1].t(true)).signum();
            (i - 1, true, way, Some(i))
        };
        let joint = &chain.joints[j];
        let (place, t0) = self.joint_on(joint, link, after)?;
        let reach = match joint {
            Joint::Node(m) => self.follow(c, m, link)?,
            Joint::Free => return None,
            _ => self.march(c, link, place, t0, dir, None),
        };
        let mut pts = reach.pts;
        if pts.len() < 2 || (pts[pts.len() - 1].0 - pts[0].0) * dir <= 0.0 {
            return None;
        }
        if let Some(e) = to {
            let end = &chain.joints[e];
            let (pe, te) = self.joint_on(end, link, false)?;
            pts.retain(|p| (te - p.0) * dir > 0.0);
            pts.push((te, end.point()?, pe));
        }
        Some(pts)
    }

    /// Going out along a chain from its joint `from` (up its links, or down them), the first
    /// place `f` turns from negative to not: the link, its point before and its point after.
    #[allow(clippy::type_complexity)]
    fn first_past(
        &self,
        c: f64,
        chain: &Chain,
        from: usize,
        up: bool,
        f: &dyn Fn(&P3) -> f64,
    ) -> Option<(usize, (f64, P3, Place), (f64, P3, Place))> {
        let k = chain.links.len();
        let order: Vec<usize> = if up {
            (from + 1..k).collect()
        } else {
            (0..=from).rev().collect()
        };
        for i in order {
            let mut pts = self.link_points(c, chain, i)?;
            // (Outward: a link below the joint, but the chain's first, runs back from its
            // second joint.)
            if !up && i > 0 {
                pts.reverse();
            }
            if let Some(w) = pts
                .windows(2)
                .find(|w| f(&w[0].1) < 0.0 && f(&w[1].1) >= 0.0)
            {
                return Some((i, w[0], w[1]));
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// The chains of slice `c` that have two or more of `like`'s links, each followed on past
    /// the target as far as it goes.
    fn full_chains(&self, c: f64, like: &[Link], about: f64) -> Vec<Chain> {
        let nodes = self.nodes(c, self.window, self.reach);
        let cands = self.cands(c, &nodes, about);
        let mut out: Vec<Chain> = Vec::new();
        // (From every node within the target: one within what the tool sweeps, where an
        // envelope turns back on itself, makes a chain of its own that is no outline, and has
        // the outline's other nodes all the same.)
        for seed in nodes.iter().filter(|n| !self.clear_of_target(&n.p)) {
            let Some(ch) = self.chain(c, seed, &cands, about, 16) else {
                continue;
            };
            if ch.links.iter().filter(|l| like.contains(l)).count() < 2 {
                continue;
            }
            if !out.iter().any(|o| same_chain(o, &ch, None, self.dt)) {
                out.push(ch);
            }
        }
        out
    }

    /// Where a chain of slice `c` comes `level` clear of the target at each end, going out
    /// from its joint deepest in it, and that joint: all in the slice's coordinates.
    fn exits(&self, c: f64, chain: &Chain, level: f64) -> Option<[(f64, f64); 3]> {
        let far = |p: &P3| self.target.distance(p) - level;
        let (deep, at) = chain
            .joints
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
            .filter_map(|(j, m)| Some((j, m.point()?)))
            .min_by(|a, b| far(&a.1).total_cmp(&far(&b.1)))?;
        if far(&at) >= -level {
            return None;
        }
        let out = |up: bool| -> Option<(f64, f64)> {
            let (_, u, v) = self.first_past(c, chain, deep, up, &far)?;
            let (fu, fv) = (far(&u.1), far(&v.1));
            let x = u.1 + (v.1 - u.1) * (fu / (fu - fv));
            Some(self.chart.inner(&x, chain.about))
        };
        Some([out(false)?, out(true)?, self.chart.inner(&at, chain.about)])
    }

    /// Where a link meets the roof in slice `c`, from an instant and a place of it near there.
    fn cut_at(&self, roof: &Roof, c: f64, link: Link, guess: (f64, Place)) -> Option<(f64, Place)> {
        let at = |t: f64, near: Place| -> Option<(f64, Place)> {
            let on = self.place(link, t, c, near)?;
            Some((roof.past(&self.chart, &self.at_place(link, t, on)?), on))
        };
        let h = 1e-3 * self.dt;
        let why = |what: &str, t: f64| {
            if self.trace {
                eprintln!(
                    "    slice {c:.6}: {link:?} to the roof from t {:.9}: {what} at t {t:.9}",
                    guess.0
                );
            }
        };
        let (mut t, mut on) = guess;
        let Some((mut v, here)) = at(t, on) else {
            why("no place to start from", t);
            return None;
        };
        on = here;
        for _ in 0..60 {
            // (On the roof as nearly as numbers tell, where the link meets it at so slight an
            // angle that the instant itself won't settle.)
            if v.abs() <= 1e-12 {
                return Some((t, on));
            }
            let slope = match (at(t + h, on), at(t - h, on)) {
                (Some(a), Some(b)) => (a.0 - b.0) / (2.0 * h),
                (Some(a), None) => (a.0 - v) / h,
                (None, Some(b)) => (v - b.0) / h,
                (None, None) => {
                    why("no place to either side", t);
                    return None;
                }
            };
            if !(slope.abs() > 1e-300) {
                why("the link runs along the roof", t);
                return None;
            }
            // A step toward the roof, shortened while it leads off the link.
            let mut step = (-v / slope).clamp(-4.0 * self.dt, 4.0 * self.dt);
            let mut next = at(t + step, on);
            for _ in 0..40 {
                if next.is_some() {
                    break;
                }
                step *= 0.5;
                next = at(t + step, on);
            }
            let Some((vn, here)) = next else {
                why("no step toward the roof stays on the link", t);
                return None;
            };
            (t, v, on) = (t + step, vn, here);
            // (A contact's place is itself found only so closely.)
            if step.abs() < 1e-8 * self.dt {
                return Some((t, on));
            }
        }
        why("the instant doesn't settle", t);
        None
    }

    /// A chain of slice `c` trimmed at the roof: the links from the one that comes out through
    /// it on the one side to the one that does on the other, going out from the joint deepest
    /// under it; with where those two meet the roof. None where the chain doesn't come out
    /// through the roof both ways, or a joint between is over it.
    fn trimmed(&self, roof: &Roof, c: f64, chain: &Chain) -> Option<Trimmed> {
        let past = |p: &P3| roof.past(&self.chart, p);
        let (deep, at) = chain
            .joints
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
            .filter_map(|(j, m)| Some((j, m.point()?)))
            .min_by(|a, b| past(&a.1).total_cmp(&past(&b.1)))?;
        if past(&at) >= 0.0 {
            if self.trace {
                eprintln!(
                    "    slice {c:.4}: no joint of {:?} is under the roof",
                    chain.links
                );
            }
            return None;
        }
        let cut = |up: bool| -> Option<(usize, (f64, Place))> {
            let Some((i, u, v)) = self.first_past(c, chain, deep, up, &past) else {
                if self.trace {
                    eprintln!(
                        "    slice {c:.4}: going {} from joint {deep} of {:?} the roof isn't met; links followed: {:?}",
                        if up { "up" } else { "down" },
                        chain.links,
                        (0..chain.links.len())
                            .map(|i| self.link_points(c, chain, i).map(|p| {
                                (
                                    p.len(),
                                    (past(&p[0].1) * 1e4).round() / 1e4,
                                    (past(&p[p.len() - 1].1) * 1e4).round() / 1e4,
                                )
                            }))
                            .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                    );
                }
                return None;
            };
            let link = chain.links[i];
            let (mut ta, mut on, mut tb) = (u.0, u.2, v.0);
            for _ in 0..40 {
                let tm = 0.5 * (ta + tb);
                let m = self.place_on(link, (ta, tm), c, on)?;
                if past(&self.at_place(link, tm, m)?) < 0.0 {
                    (ta, on) = (tm, m);
                } else {
                    tb = tm;
                }
            }
            // (As the halving left it, where the link ends too soon after for the instant to
            // be made finer.)
            Some((i, self.cut_at(roof, c, link, (ta, on)).unwrap_or((ta, on))))
        };
        let ((e0, cut0), (e1, cut1)) = (cut(false)?, cut(true)?);
        let joints = chain.joints[e0..e1].to_vec();
        if joints
            .iter()
            .any(|m| m.point().is_none_or(|p| past(&p) >= 0.0))
        {
            if self.trace {
                eprintln!(
                    "    slice {c:.4}: of {:?} trimmed to links {e0}..{e1} a joint between is over the roof: {:?}",
                    chain.links,
                    joints
                        .iter()
                        .map(|m| m.point().map(|p| (past(&p) * 1e4).round() / 1e4))
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                );
            }
            return None;
        }
        let out = [
            (cut0.0 - joints[0].t(false)).signum(),
            (cut1.0 - joints[joints.len() - 1].t(true)).signum(),
        ];
        Some((
            Chain {
                joints,
                links: chain.links[e0..=e1].to_vec(),
                out,
                about: chain.about,
            },
            [cut0, cut1],
        ))
    }

    /// A trimmed chain with each node whose two links cross close by it made that crossing. (A
    /// contact that comes to its run and turns back on itself there leaves a loop within what
    /// the tool sweeps, from the crossing along the run to the node and back along the contact:
    /// the outline turns at the crossing. A walk misses a loop shorter than its steps.)
    fn sharpened(&self, c: f64, mut chain: Chain) -> Chain {
        let n = chain.joints.len();
        let step = 0.05 * self.dt;
        for j in 0..n {
            let Joint::Node(node) = chain.joints[j] else {
                continue;
            };
            // Each link's way in time toward the node (the one before) or from it (the one
            // after), and the instant it may be followed to.
            let (before, after) = (chain.links[j], chain.links[j + 1]);
            let (way_a, end_a) = if j == 0 {
                (-chain.out[0], f64::INFINITY)
            } else {
                let from = chain.joints[j - 1].t(true);
                ((node.t - from).signum(), (node.t - from).abs())
            };
            let (way_b, end_b) = if j == n - 1 {
                (chain.out[1], f64::INFINITY)
            } else {
                let to = chain.joints[j + 1].t(false);
                ((to - node.t).signum(), (to - node.t).abs())
            };
            // Points of each, from the node on.
            let along = |link: Link, way: f64, end: f64| -> Vec<(f64, Place, (f64, f64))> {
                let mut out = Vec::new();
                let Some(mut on) = self.place_at(&node, link) else {
                    return out;
                };
                let mut last = node.t;
                for k in 0..=80 {
                    let t = node.t + way * step * k as f64;
                    if step * k as f64 >= end {
                        break;
                    }
                    let Some(next) = self.place_on(link, (last, t), c, on) else {
                        break;
                    };
                    let Some(p) = self.at_place(link, t, next) else {
                        break;
                    };
                    (on, last) = (next, t);
                    out.push((t, on, self.chart.inner(&p, chain.about)));
                }
                out
            };
            let (pa, pb) = (along(before, -way_a, end_a), along(after, way_b, end_b));
            let cross = |u: (f64, f64), v: (f64, f64)| u.0 * v.1 - u.1 * v.0;
            let sub = |u: (f64, f64), v: (f64, f64)| (u.0 - v.0, u.1 - v.1);
            let mut found: Option<Joint> = None;
            'search: for i in 1..pa.len().saturating_sub(1) {
                for k in 1..pb.len().saturating_sub(1) {
                    let (a0, a1, b0, b1) = (pa[i].2, pa[i + 1].2, pb[k].2, pb[k + 1].2);
                    let (da, db) = (sub(a1, a0), sub(b1, b0));
                    let det = cross(da, db);
                    if det == 0.0 {
                        continue;
                    }
                    let w = sub(b0, a0);
                    let (al, be) = (cross(w, db) / det, cross(w, da) / det);
                    if !(0.0..=1.0).contains(&al) || !(0.0..=1.0).contains(&be) {
                        continue;
                    }
                    let joint = self.cross_at(
                        c,
                        (before, pa[i].1, pa[i].0 + (pa[i + 1].0 - pa[i].0) * al),
                        (after, pb[k].1, pb[k].0 + (pb[k + 1].0 - pb[k].0) * be),
                        chain.about,
                    );
                    // (On each link, short of the node: not the node itself.)
                    if let Some(x) = joint
                        && (node.t - x.t(false)) * way_a > 0.5 * step
                        && (x.t(true) - node.t) * way_b > 0.5 * step
                    {
                        found = Some(x);
                        break 'search;
                    }
                }
            }
            if let Some(x) = found {
                chain.joints[j] = x;
            }
        }
        chain
    }

    /// The tooth space's outline in slice `c`: of the chains found there, the one that trimmed
    /// at the roof has every joint on the boundary of what the tool sweeps (none of them a
    /// place the tool passes over: a chain through a node within the sweep, where an envelope
    /// turns back on itself, has such joints), told from the side its angle is less.
    fn outline(&self, roof: &Roof, c: f64, chains: &[Chain]) -> Option<Trimmed> {
        let floor = -5e-4 * self.tool.size;
        let mut good: Vec<Trimmed> = Vec::new();
        for ch in chains {
            let Some((chain, cut)) = self.trimmed(roof, c, ch) else {
                if self.trace {
                    eprintln!("  slice {c:.4}: {:?} doesn't trim at the roof", ch.links);
                }
                continue;
            };
            let chain = self.sharpened(c, chain);
            let angle = |m: &Joint| {
                m.point()
                    .map_or(0.0, |p| self.chart.inner(&p, chain.about).0)
            };
            let (chain, cut) =
                if angle(&chain.joints[0]) > angle(&chain.joints[chain.joints.len() - 1]) {
                    (chain.turned(), [cut[1], cut[0]])
                } else {
                    (chain, cut)
                };
            if good.iter().any(|g| alike(&g.0, &chain)) {
                continue;
            }
            let swept = chain
                .joints
                .iter()
                .filter_map(Joint::point)
                .map(|p| self.depth(&p, floor))
                .fold(f64::INFINITY, f64::min);
            if swept < floor {
                if self.trace {
                    eprintln!(
                        "  slice {c:.4}: {:?} {:?} has a joint within what the tool sweeps",
                        chain.links,
                        chain.joints.iter().map(Joint::told).collect::<Vec<_>>()
                    );
                }
                continue;
            }
            good.push((chain, cut));
        }
        if self.trace && good.len() > 1 {
            eprintln!(
                "  slice {c:.4}: {} outlines: {:?}",
                good.len(),
                good.iter().map(|g| &g.0.links).collect::<Vec<_>>()
            );
        }
        good.into_iter().max_by_key(|g| g.0.links.len())
    }

    /// A roofed chain's row in slice `c`, from its row in a slice nearby: None where a joint
    /// can't be followed there, its links come out of order, a joint is over the roof, or an
    /// end link doesn't run on from its joint to the roof.
    fn row_under(&self, roof: &Roof, chain: &Chain, c: f64, from: &Row) -> Option<Row> {
        let joints = self.row_at(chain, c, &from.1)?;
        if joints
            .iter()
            .any(|m| m.point().is_none_or(|p| roof.past(&self.chart, &p) >= 0.0))
        {
            return None;
        }
        let k = chain.links.len();
        // A run that crosses the contact of a face of its own does so short of their node (the
        // loop from the crossing along the one to the node and back along the other being what
        // the outline leaves out): the node lies ahead on the link the chain comes by and
        // behind on the one it goes on by. Where the crossing comes to the node the loop is
        // closed, and beyond that the two curves cross only past their ends.
        for (j, m) in joints.iter().enumerate() {
            let Joint::Cross { before, after, .. } = m else {
                continue;
            };
            // (Each link's way in time as the chain goes along it.)
            let came = if j == 0 {
                -chain.out[0]
            } else {
                (before.1 - joints[j - 1].t(true)).signum()
            };
            let goes = if j + 1 == joints.len() {
                chain.out[1]
            } else {
                (joints[j + 1].t(false) - after.1).signum()
            };
            let (run, sigma, t_run, face) =
                match (chain.links[j], chain.links[j + 1], before.0, after.0) {
                    (Link::Edge(r), Link::Face(g), Place::Run(s), _) => (r, s, before.1, g),
                    (Link::Face(g), Link::Edge(r), _, Place::Run(s)) => (r, s, after.1, g),
                    _ => continue,
                };
            let Some(side) = self.tool.runs[run].groups.iter().position(|x| *x == face) else {
                continue;
            };
            let node = self.node(run, side, c, (sigma, t_run));
            if self.trace && std::env::var_os("CADRS_GEN_NODES").is_some() {
                eprintln!(
                    "    slice {c:.5}: crossing {j} of run {run} (t {t_run:.6}) and face {face} ({:.6}): their node {:?}; came {came}, goes {goes}",
                    if matches!(chain.links[j], Link::Edge(_)) {
                        after.1
                    } else {
                        before.1
                    },
                    node.map(|n| (n.t, n.sigma))
                );
            }
            let Some(node) = node else {
                continue;
            };
            if (node.t - t_run).abs() > 8.0 * self.dt {
                continue;
            }
            // (The contact's side exactly. The run's to a small share of a step: just before
            // the crossing comes to the node the contact crosses itself beside it, over less of
            // the slices than is worth a stretch of its own, and the run, a hair past the
            // node, stands in for the contact's other branch.)
            let slack = |edge: bool| if edge { -0.1 * self.dt } else { 1e-6 * self.dt };
            let run_first = matches!(chain.links[j], Link::Edge(_));
            if (node.t - before.1) * came <= slack(run_first)
                || (after.1 - node.t) * goes <= slack(!run_first)
            {
                return None;
            }
        }
        let cut0 = self.cut_at(roof, c, chain.links[0], from.2[0])?;
        let cut1 = self.cut_at(roof, c, chain.links[k - 1], from.2[1])?;
        let runs = (cut0.0 - joints[0].t(false)) * chain.out[0] > 1e-6 * self.dt
            && (cut1.0 - joints[joints.len() - 1].t(true)) * chain.out[1] > 1e-6 * self.dt;
        runs.then_some((c, joints, [cut0, cut1]))
    }

    /// A roofed chain's row in slice `c` from one of its rows, by way of slices between where
    /// it can't be reached at once.
    fn row_toward(&self, roof: &Roof, chain: &Chain, c: f64, from: &Row) -> Option<Row> {
        if let Some(row) = self.row_under(roof, chain, c, from) {
            return Some(row);
        }
        for steps in [4, 16, 64] {
            let mut row = from.clone();
            let all = (1..=steps).all(|i| {
                let ci = from.0 + (c - from.0) * i as f64 / steps as f64;
                match self.row_under(roof, chain, ci, &row) {
                    Some(r) => {
                        row = r;
                        true
                    }
                    None => false,
                }
            });
            if all {
                return Some(row);
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// A roofed chain carried from its row `from` to the slices `lo` to `hi`, or as far each
    /// way as it stays what it is (to a thousand-millionth of the way across): its rows in
    /// order.
    fn rows_under(&self, roof: &Roof, chain: &Chain, from: &Row, (lo, hi): (f64, f64)) -> Vec<Row> {
        let step = (hi - lo) / 48.0;
        let mut rows = vec![from.clone()];
        for (dir, end) in [(1.0, hi), (-1.0, lo)] {
            let (mut row, mut h) = (from.clone(), step);
            while (end - row.0) * dir > 1e-12 * step {
                let cn = if (end - row.0) * dir <= h {
                    end
                } else {
                    row.0 + dir * h
                };
                match self.row_under(roof, chain, cn, &row) {
                    Some(r) => {
                        row = r;
                        rows.push(row.clone());
                        h = (h * 2.0).min(step);
                    }
                    None => {
                        h *= 0.5;
                        if h < 1e-9 * (hi - lo) {
                            break;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        rows.sort_by(|a, b| a.0.total_cmp(&b.0));
        rows
    }

    /// The plug of a tooth space whose chain changes along it, links coming and going within
    /// the target (see the module docs): `like` its chain in the target's middle slice, `lo`
    /// to `hi` the target's slices.
    fn roofed(&self, like: &Chain, (lo, hi): (f64, f64), pad: f64) -> Option<Body> {
        use rayon::prelude::*;
        let n = 48;
        let cs: Vec<f64> = (0..=n)
            .map(|i| lo - pad + (hi - lo + 2.0 * pad) * i as f64 / n as f64)
            .collect();
        let found: Vec<Vec<Chain>> = cs
            .par_iter()
            .map(|&c| self.full_chains(c, &like.links, like.about))
            .collect();
        // (The roof as low as may be first: what the outline does between the target and the
        // roof is so much the less to follow.)
        for level in [1.25, 2.0, 4.0, 8.0].map(|m| m * self.clear) {
            let exits: Vec<(f64, [(f64, f64); 3])> = cs
                .iter()
                .zip(&found)
                .filter_map(|(&c, chains)| {
                    Some((c, chains.iter().find_map(|ch| self.exits(c, ch, level))?))
                })
                .collect();
            if exits.len() < 6 {
                continue;
            }
            let Some(roof) = Roof::fit(&self.chart, like.about, &exits, 0.5 * self.clear) else {
                if self.debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: no straight roof {level:.4} from the target across the slices"
                    );
                }
                continue;
            };
            // (The roof itself must be clear of the target between where the chains come out.)
            let low = exits.iter().any(|(c, [a, z, _])| {
                (0..=16).any(|i| {
                    let m = i as f64 / 16.0;
                    let on = (a.0 + (z.0 - a.0) * m, a.1 + (z.1 - a.1) * m);
                    let x = (c - roof.c.0) / (roof.c.1 - roof.c.0);
                    let angle = poly_at(&roof.angle, x);
                    let over = roof.past_at(*c, on);
                    let foot = (on.0 - over * angle.cos(), on.1 - over * angle.sin());
                    self.target.distance(&self.chart.point(*c, foot)) <= 0.75 * self.clear
                })
            });
            if low {
                continue;
            }
            if self.debug {
                eprintln!(
                    "generated cut: a roof {level:.4} from the target, through {} slices' chains",
                    exits.len()
                );
            }
            if let Some(body) = self.under(&roof, like, &cs, &found) {
                return Some(body);
            }
        }
        None
    }

    /// The plug under a roof: the tooth space's outline found in each of the slices `cs` (from
    /// the chains `found` there), the slices of one outline a *stretch*, each carried to where
    /// it stops being what it is and handed over to the next there.
    fn under(&self, roof: &Roof, like: &Chain, cs: &[f64], found: &[Vec<Chain>]) -> Option<Body> {
        use rayon::prelude::*;
        let debug = self.debug;
        let all = (cs[0], cs[cs.len() - 1]);
        let range = all.1 - all.0;
        // A stretch in the making: its chain, its rows as far as they carry, and the first and
        // the last of the slices it was found in.
        struct Piece {
            chain: Chain,
            rows: Vec<Row>,
            found: (f64, f64),
            /// Its number.
            id: usize,
        }
        let mut ids = 0usize;
        let mut number = || {
            ids += 1;
            ids
        };
        let outlines: Vec<Option<Trimmed>> = cs
            .par_iter()
            .zip(found)
            .map(|(&c, chains)| self.outline(roof, c, chains))
            .collect();
        let mut pieces: Vec<Piece> = Vec::new();
        for (&c, o) in cs.iter().zip(outlines) {
            let Some((chain, cut)) = o else {
                continue;
            };
            match pieces.last_mut() {
                Some(p) if alike(&p.chain, &chain) => p.found.1 = c,
                _ => pieces.push(Piece {
                    rows: vec![(c, chain.joints.clone(), cut)],
                    chain,
                    found: (c, c),
                    id: number(),
                }),
            }
        }
        if pieces.is_empty() {
            return None;
        }
        let carry = |p: &mut Piece| {
            let from = p.rows[0].clone();
            p.rows = self.rows_under(roof, &p.chain, &from, all);
        };
        pieces.par_iter_mut().for_each(carry);
        let lim = |p: &Piece| (p.rows[0].0, p.rows[p.rows.len() - 1].0);
        let told = |p: &Piece| {
            format!(
                "{:?} {:?} found over {:.4}..{:.4}, carried over {:.6}..{:.6}",
                p.chain.links,
                p.chain.joints.iter().map(Joint::told).collect::<Vec<_>>(),
                p.found.0,
                p.found.1,
                lim(p).0,
                lim(p).1
            )
        };
        if debug {
            for p in &pieces {
                eprintln!("generated cut: an outline {}", told(p));
            }
        }
        let tol = 1e-7 * range;
        // The outline before the first of them and after the last, where those stop within
        // reach of the target: found a little beyond where they stop.
        let near = |row: &Row| {
            row.1
                .iter()
                .filter_map(Joint::point)
                .any(|p| self.target.distance(&p) <= 4.0 * self.clear)
        };
        for end in [0, 1] {
            for _ in 0..8 {
                let (edge, stop) = if end == 0 {
                    (&pieces[0], lim(&pieces[0]).0)
                } else {
                    let last = &pieces[pieces.len() - 1];
                    (last, lim(last).1)
                };
                let at_end = if end == 0 {
                    &edge.rows[0]
                } else {
                    &edge.rows[edge.rows.len() - 1]
                };
                let out = if end == 0 { -1.0 } else { 1.0 };
                if (stop - if end == 0 { all.0 } else { all.1 }).abs() <= tol || !near(at_end) {
                    break;
                }
                let fresh = [1e-3, 4e-3, 1.6e-2].into_iter().find_map(|share| {
                    let cm = stop + out * share * range;
                    let (ch, cut) =
                        self.outline(roof, cm, &self.full_chains(cm, &like.links, like.about))?;
                    (!akin(&ch, &edge.chain)).then_some((cm, ch, cut))
                });
                let Some((cm, ch, cut)) = fresh else {
                    break;
                };
                let mut p = Piece {
                    rows: vec![(cm, ch.joints.clone(), cut)],
                    chain: ch,
                    found: (cm, cm),
                    id: number(),
                };
                carry(&mut p);
                if debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: beyond the {} an outline {}",
                        if end == 0 { "first" } else { "last" },
                        told(&p)
                    );
                }
                if end == 0 {
                    pieces.insert(0, p);
                } else {
                    pieces.push(p);
                }
            }
        }
        // Where each stretch hands over to the next: (the slice the one ends in, the slice the
        // other starts in; the same but where both stop of themselves, a hair apart).
        let mut hands: Vec<(f64, f64)> = Vec::new();
        let mut upgraded: Vec<(usize, usize)> = Vec::new();
        let mut i = 0;
        while i + 1 < pieces.len() {
            if pieces.len() > 32 {
                return None;
            }
            // Two links that meet at a node in one stretch and cross in the stretch beside it:
            // the crossing goes on into the first as far as it can be carried (the loop it
            // closes too short there for the walk that found the node): a stretch between the
            // two, the first's chain with that crossing. Each node of each stretch once.
            let pick = |node: &Piece, cross: &Piece| -> Option<(usize, usize)> {
                (0..node.chain.joints.len()).find_map(|jn| {
                    if !matches!(node.chain.joints[jn], Joint::Node(_))
                        || upgraded.contains(&(node.id, jn))
                    {
                        return None;
                    }
                    let jx = (0..cross.chain.joints.len()).find(|&jx| {
                        matches!(cross.chain.joints[jx], Joint::Cross { .. })
                            && cross.chain.links[jx] == node.chain.links[jn]
                            && cross.chain.links[jx + 1] == node.chain.links[jn + 1]
                    })?;
                    Some((jn, jx))
                })
            };
            let found = (0..pieces.len() - 1).find_map(|q| {
                pick(&pieces[q], &pieces[q + 1])
                    .map(|j| (q, true, j))
                    .or_else(|| pick(&pieces[q + 1], &pieces[q]).map(|j| (q, false, j)))
            });
            if let Some((q, first, (jn, jx))) = found {
                let (node, cross) = if first {
                    (&pieces[q], &pieces[q + 1])
                } else {
                    (&pieces[q + 1], &pieces[q])
                };
                upgraded.push((node.id, jn));
                {
                    // (In a slice both have: the one with the node's nearest the other, or
                    // as near that as the other is carried.)
                    let x = if first {
                        lim(node).1.clamp(lim(cross).0, lim(cross).1)
                    } else {
                        lim(node).0.clamp(lim(cross).0, lim(cross).1)
                    };
                    let row_at = |p: &Piece| -> Option<Row> {
                        let from = p
                            .rows
                            .iter()
                            .min_by(|a, b| (a.0 - x).abs().total_cmp(&(b.0 - x).abs()))?;
                        if from.0 == x {
                            Some(from.clone())
                        } else {
                            self.row_toward(roof, &p.chain, x, from)
                        }
                    };
                    // (Then a little within the one with the node, where its own links have
                    // some length: the crossing alone is followed there.)
                    let within = (x + if first { -1e-4 } else { 1e-4 } * range)
                        .clamp(lim(node).0, lim(node).1);
                    let mut joint = row_at(cross).map(|r| r.1[jx]);
                    for step in 1..=4 {
                        let ci = x + (within - x) * step as f64 / 4.0;
                        joint = joint.and_then(|m| self.joint_at(ci, &cross.chain, jx, &m));
                    }
                    let x = within;
                    let row_at = |p: &Piece| -> Option<Row> {
                        let from = p
                            .rows
                            .iter()
                            .min_by(|a, b| (a.0 - x).abs().total_cmp(&(b.0 - x).abs()))?;
                        if from.0 == x {
                            Some(from.clone())
                        } else {
                            self.row_toward(roof, &p.chain, x, from)
                        }
                    };
                    let nrow = row_at(node);
                    if debug && (joint.is_none() || nrow.is_none()) {
                        eprintln!(
                            "generated cut: the crossing of {:?} isn't brought into {:?} at joint {jn} in slice {x:.6}: the crossing {}, the stretch's own joints {}",
                            cross.chain.links,
                            node.chain.links,
                            if joint.is_some() {
                                "followed there"
                            } else {
                                "not followed there"
                            },
                            if nrow.is_some() {
                                "found there"
                            } else {
                                "not found there"
                            }
                        );
                    }
                    if let (Some(joint), Some(nrow)) = (joint, nrow) {
                        let mut joints = nrow.1.clone();
                        joints[jn] = joint;
                        let chain = Chain {
                            joints: joints.clone(),
                            ..node.chain.clone()
                        };
                        let rows = self.rows_under(roof, &chain, &(nrow.0, joints, nrow.2), all);
                        if debug && rows[rows.len() - 1].0 - rows[0].0 <= 1e-6 * range {
                            eprintln!(
                                "generated cut: with the crossing of {:?} at joint {jn}, {:?} isn't carried from slice {x:.6}",
                                cross.chain.links, node.chain.links
                            );
                        }
                        if rows[rows.len() - 1].0 - rows[0].0 > 1e-6 * range {
                            let p = Piece {
                                chain,
                                rows,
                                found: node.found,
                                id: number(),
                            };
                            if debug {
                                eprintln!(
                                    "generated cut: with a crossing at joint {jn}, an outline {}",
                                    told(&p)
                                );
                            }
                            pieces.insert(q + 1, p);
                        }
                    }
                }
                // (The stretches' meetings are worked out afresh.)
                hands.clear();
                i = 0;
                continue;
            }
            let (a, b) = (&pieces[i], &pieces[i + 1]);
            if alike(&a.chain, &b.chain) {
                // (One outline found twice: the one carried the farther stays.)
                let keep = if lim(a).1 - lim(a).0 >= lim(b).1 - lim(b).0 {
                    i
                } else {
                    i + 1
                };
                let found = (a.found.0.min(b.found.0), a.found.1.max(b.found.1));
                pieces[keep].found = found;
                pieces.remove(2 * i + 1 - keep);
                continue;
            }
            let (a, b) = (&pieces[i], &pieces[i + 1]);
            let (la, lb) = (lim(a).1, lim(b).0);
            let (fail_a, fail_b) = (la < b.found.0 - tol, lb > a.found.1 + tol);
            let hand = match (fail_a, fail_b) {
                (true, false) => Some((la, la)),
                (false, true) => Some((lb, lb)),
                (true, true) if (la - lb).abs() <= 1e-6 * range => Some((la, lb)),
                (true, true) => {
                    // Both stop short of the other: the slice between is one's (they overlap
                    // there, and the other's stop is where they hand over), or neither's: a
                    // stretch of its own.
                    let fresh = [0.5, 0.25, 0.75].into_iter().find_map(|share| {
                        let cm = la + (lb - la) * share;
                        let (ch, cut) =
                            self.outline(roof, cm, &self.full_chains(cm, &like.links, like.about))?;
                        Some((cm, ch, cut))
                    });
                    match fresh {
                        Some((_, ch, _)) if la > lb && akin(&ch, &a.chain) => Some((la, la)),
                        Some((_, ch, _)) if la > lb && akin(&ch, &b.chain) => Some((lb, lb)),
                        Some((cm, ch, cut)) if !akin(&ch, &a.chain) && !akin(&ch, &b.chain) => {
                            let mut p = Piece {
                                rows: vec![(cm, ch.joints.clone(), cut)],
                                chain: ch,
                                found: (cm, cm),
                                id: number(),
                            };
                            carry(&mut p);
                            if debug {
                                eprintln!("generated cut: between them an outline {}", told(&p));
                            }
                            pieces.insert(i + 1, p);
                            continue;
                        }
                        _ => None,
                    }
                }
                // Neither stops: the same links joined two ways, at a crossing in the one where
                // the other has a node (a loop too short for the walk that found the other, or
                // closed by then). The one with the crossing is the outline as far as it is
                // carried.
                (false, false) if a.chain.links == b.chain.links => {
                    let crossings = |ch: &Chain| {
                        ch.joints
                            .iter()
                            .filter(|m| matches!(m, Joint::Cross { .. }))
                            .count()
                    };
                    let (ca, cb) = (crossings(&a.chain), crossings(&b.chain));
                    // (All of the other's slices, or all but a sliver of them.)
                    let sliver = 1e-4 * range;
                    if ca > cb && la >= lim(b).1 - sliver {
                        pieces[i].found.1 = pieces[i + 1].found.1;
                        pieces.remove(i + 1);
                        continue;
                    } else if cb > ca && lb <= lim(a).0 + sliver {
                        pieces[i + 1].found.0 = pieces[i].found.0;
                        pieces.remove(i);
                        // (Back to the one before it, whose hand-over was to the one gone.)
                        if i > 0 {
                            hands.pop();
                            i -= 1;
                        }
                        continue;
                    } else if ca > cb {
                        Some((la, la))
                    } else if cb > ca {
                        Some((lb, lb))
                    } else {
                        None
                    }
                }
                (false, false) => None,
            };
            let Some(hand) = hand else {
                if debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: declined: no slice at which the outline {:?} (carried to {la:.6}) hands over to {:?} (carried from {lb:.6})",
                        a.chain.links, b.chain.links
                    );
                }
                return None;
            };
            // The links the one has and the other lacks must come to nothing where they meet.
            // Where one doesn't, the outline changes once more between the slices the two were
            // found in (a crossing come under the roof, say, which a chain carried from before
            // knows nothing of): it is looked for a little to each side.
            let long = |p: &Piece, x: f64, lacking: &[usize]| -> f64 {
                let row = p
                    .rows
                    .iter()
                    .min_by(|a, b| (a.0 - x).abs().total_cmp(&(b.0 - x).abs()))
                    .and_then(|from| {
                        if from.0 == x {
                            Some(from.clone())
                        } else {
                            self.row_toward(roof, &p.chain, x, from)
                        }
                    });
                let Some(row) = row else {
                    return f64::INFINITY;
                };
                let k = p.chain.links.len();
                lacking
                    .iter()
                    .map(|&l| {
                        let point = |j: usize| row.1[j].point();
                        let cut = |e: usize| {
                            self.at_place(
                                p.chain.links[if e == 0 { 0 } else { k - 1 }],
                                row.2[e].0,
                                row.2[e].1,
                            )
                        };
                        let (from, to) = if l == 0 {
                            (cut(0), point(0))
                        } else if l == k - 1 {
                            (point(k - 2), cut(1))
                        } else {
                            (point(l - 1), point(l))
                        };
                        match (from, to) {
                            (Some(a), Some(b)) => (a - b).norm(),
                            _ => f64::INFINITY,
                        }
                    })
                    .fold(0.0, f64::max)
            };
            let (ua, ub) = unmatched(&a.chain.links, &b.chain.links);
            if long(a, hand.0, &ua).max(long(b, hand.1, &ub)) > 1e-5 * self.tool.size {
                let fresh = [1e-3, 4e-3, 1.6e-2]
                    .into_iter()
                    .flat_map(|share| [hand.0 - share * range, hand.1 + share * range])
                    .find_map(|cm| {
                        let (ch, cut) =
                            self.outline(roof, cm, &self.full_chains(cm, &like.links, like.about))?;
                        (!akin(&ch, &a.chain) && !akin(&ch, &b.chain)).then_some((cm, ch, cut))
                    });
                let Some((cm, ch, cut)) = fresh else {
                    if debug {
                        eprintln!(
                            "generated cut: declined: where the outline {:?} meets {:?} in slice {:.6} a link the other lacks doesn't come to nothing, and no outline is found between",
                            a.chain.links, b.chain.links, hand.0
                        );
                    }
                    return None;
                };
                let mut p = Piece {
                    rows: vec![(cm, ch.joints.clone(), cut)],
                    chain: ch,
                    found: (cm, cm),
                    id: number(),
                };
                carry(&mut p);
                if debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: beside where they meet an outline {}",
                        told(&p)
                    );
                }
                pieces.insert(i + 1, p);
                continue;
            }
            hands.push(hand);
            i += 1;
        }
        // (A stretch left with no slices of its own, the ones before and after it meeting where
        // it would have been, is none.)
        let mut i = 1;
        while i + 1 < pieces.len() {
            if hands[i].0 - hands[i - 1].1 <= 1e-9 * range
                && hands[i - 1].1 - hands[i].0 <= 1e-5 * range
            {
                hands[i - 1] = (hands[i - 1].0, hands[i].1);
                hands.remove(i);
                pieces.remove(i);
            } else {
                i += 1;
            }
        }
        // The slices of each stretch; the first and the last as far out as they carry, or to a
        // little past the last slice a joint of theirs is near the target in.
        let margin = 8.0 * self.clear;
        let first = &pieces[0];
        let start = first
            .rows
            .iter()
            .find(|r| near(r))
            .map_or(lim(first).0, |r| (r.0 - margin).max(lim(first).0));
        let last = &pieces[pieces.len() - 1];
        let end = last
            .rows
            .iter()
            .rev()
            .find(|r| near(r))
            .map_or(lim(last).1, |r| (r.0 + margin).min(lim(last).1));
        let whole = (start, end);
        let mut stretches: Vec<Carried> = Vec::new();
        for (i, p) in pieces.iter().enumerate() {
            let c = (
                if i == 0 { start } else { hands[i - 1].1 },
                if i + 1 == pieces.len() {
                    end
                } else {
                    hands[i].0
                },
            );
            if !(c.0 < c.1) {
                if debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: declined: the outline {:?} has no slices of its own ({:.6}..{:.6})",
                        p.chain.links, c.0, c.1
                    );
                }
                return None;
            }
            // Its rows from the one end to the other, with a row at each.
            let at = |x: f64| -> Option<Row> {
                let from = p
                    .rows
                    .iter()
                    .min_by(|a, b| (a.0 - x).abs().total_cmp(&(b.0 - x).abs()))?;
                if from.0 == x {
                    return Some(from.clone());
                }
                self.row_toward(roof, &p.chain, x, from)
            };
            let (Some(a), Some(z)) = (at(c.0), at(c.1)) else {
                if debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: declined: the outline {:?} isn't carried to its ends {:.6} and {:.6}",
                        p.chain.links, c.0, c.1
                    );
                }
                return None;
            };
            // (Not the many close together where the chain was carried to its end by ever
            // smaller steps: curves through values at slices so crowded sway between them.)
            let apart = (c.1 - c.0) / 64.0;
            let mut rows = vec![a];
            for r in &p.rows {
                if r.0 - rows[rows.len() - 1].0 >= apart && c.1 - r.0 >= apart {
                    rows.push(r.clone());
                }
            }
            rows.push(z);
            // (A short stretch has few: some between, for its joints to be bound in.)
            if rows.len() < 9 {
                for i in 1..8 {
                    let x = c.0 + (c.1 - c.0) * i as f64 / 8.0;
                    if let Some(from) = rows
                        .iter()
                        .min_by(|a, b| (a.0 - x).abs().total_cmp(&(b.0 - x).abs()))
                        && (from.0 - x).abs() > 1e-3 * (c.1 - c.0)
                        && let Some(row) = self.row_toward(roof, &p.chain, x, from)
                    {
                        rows.push(row);
                    }
                }
                rows.sort_by(|a, b| a.0.total_cmp(&b.0));
            }
            // The links that come to nothing where it meets the stretch before (0) or after
            // (1): those the other lacks. Each must be next to nothing there.
            let k = p.chain.links.len();
            let mut gone: [Vec<usize>; 2] = [Vec::new(), Vec::new()];
            if i > 0 {
                gone[0] = unmatched(&pieces[i - 1].chain.links, &p.chain.links).1;
            }
            if i + 1 < pieces.len() {
                gone[1] = unmatched(&p.chain.links, &pieces[i + 1].chain.links).0;
            }
            for (end, row) in [(0, &rows[0]), (1, &rows[rows.len() - 1])] {
                for &l in &gone[end] {
                    let point = |j: usize| row.1[j].point();
                    let cut = |e: usize| {
                        self.at_place(
                            p.chain.links[if e == 0 { 0 } else { k - 1 }],
                            row.2[e].0,
                            row.2[e].1,
                        )
                    };
                    let (from, to) = if l == 0 {
                        (cut(0), point(0))
                    } else if l == k - 1 {
                        (point(k - 2), cut(1))
                    } else {
                        (point(l - 1), point(l))
                    };
                    let long = match (from, to) {
                        (Some(a), Some(b)) => (a - b).norm(),
                        _ => f64::INFINITY,
                    };
                    if long > 1e-5 * self.tool.size {
                        if debug {
                            eprintln!(
                                "generated cut: declined: where the outline {:?} meets the next in slice {:.6} its link {l} ({:?}), which the other lacks, is {long:.3e} long",
                                p.chain.links, row.0, p.chain.links[l]
                            );
                        }
                        return None;
                    }
                }
            }
            let span = Span {
                chain: p.chain.clone(),
                rows: rows.iter().map(|r| (r.0, r.1.clone())).collect(),
                c,
                skip: [0, 0],
            };
            let pinch = gone
                .clone()
                .map(|g| g.into_iter().filter(|&l| l > 0 && l < k - 1).collect());
            let Some((bound, before, after)) = self.bind(&span, &pinch) else {
                if debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: declined: the joints of the outline {:?} can't be bound for its sheets over {:.6}..{:.6}",
                        p.chain.links, c.0, c.1
                    );
                }
                return None;
            };
            // Where the two end links meet the roof, in the slices the joints were bound in.
            let bcs: Vec<f64> = bound.iter().map(|r| r.0).collect();
            let cut_ts: Option<Vec<[f64; 2]>> = bcs
                .par_iter()
                .map(|&x| {
                    let from = rows
                        .iter()
                        .min_by(|a, b| (a.0 - x).abs().total_cmp(&(b.0 - x).abs()))?;
                    let ends = [0, 1].map(|e| {
                        let link = p.chain.links[if e == 0 { 0 } else { k - 1 }];
                        self.cut_at(roof, x, link, from.2[e]).or_else(|| {
                            // (By way of slices between.)
                            let mut g = from.2[e];
                            for s in 1..=16 {
                                g = self.cut_at(
                                    roof,
                                    from.0 + (x - from.0) * s as f64 / 16.0,
                                    link,
                                    g,
                                )?;
                            }
                            Some(g)
                        })
                    });
                    Some([ends[0]?.0, ends[1]?.0])
                })
                .collect();
            let Some(mut cut_ts) = cut_ts else {
                if debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: declined: an end link of the outline {:?} isn't followed to the roof",
                        p.chain.links
                    );
                }
                return None;
            };
            // (An end link that comes to nothing where the stretch ends: cut at its joint
            // there, exactly.)
            for (end, at) in [(0, 0), (1, bcs.len() - 1)] {
                if gone[end].contains(&0) {
                    cut_ts[at][0] = before[0].point(bcs[at]).x;
                }
                if gone[end].contains(&(k - 1)) {
                    cut_ts[at][1] = after[k - 2].point(bcs[at]).x;
                }
            }
            let cuts =
                [0, 1].map(|e| through(&bcs, &cut_ts.iter().map(|t| t[e]).collect::<Vec<_>>()));
            stretches.push(Carried {
                chain: p.chain.clone(),
                c,
                whole,
                rows: bound,
                before,
                after,
                ends: [Vec::new(), Vec::new()],
                fill: None,
                cuts: Some(cuts),
            });
        }
        if debug {
            eprintln!(
                "generated cut: {} stretches under the roof over {:.4}..{:.4}",
                stretches.len(),
                whole.0,
                whole.1
            );
        }
        self.plug(&stretches)
    }
}

/// The two turns of a motion that is the first about one line and the second about another,
/// not parallel: (the tool's axis, the target's axis).
fn two_turns(steps: &[RigidStep]) -> Option<(Axis, Axis)> {
    let [
        RigidStep::Turn {
            axis: a,
            from: a0,
            to: a1,
        },
        RigidStep::Turn {
            axis: b,
            from: b0,
            to: b1,
        },
    ] = steps
    else {
        return None;
    };
    let turning = (a1 - a0).abs() > 1e-9 && (b1 - b0).abs() > 1e-9;
    let apart = a.dir.cross(&b.dir).norm() > 1e-6;
    (turning && apart).then_some((*a, *b))
}

/// `target` less what `tool` passes through under `steps` (two turns): see the module docs.
/// None where the cut isn't made this way.
pub(super) fn cut(
    k: &mut NativeKernel,
    target: BodyId,
    tool: &Body,
    steps: &[RigidStep],
) -> Option<Result<OpResult>> {
    let debug = std::env::var_os("CADRS_SWEEP_DEBUG").is_some();
    let t_start = web_time::Instant::now();
    let (tool_axis, target_axis) = two_turns(steps)?;
    if tool.solids.len() != 1 {
        return None;
    }
    let tb = (**k.get(target).ok()?).clone();
    let motion = Motion { steps };
    let tl = Tool::new(tool);
    let size = tl.size;
    if debug {
        let count = |k: EdgeKind| tl.kind.iter().filter(|x| **x == k).count();
        let mut groups = tl.group.clone();
        groups.sort_unstable();
        groups.dedup();
        eprintln!(
            "generated cut: a tool of {} faces in {} smooth groups; edges: {} convex, {} concave, {} smooth, {} other, the sharp ones in {} runs",
            tool.faces.len(),
            groups.len(),
            count(EdgeKind::Convex),
            count(EdgeKind::Concave),
            count(EdgeKind::Smooth),
            count(EdgeKind::Other),
            tl.runs.len()
        );
    }
    let tsize = tb.bbox().diagonal().max(super::tol::POINT);
    // The tool's ends must be clear of the target (else its places there bound the cut too).
    let (
        RigidStep::Turn {
            from: a0, to: a1, ..
        },
        RigidStep::Turn {
            from: b0, to: b1, ..
        },
    ) = (steps[0], steps[1])
    else {
        return None;
    };
    // A motion that repeats: the tool turning whole turns (each leaves it as it was) while the
    // target turns a whole number of turns in all: (how many times, the turn about the target's
    // axis from one to the next).
    let turns = (a1 - a0).abs() / TAU;
    let whole = |x: f64| (x - x.round()).abs() < 1e-9;
    let repeats = (turns >= 2.0 - 1e-9 && whole(turns) && whole((b1 - b0).abs() / TAU))
        .then(|| (turns.round() as usize, (b1 - b0) / turns.round()));
    let defl = 2e-4 * tsize;
    let dist = MeshDistance::new(&tb, defl)?;
    let clear = 4.0 * defl;
    // The speed of the tool's far reach, and the time it takes over a small share of its size.
    let bb = tool.bbox();
    let speed = (0..=16)
        .flat_map(|j| {
            let tw = motion.twist(j as f64 / 16.0);
            (0..8).map(move |i| {
                let p = P3::new(
                    if i & 1 == 0 { bb.min.x } else { bb.max.x },
                    if i & 2 == 0 { bb.min.y } else { bb.max.y },
                    if i & 4 == 0 { bb.min.z } else { bb.max.z },
                );
                (tw.0.cross(&p.coords) + tw.1).norm()
            })
        })
        .fold(0.0, f64::max);
    if speed <= 0.0 || !speed.is_finite() {
        return None;
    }
    let dt = size / 128.0 / speed;
    let z = target_axis.dir.into_inner();
    let x = any_perpendicular(&z);
    let y = z.cross(&x);
    // The point of the target's axis nearest the tool's.
    let apex = {
        let (d1, d2) = (z, tool_axis.dir.into_inner());
        let w = target_axis.origin - tool_axis.origin;
        let (b, d, e) = (d1.dot(&d2), d1.dot(&w), d2.dot(&w));
        let den = 1.0 - b * b;
        target_axis.origin + d1 * ((b * e - d) / den)
    };
    if !repeats.is_some() {
        // (One pass: the tool where it starts and where it ends must be clear of the target.)
        let (mesh, _) = super::tess::mesh_body(tool, 1e-3 * size, 0.3);
        for t in [0.0, 1.0] {
            let (r, d) = motion.place(t);
            if mesh
                .iter()
                .flat_map(|m| m.positions.iter())
                .any(|p| dist.distance(&P3::from(r * p.coords + d)) <= clear)
            {
                if debug {
                    eprintln!("generated cut: declined: the tool starts or ends within the target");
                }
                return None;
            }
        }
    }
    let period = repeats.map(|(n, _)| 1.0 / n as f64);
    let tool_mesh = MeshDistance::new(tool, 1e-4 * size)?;
    let mut made: Option<(Vec<Body>, Slices)> = None;
    let gen_of = |chart: Chart| Gen {
        tool: &tl,
        motion: &motion,
        chart,
        target: &dist,
        clear,
        speed,
        dt,
        span: if repeats.is_some() {
            None
        } else {
            Some((0.0, 1.0))
        },
        repeat: repeats.map(|(n, angle)| (1.0 / n as f64, target_axis, angle)),
        window: (0.0, period.unwrap_or(1.0)),
        reach: 0.25 * tsize,
        tool_mesh: &tool_mesh,
        tool_box: tool.bbox(),
        near_joint: 2.0,
        debug,
        trace: std::env::var_os("CADRS_GEN_TRACE").is_some(),
    };
    // (The charts whose middle slice has chains, but which made no plug of them.)
    #[allow(clippy::type_complexity)]
    let mut tried: Vec<(Chart, (f64, f64), f64, Vec<Chain>)> = Vec::new();
    for kind in [Slices::Height, Slices::Radius, Slices::Sphere] {
        let chart = Chart {
            kind,
            o: if kind == Slices::Sphere {
                apex
            } else {
                target_axis.origin
            },
            x,
            y,
            z,
        };
        let g = gen_of(chart);
        // The target's slices, from its mesh.
        let (mesh, _) = super::tess::mesh_body(&tb, defl, 0.3);
        let (lo, hi) = mesh
            .iter()
            .flat_map(|m| m.positions.iter())
            .map(|p| chart.c(p))
            .fold((f64::INFINITY, f64::NEG_INFINITY), |(l, h), c| {
                (l.min(c), h.max(c))
            });
        if !(hi - lo > 1e-6 * tsize) {
            continue;
        }
        let pad = 0.02 * (hi - lo);
        let mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi);
        let nodes = g.nodes(mid, g.window, g.reach);
        if debug {
            eprintln!(
                "generated cut: {kind:?} slices {lo:.4}..{hi:.4}: {} nodes in the middle one ({:.0} ms)",
                nodes.len(),
                (web_time::Instant::now() - t_start).as_secs_f64() * 1e3
            );
        }
        let seeds: Vec<&Node> = nodes.iter().filter(|n| !g.clear_of_target(&n.p)).collect();
        let Some(first) = seeds.first() else {
            continue;
        };
        let about = chart.inner(&first.p, 0.0).0;
        let cands = g.cands(mid, &nodes, about);
        if debug {
            eprintln!(
                "generated cut: {} curves to cross in the middle slice ({:.0} ms)",
                cands.len(),
                (web_time::Instant::now() - t_start).as_secs_f64() * 1e3
            );
        }
        let chains = g.chains_at(mid, &nodes, &cands, about).unwrap_or_default();
        if chains.is_empty() {
            continue;
        }
        if debug {
            for c in &chains {
                eprintln!(
                    "generated cut: a chain of {} links: {:?}, joints at t {:?}",
                    c.links.len(),
                    c.links,
                    c.joints.iter().map(Joint::told).collect::<Vec<_>>()
                );
            }
        }
        if let Ok(spec) = std::env::var("CADRS_GEN_DUMP") {
            // `<file>:<slice>,<slice>,…`: every curve of those slices, as lines of
            // "slice link t a b distance-from-the-target".
            let (file, at) = spec.split_once(':').unwrap_or((&spec, ""));
            let mut out = String::new();
            for c in at.split(',').filter_map(|x| x.parse::<f64>().ok()) {
                let nodes = g.nodes(c, g.window, g.reach);
                for (i, cand) in g.cands(c, &nodes, about).iter().enumerate() {
                    for (p, ab) in cand.pts.iter().zip(&cand.ab) {
                        out.push_str(&format!(
                            "{kind:?} {c} {i} {:?} {} {} {} {}\n",
                            cand.link,
                            p.0,
                            ab.0,
                            ab.1,
                            dist.distance(&p.1)
                        ));
                    }
                }
            }
            let _ = std::fs::write(format!("{file}.{kind:?}.txt"), out);
        }
        if std::env::var_os("CADRS_GEN_SURVEY").is_some() {
            // Every chain found afresh in each of some slices.
            let mut surveyed: Vec<Vec<Link>> = Vec::new();
            for ci in 0..=32 {
                let c = lo - pad + (hi - lo + 2.0 * pad) * ci as f64 / 32.0;
                let nodes = g.nodes(c, g.window, g.reach);
                let cands = g.cands(c, &nodes, about);
                let mut told: Vec<String> = Vec::new();
                for seed in nodes.iter().filter(|n| !g.clear_of_target(&n.p)) {
                    let found = g.chain(c, seed, &cands, about, 0);
                    if let Some(ch) = &found
                        && !surveyed.contains(&ch.links)
                    {
                        // How far this chain can be carried, and how far from the target its
                        // joints are where it stops.
                        surveyed.push(ch.links.clone());
                        let rows = g.rows(ch, c, (lo - pad, hi + pad));
                        let far = |row: &(f64, Vec<Joint>)| -> Vec<String> {
                            row.1
                                .iter()
                                .map(|j| {
                                    let p = j.point().unwrap_or_else(P3::origin);
                                    format!("{:.4}", dist.distance(&p))
                                })
                                .collect()
                        };
                        for row in rows.iter().step_by((rows.len() / 14).max(1)) {
                            eprintln!(
                                "survey:   slice {:.4}: {:?}",
                                row.0,
                                row.1
                                    .iter()
                                    .map(|j| {
                                        format!(
                                            "{} ({:.3})",
                                            j.told(),
                                            j.point().map_or(f64::NAN, |p| dist.distance(&p))
                                        )
                                    })
                                    .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                            );
                        }
                        eprintln!(
                            "survey: {:?} found at {c:.4} carries over {:.5}..{:.5}; its joints from the target there: {:?} and {:?}",
                            ch.links,
                            rows[0].0,
                            rows[rows.len() - 1].0,
                            far(&rows[0]),
                            far(&rows[rows.len() - 1])
                        );
                    }
                    let line = match found {
                        Some(ch) => format!(
                            "{:?} {:?}",
                            ch.links,
                            ch.joints.iter().map(Joint::told).collect::<Vec<_>>()
                        ),
                        None => format!(
                            "none from run {} side {} t {:.4}",
                            seed.r, seed.side, seed.t
                        ),
                    };
                    if !told.contains(&line) {
                        told.push(line);
                    }
                }
                eprintln!(
                    "survey {kind:?} slice {c:.4}: {} nodes; {told:?}",
                    nodes.len()
                );
            }
        }
        // The plug of the tooth space whose chain is `chain` in slice `from`.
        let build = |chain: &Chain, from: f64| -> Option<Body> {
            // How far clear of the target each end link gets in the middle slice: the cuts are
            // tried at shares of the lesser.
            let n = chain.joints.len();
            let far = [
                (0, chain.links[0], false),
                (n - 1, chain.links[chain.links.len() - 1], true),
            ]
            .iter()
            .filter_map(|&(j, link, after)| {
                let reach = match &chain.joints[j] {
                    Joint::Node(m) => g.follow(from, m, link)?,
                    joint => {
                        let (place, t) = g.joint_on(joint, link, after)?;
                        g.march(from, link, place, t, chain.out[usize::from(after)], None)
                    }
                };
                Some(
                    reach
                        .pts
                        .iter()
                        .map(|p| dist.distance(&p.1))
                        .fold(f64::NEG_INFINITY, f64::max),
                )
            })
            .fold(f64::INFINITY, f64::min);
            let spans = g.spans(chain, from, (lo - pad, hi + pad), (lo, hi))?;
            let whole = (spans[0].c.0, spans[spans.len() - 1].c.1);
            let bound: Option<Vec<_>> = spans
                .iter()
                .map(|s| g.bind(s, &[Vec::new(), Vec::new()]))
                .collect();
            let Some(bound) = bound else {
                if debug {
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut: declined: a stretch's joints can't be bound for its sheets"
                    );
                }
                return None;
            };
            // (Each stretch's rows from here on: the many its joints were bound in.)
            let spans: Vec<Span> = spans
                .into_iter()
                .zip(&bound)
                .map(|(s, (rows, ..))| Span {
                    rows: rows.clone(),
                    ..s
                })
                .collect();
            if debug {
                eprintln!(
                    "generated cut: carried over {:.4}..{:.4} in {} stretch(es) ({:.0} ms)",
                    whole.0,
                    whole.1,
                    spans.len(),
                    (web_time::Instant::now() - t_start).as_secs_f64() * 1e3
                );
            }
            let mut plug = None;
            let mut tries = vec![2.0 * clear];
            tries.extend(
                [0.15, 0.3, 0.6]
                    .map(|share| share * far)
                    .into_iter()
                    .filter(|p| *p > 2.5 * clear),
            );
            for past in tries {
                if !(far.is_finite() && past < far) {
                    continue;
                }
                let Some(ends) = g.cuts(&spans, past, (lo, hi)) else {
                    continue;
                };
                // (A stretch closed by fillers cuts its own end link there, as clear of the
                // target.)
                let own: Vec<[Option<Vec<f64>>; 2]> = spans
                    .iter()
                    .map(|s| {
                        [0, 1].map(|end| {
                            (s.skip[end] > 0)
                                .then(|| g.cut_of(&[s], end, whole, past, (lo, hi)))
                                .flatten()
                        })
                    })
                    .collect();
                let blends: &[f64] = if spans.iter().any(|s| s.skip != [0, 0]) {
                    &[0.25, 0.5, 1.0]
                } else {
                    &[1.0]
                };
                for &blend in blends {
                    let Some(stretches) = carried(&spans, &bound, whole, &ends, &own, blend) else {
                        continue;
                    };
                    plug = g.plug(&stretches);
                    if plug.is_some() {
                        break;
                    }
                }
                if plug.is_some() {
                    break;
                }
            }
            plug
        };
        let all = |chains: &[(Chain, f64)]| -> Option<Vec<Body>> {
            chains
                .iter()
                .map(|(chain, from)| build(chain, *from))
                .collect()
        };
        let mut masters: Vec<(Chain, f64)> = chains.iter().map(|c| (c.clone(), mid)).collect();
        let mut plugs = all(&masters);
        if plugs.is_none() {
            // A chain may have more links in another slice: one that leaves the target here,
            // and is the chain's last, is crossed there within it by the next. The chains of
            // the target's two end slices: one that has all of the middle slice's links and
            // more is followed from its own slice instead.
            let window = |big: &[Link], small: &[Link]| {
                let turned: Vec<Link> = small.iter().rev().copied().collect();
                big.windows(small.len())
                    .any(|w| w == small || w == turned.as_slice())
            };
            let mut grown = false;
            for c in [lo + pad, hi - pad] {
                let nodes = g.nodes(c, g.window, g.reach);
                let cands = g.cands(c, &nodes, about);
                for there in g.chains_at(c, &nodes, &cands, about).unwrap_or_default() {
                    for m in masters.iter_mut() {
                        if there.links.len() > m.0.links.len() && window(&there.links, &m.0.links) {
                            if debug {
                                eprintln!(
                                    "generated cut: in slice {c:.4} the chain has more links: {:?}",
                                    there.links
                                );
                            }
                            *m = (there.clone(), c);
                            grown = true;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            if grown {
                plugs = all(&masters);
            }
        }
        let plugs = plugs.unwrap_or_default();
        if !plugs.is_empty() {
            made = Some((plugs, kind));
            break;
        }
        tried.push((chart, (lo, hi), pad, chains));
    }
    if made.is_none() && repeats.is_none() {
        // A tooth space whose chain changes along it within the target: made in stretches
        // under a roof, by the chart its roof is straight in.
        for want in [Slices::Sphere, Slices::Radius, Slices::Height] {
            let Some((chart, slices, pad, chains)) = tried.iter().find(|t| t.0.kind == want) else {
                continue;
            };
            let g = Gen {
                near_joint: 0.1,
                ..gen_of(*chart)
            };
            if debug {
                eprintln!(
                    "generated cut: by {want:?} slices under a roof ({:.0} ms)",
                    (web_time::Instant::now() - t_start).as_secs_f64() * 1e3
                );
            }
            let plugs: Option<Vec<Body>> = chains
                .iter()
                .map(|chain| g.roofed(chain, *slices, *pad))
                .collect();
            if let Some(plugs) = plugs.filter(|p| !p.is_empty()) {
                made = Some((plugs, want));
                break;
            }
        }
    }
    let (plugs, kind) = made?;
    if debug {
        eprintln!(
            "generated cut: {} plug(s) by {kind:?} slices, {} faces ({:.0} ms)",
            plugs.len(),
            plugs.iter().map(|p| p.faces.len()).sum::<usize>(),
            (web_time::Instant::now() - t_start).as_secs_f64() * 1e3
        );
    }
    if debug && std::env::var_os("CADRS_GEN_PLUG").is_some() {
        // (The plugs themselves: what is wrong with each as a solid, and its least edges.)
        for p in &plugs {
            let faults = p.check_with(super::topo::CheckLevel::Full);
            let mut edges: Vec<f64> = p
                .edges
                .iter()
                .filter(|e| !e.degenerate)
                .map(|e| (e.point(e.t[1]) - e.point(e.t[0])).norm())
                .collect();
            edges.sort_by(f64::total_cmp);
            eprintln!(
                "generated cut: a plug of {} faces, {} edges ({} of no length); its shortest edges' ends are {:?} apart; {} faults: {:?}",
                p.faces.len(),
                p.edges.len(),
                p.edges.iter().filter(|e| e.degenerate).count(),
                edges
                    .iter()
                    .take(8)
                    .map(|x| format!("{x:.2e}"))
                    .collect::<Vec<_>>(),
                faults.len(),
                faults.iter().take(6).collect::<Vec<_>>()
            );
            for fault in &faults {
                let Some(fi) = fault
                    .strip_prefix("face ")
                    .and_then(|r| r.split(' ').next())
                    .and_then(|n| n.parse::<usize>().ok())
                else {
                    continue;
                };
                for (k, co) in p.faces[fi].loops.iter().flatten().enumerate() {
                    let e = &p.edges[co.edge];
                    let (a, z) = if co.fwd {
                        (e.t[0], e.t[1])
                    } else {
                        (e.t[1], e.t[0])
                    };
                    let (pa, pz) = (co.pc.point(a), co.pc.point(z));
                    // (Where along the edge its p-curve is farthest from it.)
                    let far = (0..=64)
                        .map(|i| {
                            let t = e.t[0] + (e.t[1] - e.t[0]) * i as f64 / 64.0;
                            let q = co.pc.point(t);
                            ((p.faces[fi].surf.eval(q.x, q.y) - e.point(t)).norm(), i)
                        })
                        .max_by(|a, b| a.0.total_cmp(&b.0));
                    if let Some((d, i)) = far.filter(|f| f.0 > 1e-6) {
                        eprintln!(
                            "generated cut:   (next: its p-curve is {d:.3e} from it at {}/64 of the way)",
                            i
                        );
                    }
                    eprintln!(
                        "generated cut:   face {fi} coedge {k}: edge {} ({}) from vertex {} to {}, {:.3e} long, in the face from ({:.6}, {:.6}) to ({:.6}, {:.6})",
                        co.edge,
                        if e.degenerate { "a point" } else { "a curve" },
                        if co.fwd { e.v[0] } else { e.v[1] },
                        if co.fwd { e.v[1] } else { e.v[0] },
                        (e.point(e.t[1]) - e.point(e.t[0])).norm(),
                        pa.x,
                        pa.y,
                        pz.x,
                        pz.y
                    );
                }
            }
        }
    }
    // Every copy of each plug, subtracted.
    let copies = repeats.map_or(1, |(n, _)| n);
    let about = |i: usize| -> Affine {
        let angle = repeats.map_or(0.0, |(_, a)| a) * i as f64;
        let r = Rotation3::from_axis_angle(&target_axis.dir, angle);
        let c = target_axis.origin.coords;
        Affine {
            m: *r.matrix(),
            t: c - r * c,
        }
    };
    // The copies in groups of solids apart, each group one tool (a subtraction with nothing
    // to unite first): all of them where a plug stands clear of its copy a turn on; every
    // other one where it meets that copy (as plugs may, outside the target) but not the one
    // two turns on; else each on its own.
    let groups: Vec<Vec<usize>> = if copies > 1 && plugs.len() == 1 {
        let polys: Vec<Vec<Vec<P2>>> = plugs[0]
            .faces
            .iter()
            .map(|f| super::classify::face_polygons(&plugs[0], f))
            .collect();
        let (mesh, _) = super::tess::mesh_body(&plugs[0], 2e-3 * size, 0.3);
        let points: Vec<P3> = mesh
            .iter()
            .flat_map(|m| m.positions.iter().copied())
            .collect();
        // Whether the plug is clear of its copy `turns` on (either way): none of the copy's
        // points in or on the plug.
        let clear_of = |turns: usize| -> bool {
            use rayon::prelude::*;
            [turns, copies - turns].iter().all(|&j| {
                let m = about(j);
                points.par_iter().all(|p| {
                    super::classify::classify_point(&plugs[0], &polys, &m.point(p), 1e-6 * size)
                        == crate::PointClass::Outside
                })
            })
        };
        if clear_of(1) {
            vec![(0..copies).collect()]
        } else if copies >= 4 && clear_of(2) {
            // (Every other one; the last on its own where their number is odd.)
            let even = copies - copies % 2;
            let mut g = vec![
                (0..even).step_by(2).collect::<Vec<_>>(),
                (1..even).step_by(2).collect::<Vec<_>>(),
            ];
            if copies % 2 == 1 {
                g.push(vec![copies - 1]);
            }
            g
        } else {
            (0..copies).map(|i| vec![i]).collect()
        }
    } else {
        (0..copies).map(|i| vec![i]).collect()
    };
    let mut at = target;
    let mut cut: Result<OpResult> = Err(KernelError::Unsupported("a cut with nothing to cut"));
    'plugs: for plug in &plugs {
        for group in &groups {
            let mut tool = Body::default();
            for &i in group {
                tool.append(&if i == 0 {
                    plug.clone()
                } else {
                    plug.transformed(&about(i))
                });
            }
            let tool = k.insert(tool);
            let step = k.boolean(BoolOp::Subtract, at, &[tool]);
            k.release(tool);
            if at != target {
                k.release(at);
            }
            match step {
                Ok(r) if r.bodies.len() == 1 => {
                    at = r.bodies[0];
                    cut = Ok(r);
                }
                Ok(r) => {
                    for id in r.bodies {
                        k.release(id);
                    }
                    cut = Err(KernelError::Unsupported(
                        "a cut that leaves the target in pieces",
                    ));
                    break 'plugs;
                }
                Err(e) => {
                    cut = Err(e);
                    break 'plugs;
                }
            }
        }
    }
    let apart = groups.len();
    if debug {
        eprintln!(
            "generated cut: subtracted in {apart} tool(s) of solids apart ({:.0} ms): {}",
            (web_time::Instant::now() - t_start).as_secs_f64() * 1e3,
            match &cut {
                Ok(_) => "done".to_string(),
                Err(e) => e.to_string(),
            }
        );
    }
    match cut {
        Ok(r) if r.bodies.iter().all(|&id| k.sound(id)) => Some(Ok(r)),
        Ok(r) => {
            for id in r.bodies {
                k.release(id);
            }
            None
        }
        Err(_) => None,
    }
}
